/* Power Up — questions en anglais (m365). Clé = question française + « ¦ » + première réponse. */
PU_I18N.questions({
  "Où l'admin crée un utilisateur et lui attribue une licence ? ¦ Dans le centre d'administration Teams": {"q":"Where does an admin create a user and assign them a license?","e":"The Microsoft 365 admin center manages users, licenses, groups, and billing.","a":["In the Teams admin center","In the Microsoft 365 admin center","In the SharePoint admin center"]},
  "Pour interdire le partage externe sur un site SharePoint sensible : ¦ On masque le site des résultats de recherche Microsoft 365": {"q":"To prevent external sharing on a sensitive SharePoint site:","e":"External sharing is set at the organization level, then site by site, and a site can never be more permissive than the organization.","a":["You hide the site from Microsoft 365 search results","You configure the site's external sharing setting in the SharePoint admin center","You disable guest access in the Teams admin center"]},
  "Quel rôle permet de réinitialiser le mot de passe des utilisateurs, sans être administrateur global ? ¦ Administrateur du support technique": {"q":"Which role can reset users' passwords without being a global administrator?","e":"The Helpdesk Administrator can reset passwords for non-admin users: this is the principle of least privilege.","a":["Helpdesk Administrator","Global Reader","Billing Administrator"]},
  "Accueillir un nouvel utilisateur dans M365 : ¦ Créer le compte": {"q":"Onboarding a new user in M365:","e":"Without a license, there is no mailbox or Teams; groups grant access to resources; MFA is set up at first sign-in.","items":["Create the account","Assign a license","Add to groups and teams","Hand over access and have them set up MFA"]},
  "Bonnes pratiques pour les comptes administrateurs : ¦ MFA obligatoire, idéalement résistante au phishing": {"q":"Best practices for administrator accounts:","e":"Dedicated account, MFA, few global admins. Admin accounts should stay “cloud-only”: if they are synced from the on-premises AD, they fall with it if the AD is compromised.","a":["MFA required, ideally phishing-resistant","An admin account separate from the everyday account","Limit the number of global administrators","Sync admin accounts from the on-premises AD with Entra Connect"]},
  "Appliquer le moindre privilège aux rôles d'administration : ¦ Le rôle Administrateur global pour chaque technicien, avec MFA": {"q":"Applying least privilege to administration roles:","e":"Privileged Identity Management grants the role only when needed, for a limited time, with justification and an audit trail.","a":["The Global Administrator role for every technician, with MFA","A shared admin account, protected by a FIDO2 key","Roles activated “just in time” with PIM"]},
  "Teams ne marche plus chez tout le monde. Où l'admin vérifie-t-il s'il s'agit d'une panne Microsoft ? ¦ Dans l'Intégrité du service du centre d'administration": {"q":"Teams has stopped working for everyone. Where does the admin check whether it is a Microsoft outage?","e":"The “Service health” page shows ongoing Microsoft incidents, their impact, and their progress. The Message center announces upcoming changes, not outages.","a":["In Service health in the admin center","In Message center in the admin center","In the Entra ID sign-in logs"]},
  "Combien d'administrateurs globaux Microsoft recommande-t-il ? ¦ Un seul, pour réduire au maximum la surface d'attaque": {"q":"How many global administrators does Microsoft recommend?","e":"It is the most powerful role. With a single global admin, you risk being locked out if that person is unavailable. It is reserved for very few accounts, and more limited roles are used day to day.","a":["Just one, to minimize the attack surface as much as possible","Fewer than 5, and at least 2 so you don't get locked out","One per department or site, to delegate as close as possible"]},
  "Un collaborateur quitte l'entreprise. Quelles actions prévoir ? ¦ Bloquer la connexion et révoquer ses sessions": {"q":"An employee is leaving the company. Which actions should you plan? (several answers)","e":"You cut access immediately, hand over the data, then free up the license. Deleting the account too early means losing the mailbox and OneDrive before the manager has retrieved what they need.","a":["Block sign-in and revoke their sessions","Give their manager access to their mailbox and OneDrive if needed","Remove the license once the data has been transferred","Delete the account as soon as they leave, before any transfer"]},
  "Pour un prestataire infogéreur (MSP), le GDAP permet… ¦ D'obtenir des droits d'administration délégués limités et temporaires chez ses clients": {"q":"For a managed service provider (MSP), GDAP allows it to…","e":"Granular Delegated Admin Privileges: the partner receives only the roles it needs, for a defined period. Permanent global admin access was the old DAP model, which has been phased out precisely for that reason.","a":["Obtain limited, temporary delegated administration rights at its customers","Have unlimited global administrator access at all its customers","Merge all its customers' directories into its own tenant"]},
  "Pour attribuer automatiquement les licences à tous les membres d'un service : ¦ Les licences basées sur les groupes": {"q":"To automatically assign licenses to all members of a department:","e":"You assign the license to a group; every new hire added to the group receives it automatically.","a":["Group-based licensing","Entra ID administrative units","Intune app assignment policies"]},
  "Où l'admin suit-il les changements annoncés par Microsoft pour son tenant ? ¦ Dans le Centre de messages": {"q":"Where does the admin track the changes Microsoft announces for their tenant?","e":"New features, retirements, actions to take before a deadline: the Message center is the M365 admin's official source of updates.","a":["In the Message center","In Service health","In usage reports"]},
  "Le rôle « Administrateur de facturation » permet… ¦ De gérer abonnements, achats et factures": {"q":"The “Billing Administrator” role allows you to…","e":"A good example of least privilege: accounting manages billing without access to data or accounts. Assigning licenses requires another role (License Administrator or User Administrator).","a":["Manage subscriptions, purchases, and invoices","Reset non-admins' passwords","Assign and remove users' licenses"]},
  "Un utilisateur supprimé dans Microsoft 365 peut être restauré pendant 30 jours. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A user deleted in Microsoft 365 can be restored for 30 days.","e":"True: they are kept in deleted users for 30 days, along with their data, before permanent deletion."},
  "La feuille de route Microsoft 365 (Roadmap) sert à… ¦ Voir les fonctionnalités en développement et leur date de déploiement prévue": {"q":"The Microsoft 365 Roadmap is used to…","e":"Handy for anticipating a new feature, training users, or preparing a configuration change.","a":["See the features in development and their planned rollout date","See ongoing incidents on services and their progress","Plot the route of the Friday lunchtime pizza delivery driver"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet PowerShell ouvre une session vers Microsoft Graph ? ¦ Connect-MgGraph": {"q":"Which PowerShell cmdlet opens a session to Microsoft Graph?","e":"Connect-MgGraph -Scopes \"User.Read.All\": you request only the permissions you need. Disconnect-MgGraph closes the session.","placeholder":"Verb-Noun…","answers":["Connect-MgGraph"]},
  "Quelle est l'adresse web du Centre d'administration Microsoft 365 ? ¦ admin.microsoft.com": {"q":"What is the web address of the Microsoft 365 admin center?","e":"admin.microsoft.com gives access to users, licenses, billing, service health, and the message center. The specialized centers (Entra, Exchange, Defender…) are opened from there.","placeholder":"address.example.com","answers":["admin.microsoft.com","https://admin.microsoft.com","http://admin.microsoft.com","admin.microsoft.com/","https://admin.microsoft.com/"]},
  "Une entreprise veut Entra ID P2 (PIM, ID Protection) et Defender for Endpoint Plan 2 sans acheter de modules complémentaires. Quelle licence choisir ? ¦ Microsoft 365 E3": {"q":"A company wants Entra ID P2 (PIM, ID Protection) and Defender for Endpoint Plan 2 without buying add-ons. Which license should it choose?","e":"E3 includes Entra ID P1 and Defender for Endpoint Plan 1. Business Premium provides Entra ID P1 and Defender for Business. Only E5 bundles Entra ID P2, Defender for Endpoint P2, and advanced Purview features.","a":["Microsoft 365 E3","Microsoft 365 E5","Microsoft 365 Business Premium"]},
  "Concrètement, c'est quoi une licence Microsoft 365 ? ¦ La clé produit à 25 caractères à saisir dans Word ou Excel": {"q":"In practical terms, what is a Microsoft 365 license?","e":"A license (Microsoft 365 E3, Business Premium…) is assigned to an account and gives it access to services such as Exchange, Teams, or OneDrive. Without a license, the account exists but cannot use these services.","a":["The 25-character product key you enter in Word or Excel","A right to use assigned to your account, which unlocks services","The Office installation file to download to your PC","The personal Microsoft account created with your work email address"]},
  "Premier jour : tu te connectes, mais Outlook t'indique que ta boîte aux lettres est introuvable. Cause la plus probable ? ¦ Ton écran est trop petit pour afficher Outlook": {"q":"First day: you sign in, but Outlook tells you your mailbox cannot be found. Most likely cause?","e":"The Exchange Online mailbox is created when a license that includes it is assigned. A brand-new account without a license can sign in but does not have a mailbox yet.","a":["Your screen is too small to display Outlook","Your temporary password has not been changed yet at first sign-in","Your PC has not yet been enrolled in Intune by support","No license that includes Exchange Online has been assigned to your account yet"]},
  "Ton compte professionnel (prenom.nom@entreprise.fr) et un compte Microsoft personnel (Outlook.com, Hotmail) sont la même chose. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Your work account (prenom.nom@entreprise.fr) and a personal Microsoft account (Outlook.com, Hotmail) are the same thing.","e":"They are two distinct account types: the work account is managed by your organization in Microsoft Entra ID, while the personal account belongs to you. On the sign-in screen, always choose “work or school account” for work."},
  "Tu as besoin d'une licence supplémentaire (Visio, par exemple) pour ton travail. À qui t'adresses-tu ? ¦ Au support informatique ou à l'administrateur de ton organisation": {"q":"You need an additional license (Visio, for example) for your work. Who do you go to?","e":"Licenses are purchased and assigned by your organization: go through internal support. Sharing an account is prohibited and dangerous, and Microsoft support only deals with the tenant's administrators.","a":["IT support or your organization's administrator","Microsoft support directly","A colleague who already has Visio, so they can lend you their account","No one: you install a trial version found on the Internet"]},
  "Où un utilisateur peut-il voir lui-même les licences et abonnements attribués à son compte ? ¦ Dans le Centre de messages": {"q":"Where can a user see the licenses and subscriptions assigned to their own account?","e":"The My Account page lists the work account's subscriptions, without needing admin rights. The Message center and the Billing section of the admin center are reserved for administrators.","a":["In the Message center","In the Microsoft Store","On the My Account page (myaccount.microsoft.com), under Subscriptions","In the Microsoft 365 admin center, under Billing"]},
  "Dans le vocabulaire Microsoft 365, que désigne un « tenant » (locataire) ? ¦ Un utilisateur invité venant d'une autre entreprise partenaire": {"q":"In Microsoft 365 terminology, what does a “tenant” refer to?","e":"Each organization has its own tenant, isolated from the others. All of the company's accounts, licenses, domains, and settings are attached to it.","a":["A guest user coming from another partner company","Your organization's Microsoft 365 space (accounts, domains, data)","A physical Microsoft server installed on the company's premises","The commercial name of the Microsoft 365 E5 offer for large companies"]},
  "Dans une entreprise, qui attribue normalement les licences Microsoft 365 aux employés ? ¦ Chaque employé, depuis Word au premier lancement": {"q":"In a company, who normally assigns Microsoft 365 licenses to employees?","e":"Assignment is done in the Microsoft 365 admin center (or by group) by an admin with a role such as License Administrator or User Administrator.","a":["Each employee, from Word on first launch","The intern, with the admin password found under the keyboard","Microsoft, automatically upon hiring","An administrator with the appropriate role (licenses or users)"]},
  "Un service ne fonctionne pas. Quelles informations utiles donnes-tu au support ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Le message d'erreur exact ou une capture d'écran": {"q":"A service is not working. What useful information do you give to support? (several answers)","e":"The error message, service, time, and number of people affected help diagnose quickly (general outage or account problem). A technician will never ask you for your password.","a":["The exact error message or a screenshot","The affected service and the time of the problem","Your password, so they can test for you","Whether colleagues have the same issue"]},
  "Plusieurs collègues n'arrivent plus à ouvrir Outlook en même temps. Quel est le bon premier réflexe ? ¦ Réinstaller Outlook sur ton poste depuis le portail Office": {"q":"Several colleagues can no longer open Outlook at the same time. What is the right first reflex?","e":"When several people are affected at the same time, it is often a service-side incident: support checks the Microsoft 365 service status. Heavy manipulations on your workstation would fix nothing.","a":["Reinstall Outlook on your workstation from the Office portal","Notify support, who will check whether there is a Microsoft incident","Immediately change your password, in case it has leaked","Delete your Outlook profile, then create a new one"]},
  "Un compte utilisateur peut exister dans Microsoft 365 sans avoir de licence attribuée. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A user account can exist in Microsoft 365 without having a license assigned.","e":"True: the account (identity) and the license are two separate things. An account without a license can sign in but has no access to Outlook, Teams, or the other licensed services."},
  "Comment s'appelle le rôle d'administration qui a tous les droits sur le tenant ? (Administrateur …) ¦ global": {"q":"What is the name of the administration role that has all rights on the tenant? (… Administrator)","e":"The Global Administrator can do everything in the tenant. That is why we limit the number of people who have it and prefer more targeted roles day to day.","placeholder":"global","answers":["global","administrateur global","admin global","global administrator","global admin"]},
  "Tu débutes au support : remets dans l'ordre la prise en charge d'un signalement « Teams ne marche pas » : ¦ Recueillir les infos : message d'erreur, utilisateurs touchés, heure": {"q":"You're starting out in support: put the handling of a “Teams is not working” report in order:","e":"You start by understanding the problem, then rule out a Microsoft outage before looking on the user's side. You only close the ticket after informing the user.","items":["Gather information: error message, affected users, time","Check the Microsoft 365 service status","Apply the fix or escalate to the next level","Inform the user and close the ticket"]},
  "Dans l'adresse ines.martin@contoso.fr, que représente « contoso.fr » ? ¦ Le nom du serveur de ton PC": {"q":"In the address ines.martin@contoso.fr, what does “contoso.fr” represent?","e":"The domain identifies the organization. The company adds and verifies it in the admin center (Settings > Domains) to use it in addresses and sign-in names.","a":["The name of your PC's server","The name of your Teams team","The organization's domain name","Your license ID"]},
  "Que désigne le domaine « contoso.onmicrosoft.com » d'un tenant ? ¦ Le domaine initial du tenant, créé d'office et impossible à supprimer": {"q":"What does the domain “contoso.onmicrosoft.com” of a tenant refer to?","e":"The onmicrosoft.com domain is provided when the tenant is created and is always present, even after a custom domain is added. However, you can choose a different default domain.","a":["The tenant's initial domain, created automatically and impossible to delete","A temporary test domain, to be deleted as soon as the tenant goes live","The domain reserved for guest accounts from other organizations","A domain that the company bought from a registrar such as OVH"]},
  "Retirer la licence d'un utilisateur supprime immédiatement et définitivement sa boîte aux lettres. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Removing a user's license immediately and permanently deletes their mailbox.","e":"False: after the license is removed, the mailbox data is kept for a 30-day grace period before deletion. Reassigning the license in time lets you recover everything."},
  "Un utilisateur a bien une licence Microsoft 365 E3, mais Teams ne s'ouvre pas pour lui. Cause possible côté admin ? ¦ Le rôle Administrateur Teams ne lui a pas été attribué": {"q":"A user does have a Microsoft 365 E3 license, but Teams won't open for them. Possible cause on the admin side?","e":"In the user's page (Licenses and apps), the admin can disable certain apps included in a license: check these boxes before looking any further. Also check the exact license: Microsoft sells Microsoft 365 E3 with Teams and an “E3 (no Teams)” version, which requires a separate Teams Enterprise license. No admin role or team membership is needed to open Teams.","a":["The Teams Administrator role has not been assigned to them","They are not yet a member of any team in Teams","The Teams app was unchecked in their license options","Their Teams meeting policy prohibits recording"]},
  "Depuis la fiche d'un utilisateur dans le centre d'admin Microsoft 365, que peut faire un admin ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Réinitialiser son mot de passe": {"q":"From a user's page in the Microsoft 365 admin center, what can an admin do? (several answers)","e":"The user page lets you manage the account, password, licenses, and sign-in. Reading someone's emails requires explicit delegated access (and a legal basis), not a simple click.","a":["Reset their password","Manage their licenses and apps","Directly read the content of their emails","Block their sign-in"]},
  "Dans le centre d'admin, quel menu sous « Facturation » liste les abonnements achetés par l'organisation ? ¦ Vos produits": {"q":"In the admin center, which menu under “Billing” lists the subscriptions purchased by the organization?","e":"Billing > Your products shows each subscription, its number of licenses, and its options. Assigned licenses can also be tracked in Billing > Licenses.","placeholder":"Billing > …","answers":["Vos produits","Your products"]},
  "Un collaborateur est suspendu temporairement. Comment l'empêcher de se connecter sans supprimer son compte ? ¦ Retirer toutes ses licences suffit à bloquer la connexion": {"q":"An employee is temporarily suspended. How do you prevent them from signing in without deleting their account?","e":"“Block sign-in” prevents any new authentication while keeping the account, licenses, and data. Removing licenses does not block sign-in and starts the countdown to data deletion.","a":["Removing all their licenses is enough to block sign-in","Use the “Block sign-in” option on their account","Rename their email address","Delete their account and restore it later"]},
  "Un problème nécessite l'aide de Microsoft. Comment l'admin ouvre-t-il une demande de support ? ¦ En publiant un message dans le Centre de messages du centre d'admin": {"q":"A problem requires help from Microsoft. How does the admin open a support request?","e":"The Help & support button in the admin center first suggests solutions, then lets you create a service request. The Message center and the roadmap are read-only.","a":["By posting a message in the Message center of the admin center","By adding a comment on the Microsoft 365 roadmap","By calling the support number shown in Outlook's help","Via “Help & support” in the Microsoft 365 admin center"]},
  "Lors de l'ajout d'un domaine personnalisé, comment prouves-tu à Microsoft que tu en es propriétaire ? ¦ En envoyant au support une facture du registrar à ton nom": {"q":"When adding a custom domain, how do you prove to Microsoft that you own it?","e":"Microsoft provides a value to publish (usually a TXT record, sometimes an MX) in the domain's DNS, then checks that it is present. Only after that do you configure the service records.","a":["By sending support an invoice from the registrar in your name","By adding the TXT record provided by Microsoft to the DNS zone","By creating an admin@ mailbox on the domain to receive a code","By importing the domain's SSL certificate into the admin center"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre l'ajout d'un domaine personnalisé dans Microsoft 365 : ¦ Paramètres > Domaines > Ajouter un domaine, puis saisir le nom": {"q":"Put the steps for adding a custom domain in Microsoft 365 in order:","e":"You add and verify the domain, then create the records that make email and clients work. Users only switch to the new domain once everything is in place.","items":["Settings > Domains > Add domain, then enter the name","Publish the TXT record and start the verification","Create the DNS records for the services (MX, CNAME autodiscover, SPF…)","Update users' sign-in names (UPN) and addresses"]},
  "Le Centre de messages peut envoyer aux admins un résumé hebdomadaire par e-mail de ses publications. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"The Message center can send admins a weekly email digest of its posts.","e":"True: in the Message center preferences (Email tab), you can enable the weekly digest and emails for major updates, including to addresses other than your own."},
  "Dans les rapports d'utilisation, les noms des utilisateurs apparaissent sous forme d'identifiants illisibles. Pourquoi ? ¦ Les rapports sont corrompus et doivent être régénérés depuis le centre d'admin": {"q":"In usage reports, users' names appear as unreadable identifiers. Why?","e":"By default, Microsoft conceals user, group, and site names in reports for privacy. An authorized admin can turn off this concealment in Settings > Org settings > Services > Reports.","a":["The reports are corrupted and must be regenerated from the admin center","Only the Global Administrator sees the real names, not the Reports Reader","An E5 or Power BI Pro license is required to display names","Name concealment, enabled by default in the Reports settings"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet Microsoft Graph PowerShell attribue ou retire des licences à un utilisateur ? ¦ Set-MgUserLicense": {"q":"Which Microsoft Graph PowerShell cmdlet assigns or removes licenses for a user?","e":"Set-MgUserLicense takes the -AddLicenses and -RemoveLicenses parameters. It replaces Set-MsolUserLicense (MSOnline) and Set-AzureADUserLicense (AzureAD).","placeholder":"Verb-Noun…","answers":["Set-MgUserLicense"]},
  "Set-MgUserLicense échoue sur un compte tout juste créé par script. Quelle propriété manque le plus souvent ? ¦ UsageLocation": {"q":"Set-MgUserLicense fails on an account that was just created by script. Which property is most often missing?","e":"A license cannot be assigned to a user without a usage location (UsageLocation, a country code such as FR), because service availability depends on the country. The admin center asks for it automatically; a script does not.","a":["UsageLocation","Department","OnPremisesImmutableId","PreferredLanguage"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet liste les SKU du tenant avec les unités activées et consommées (ConsumedUnits) ? ¦ Get-MgUserLicenseDetail": {"q":"Which cmdlet lists the tenant's SKUs with the enabled and consumed units (ConsumedUnits)?","e":"Get-MgSubscribedSku returns SkuPartNumber, SkuId, ConsumedUnits, and PrepaidUnits. Get-MgUserLicenseDetail works per user, and Get-MsolAccountSku comes from the retired MSOnline module.","a":["Get-MgUserLicenseDetail","Get-MsolAccountSku","Get-MgSubscribedSku","Get-MgOrganization"]},
  "En 2026, les modules MSOnline et AzureAD restent la méthode recommandée pour gérer les licences par script. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In 2026, the MSOnline and AzureAD modules remain the recommended way to manage licenses by script.","e":"False: MSOnline stopped working in 2025, and AzureAD was in turn retired starting in late 2025. Microsoft recommends Microsoft Graph PowerShell (Get-MgSubscribedSku, Set-MgUserLicense), Microsoft Entra PowerShell, or the Graph API."},
  "Quelles affirmations sur l'attribution de licences par groupe sont exactes ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Un utilisateur peut hériter de licences de plusieurs groupes à la fois": {"q":"Which statements about group-based license assignment are correct? (several answers)","e":"A user can be a member of several groups carrying licenses, only direct members of a group receive its license, and dynamic groups are supported. An inherited license cannot be removed on the user: you must remove them from the group or change the group's license.","a":["A user can inherit licenses from several groups at once","Members of a nested group do not inherit the parent group's license","It works with dynamic groups","A license inherited from a group can be removed directly on the user's page"]},
  "Quel rôle peut lire l'état des services et le Centre de messages et ouvrir des demandes de support Microsoft, sans gérer utilisateurs ni licences ? ¦ Administrateur du support technique": {"q":"Which role can read service health and the Message center and open Microsoft support requests, without managing users or licenses?","e":"The Service Support Administrator is made for this. The Helpdesk Administrator can also open requests, but they reset users' passwords; the Message Center Reader only sees Message center posts.","a":["Helpdesk Administrator","Service Support Administrator","Message Center Reader","User Administrator"]},
  "Quel rôle peut attribuer n'importe quel rôle Microsoft Entra, y compris Administrateur global, sans être lui-même Administrateur global ? ¦ Administrateur des utilisateurs": {"q":"Which role can assign any Microsoft Entra role, including Global Administrator, without being a Global Administrator themselves?","e":"The Privileged Role Administrator manages role assignments and PIM: it is as sensitive a role as Global Administrator. The Privileged Authentication Administrator manages authentication methods, not roles.","a":["User Administrator","Security Administrator","Privileged Authentication Administrator","Privileged Role Administrator"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la migration de licences attribuées directement vers une attribution par groupe : ¦ Créer ou choisir le groupe cible (statique ou dynamique)": {"q":"Put the migration of directly assigned licenses to group-based assignment in order:","e":"You remove the direct assignments last: a user who has the same license both directly and through a group consumes only one, so there is no service interruption during the switch.","items":["Create or choose the target group (static or dynamic)","Assign the license to the group","Check that the inherited licenses are active and error-free","Remove the licenses directly assigned to users"]},
  "Attribution par groupe : un membre est en erreur « Plans de service en conflit ». Que se passe-t-il ? ¦ Le groupe dépasse la limite de membres pour l'attribution par groupe": {"q":"Group-based assignment: a member shows the error “Conflicting service plans”. What is happening?","e":"Some plans are mutually exclusive (two variants of the same service, for example). You must remove the conflicting direct license or disable the plan concerned. A lack of licenses causes a different error.","a":["The group exceeds the member limit for group-based assignment","There are no longer enough licenses available in the subscription","One of their licenses contains a plan that is incompatible with the group's license","Their usage location differs from the tenant's country"]},
  "Avec Set-MgUserLicense, comment attribuer une licence en désactivant un de ses plans de service ? ¦ -AddLicenses @{SkuId=$sku; DisabledPlans=@($planId)} -RemoveLicenses @()": {"q":"With Set-MgUserLicense, how do you assign a license while disabling one of its service plans?","e":"Disabled plans are passed in the AddLicenses hash table (DisabledPlans, with the plan GUIDs). -RemoveLicenses is mandatory, even if empty. The other parameters do not exist.","a":["-AddLicenses @{SkuId=$sku; DisabledPlans=@($planId)} -RemoveLicenses @()","-AddLicenses $sku -DisabledPlans $planId","-SkuId $sku -ExcludePlans $planId","-AddLicenses @{SkuId=$sku} -RemoveServicePlans @($planId)"]},
  "Copilot peut se tromper : il faut relire et vérifier ce qu'il produit. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Copilot can be wrong: you must proofread and verify what it produces.","e":"True: an AI can make up information with great confidence. It helps you go fast, but responsibility for the content remains yours."},
  "On peut coller des données confidentielles de l'entreprise dans n'importe quelle IA grand public. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"You can paste confidential company data into any consumer AI.","e":"False: this data may be stored or reused outside the company. Use only company-approved tools, such as Copilot with your work account."},
  "Tu veux que Copilot s'appuie sur un fichier précis plutôt que de chercher au hasard. Que fais-tu ? ¦ Tu désactives l'accès au web": {"q":"You want Copilot to rely on a specific file rather than searching at random. What do you do?","e":"Attaching the file or referring to it in the prompt gives Copilot the right source: the answer is more accurate, and the references let you check it.","a":["You turn off web access","You attach or cite the file in your prompt","You add the file to your OneDrive favorites","You pin the file in your “Recent” list"]},
  "Dans Outlook, Copilot est particulièrement utile pour… ¦ Résumer un long fil de discussion": {"q":"In Outlook, Copilot is particularly useful for…","e":"It summarizes conversations and suggests a draft reply, and you stay in control to adjust it.","a":["Summarizing a long email thread","Recovering a permanently deleted email","Unblocking your mailbox when it is full"]},
  "Karim demande à Microsoft 365 Copilot de résumer le budget RH, un fichier auquel il n'a pas accès. Que se passe-t-il ? ¦ Copilot le résume quand même, car il voit tout le tenant": {"q":"Karim asks Microsoft 365 Copilot to summarize the HR budget, a file he does not have access to. What happens?","e":"Microsoft 365 Copilot respects existing permissions: it only uses what the user can already open. That is why you should fix overly broad sharing before deployment: a poorly shared file becomes easy to find.","a":["Copilot summarizes it anyway, because it sees the whole tenant","Copilot cannot use that file, because Karim is not allowed to see it","Copilot automatically requests access from the file owner"]},
  "Dans Word, Copilot peut notamment… ¦ Rédiger un premier jet à partir de ta consigne": {"q":"In Word, Copilot can notably…","e":"Copilot saves you time on the draft; you check it, correct it, and take responsibility for the final content.","a":["Write a first draft from your instructions","Guarantee that the figures it cites are accurate","Sign the contract for you (with a pen, no less)"]},
  "Dans Teams, Copilot peut… ¦ Résumer une réunion et lister les actions, grâce à la transcription": {"q":"In Teams, Copilot can…","e":"To summarize a meeting, Copilot relies on the transcript. Handy if you arrive late or need to write up meeting minutes.","a":["Summarize a meeting and list the action items, thanks to the transcript","Attend the meeting in your place, with your cloned voice","Summarize your colleagues' private conversations for you"]},
  "Pour une bonne demande à Copilot, Microsoft conseille d'indiquer… ¦ L'objectif, le contexte, les sources à utiliser et le résultat attendu": {"q":"For a good request to Copilot, Microsoft recommends stating…","e":"Example: “Summarize this email thread (source) for my manager (context) in 5 bullet points (expectation) to prepare tomorrow's meeting (goal).”","a":["The goal, the context, the sources to use and the expected result","Short keywords, like for a Bing search","The AI model to use, the temperature and the language"]},
  "Utilisé avec ton compte professionnel, Copilot applique la protection des données d'entreprise. Ça signifie notamment… ¦ Que tes demandes ne servent pas à entraîner les modèles d'IA": {"q":"Used with your work account, Copilot applies enterprise data protection. Among other things, this means…","e":"Your prompts are still retained (and searchable in eDiscovery), and the web remains usable, but nothing is used to train the models. That is why you use Copilot with your work account for company data.","a":["That your prompts are not used to train the AI models","That your prompts are erased as soon as the session ends","That Copilot no longer has access to web results"]},
  "Quelles tâches sont bien adaptées à Copilot ? ¦ Résumer un long document": {"q":"Which tasks are well suited to Copilot?","e":"Copilot is an excellent writing and summarization assistant. Decisions that carry commitments remain human.","a":["Summarizing a long document","Suggesting a presentation outline","Rephrasing an email that is too curt","Validating the legal compliance of a contract"]},
  "Pendant le pilote Copilot, une utilisatrice retrouve via Copilot un fichier des salaires partagé par erreur à toute l'organisation. Quelle action est prioritaire ? ¦ Retirer la licence Copilot de l'utilisatrice concernée": {"q":"During the Copilot pilot, a user finds, through Copilot, a salary file that was mistakenly shared with the whole organization. What is the priority action?","e":"Copilot did not “hack” anything: it found a file the user could already open. The problem is the sharing: you fix it at the source and look for other similar cases on the site.","a":["Remove the Copilot license from the user concerned","Fix the file's sharing, then review its site","Delete the Copilot conversation history","Turn off Copilot for the whole company during the investigation"]},
  "Copilot dans Excel donne de meilleurs résultats quand les données sont… ¦ Mises sous forme de tableau, avec des en-têtes clairs": {"q":"Copilot in Excel gives better results when the data is…","e":"Well-named columns and a real table (Ctrl+T) help Copilot understand what it is analyzing.","a":["Formatted as a table, with clear headers","Spread across several sheets, one per month","Presented with merged cells for the titles"]},
  "Copilot Studio permet… ¦ De créer des agents personnalisés, par exemple sur les procédures internes": {"q":"Copilot Studio lets you…","e":"You define the sources (SharePoint sites, documents…) and the agent's behavior, with the organization's access rights. Dashboards are Power BI; business apps are Power Apps.","a":["Build custom agents, for example on internal procedures","Build interactive dashboards from data","Design business apps on SharePoint lists"]},
  "Comment Microsoft 365 Copilot accède-t-il aux données de l'organisation ? ¦ Via Microsoft Graph, dans la limite des autorisations de l'utilisateur": {"q":"How does Microsoft 365 Copilot access the organization's data?","e":"Graph provides access to emails, files, meetings and chats… but only those the user can already see.","a":["Through Microsoft Graph, within the limits of the user's permissions","Through a Copilot service account that reads the whole tenant, then filters","Through an index copied every night into Azure OpenAI storage"]},
  "Pourquoi recommande-t-on un audit des permissions SharePoint avant de déployer Copilot ? ¦ Copilot contourne les permissions et lit tout le tenant : il faut les durcir": {"q":"Why is a SharePoint permissions audit recommended before deploying Copilot?","e":"Copilot respects existing permissions… including the bad ones. An HR folder open to “Everyone” suddenly becomes easy to find: you fix the oversharing beforehand.","a":["Copilot bypasses permissions and reads the whole tenant: they need to be tightened","Copilot surfaces everything the user can open, even an oversharing file","Copilot only indexes sites whose permissions have been audited"]},
  "Dans PowerPoint, Copilot peut notamment… ¦ Créer un brouillon de présentation à partir d'un document Word": {"q":"In PowerPoint, Copilot can notably…","e":"You give it a file or a topic, and it suggests slides with titles, content and visuals. The result remains a draft to review and adjust.","a":["Create a draft presentation from a Word document","Email the presentation to all attendees","Present in your place while you grab a coffee"]},
  "Quelle différence entre Microsoft Copilot Chat (inclus) et Microsoft 365 Copilot (licence payante) ? ¦ Copilot Chat ne fonctionne qu'en anglais et dans le navigateur Edge": {"q":"What is the difference between Microsoft Copilot Chat (included) and Microsoft 365 Copilot (paid license)?","e":"Both apply enterprise data protection. Copilot Chat mostly relies on the web and on what you provide to it (with limited grounding in Outlook). The Microsoft 365 Copilot license adds broad grounding in tenant data (Graph) and full integration in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook and Teams.","a":["Copilot Chat only works in English and in the Edge browser","Only the paid version applies enterprise data protection (EDP)","Copilot Chat relies on the web; the license adds your emails and files (Graph)"]},
  "Avant un déploiement Copilot, un site SharePoint sensible est mal protégé. Quelle fonction de SharePoint Advanced Management l'exclut des résultats de Copilot et de la recherche à l'échelle de l'organisation ? ¦ Le verrouillage du site en lecture seule": {"q":"Before a Copilot deployment, a sensitive SharePoint site is poorly protected. Which SharePoint Advanced Management feature excludes it from Copilot and organization-wide search results?","e":"Restricted Content Discovery prevents the site's content from surfacing in Copilot and in organization-wide search, including files the user recently accessed, and removes Copilot entry points from the site, without changing permissions. It is a stopgap: you then need to fix the site's permissions.","a":["Locking the site as read-only","Restricted Content Discovery","Data access governance (DAG) reports"]},
  "Comment appelle-t-on la question ou l'instruction que tu écris à Copilot ? ¦ prompt": {"q":"What do you call the question or instruction you write to Copilot?","e":"The prompt is the request you give Copilot. The clearer and more precise it is, the more useful the answer.","placeholder":"One word…","answers":["prompt","invite","requête","requete","un prompt","le prompt","une invite","prompts","consigne","une consigne","a prompt","the prompt","request","instruction"]},
  "Copilot t'affiche avec assurance un chiffre ou une citation qui n'existe nulle part dans tes documents. Comment appelle-t-on ce phénomène ? ¦ Un bug d'affichage": {"q":"Copilot confidently shows you a figure or a quote that exists nowhere in your documents. What is this phenomenon called?","e":"A generative AI can produce information that is plausible but false: this is called a hallucination. That is why you always verify important facts before reusing them.","a":["A display bug","A data leak","A hallucination","A version conflict"]},
  "Si tu poses exactement la même question deux fois à Copilot, tu obtiens toujours mot pour mot la même réponse. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"If you ask Copilot exactly the same question twice, you always get the exact same answer word for word.","e":"False: Copilot generates new text with each request, so the wording can vary from one time to the next. This is not a malfunction."},
  "Dans une réponse de Copilot, à quoi servent les références (citations) affichées sous le texte ? ¦ À noter la réponse de 1 à 5": {"q":"In a Copilot response, what are the references (citations) displayed below the text for?","e":"The references point to the documents, emails or pages Copilot relied on. One click is enough to check that the answer matches the source.","a":["Rating the response from 1 to 5","Finding and checking the sources used","Sharing the response with your team","Translating the response into another language"]},
  "Tu voudrais utiliser Microsoft 365 Copilot dans Word et Outlook avec ton compte pro. Qui peut t'attribuer la licence nécessaire ? ¦ Toi-même, depuis les paramètres de Word": {"q":"You would like to use Microsoft 365 Copilot in Word and Outlook with your work account. Who can assign you the required license?","e":"Microsoft 365 Copilot is a license that the company buys and that an administrator assigns to users. You cannot activate it for yourself from an app.","a":["Yourself, from Word's settings","Any colleague who already has the license","Microsoft support, by phone","An administrator in your organization"]},
  "La réponse de Copilot ne te convient pas (trop longue, ton trop formel). Que peux-tu faire ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Lui demander une version plus courte": {"q":"Copilot's response does not suit you (too long, tone too formal). What can you do? (several answers)","e":"Copilot works as a conversation: you refine with follow-up requests (shorter, simpler, different tone…). It does not “retrain” on your emails, and threats do not impress it.","a":["Ask it for a shorter version","Ask it to retrain its model on your emails","Specify the desired tone in a new request","Threaten to switch to a competitor"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre les étapes pour rédiger un document avec Copilot dans Word : ¦ Ouvrir Copilot dans le document Word": {"q":"Put the steps for writing a document with Copilot in Word in order:","e":"You ask, read, adjust, then keep. The final review remains essential: you are responsible for the document you distribute.","items":["Open Copilot in the Word document","Write a prompt describing the document you want","Read the proposed draft","Refine with a follow-up request if needed","Keep the text, then review it before distributing it"]},
  "Tu commences ton prompt par « Agis comme un formateur qui s'adresse à des débutants ». À quoi ça sert ? ¦ À adapter le ton et le niveau de la réponse": {"q":"You start your prompt with “Act as a trainer speaking to beginners”. What is the purpose of this?","e":"Giving a role and a target audience helps Copilot choose the vocabulary, level of detail and tone. It changes neither your rights nor your profile.","a":["To adapt the tone and level of the response","To give Copilot additional rights","To save this role in your Microsoft 365 profile","To share the conversation with the beginners"]},
  "Un utilisateur veut que Copilot lui résume une réunion Teams après sa fin, mais Copilot n'a rien à exploiter. Quelle est la cause la plus courante ? ¦ La réunion comptait trop de participants pour que Copilot l'analyse": {"q":"A user wants Copilot to summarize a Teams meeting after it ends, but Copilot has nothing to work with. What is the most common cause?","e":"To summarize a meeting after the fact, Copilot relies on the transcript. Without a transcript, Copilot can only be used during the meeting, depending on the options chosen by the organizer.","a":["The meeting had too many participants for Copilot to analyze it","Transcription was not turned on during the meeting","The meeting was scheduled from Outlook rather than from Teams","The user was not the meeting organizer"]},
  "Un agent Copilot branché sur un site SharePoint ne répond à chaque utilisateur qu'à partir des contenus que cet utilisateur a le droit de consulter. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A Copilot agent connected to a SharePoint site answers each user only from content that this user is allowed to view.","e":"True: the agent queries the sources with the identity of the person using it. Two colleagues can therefore get different answers if they do not have the same rights on the site."},
  "À quoi sert Copilot Pages ? ¦ À créer des sites SharePoint à partir d'un prompt": {"q":"What is Copilot Pages for?","e":"Copilot Pages lets you take a Copilot response into a collaborative page that you can enrich and share with your colleagues so you can work on it together.","a":["Creating SharePoint sites from a prompt","Scheduling the automatic sending of Copilot responses by email","Turning a Copilot response into an editable, shareable page","Displaying the prompt history of the entire organization"]},
  "Quels principes font partie des principes d'IA responsable affichés par Microsoft ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Équité": {"q":"Which principles are among the responsible AI principles published by Microsoft? (several answers)","e":"Microsoft has six principles: fairness, reliability and safety, privacy and security, inclusiveness, transparency and accountability. “Comprehensiveness” is not one of them.","a":["Fairness","Transparency","Comprehensiveness","Accountability"]},
  "Ticket support : la licence Microsoft 365 Copilot vient d'être attribuée à Léa, mais le bouton Copilot n'apparaît pas dans Word sur son PC. Que vérifies-tu d'abord ? ¦ Que son PC est un PC Copilot+ équipé d'une puce NPU": {"q":"Support ticket: the Microsoft 365 Copilot license has just been assigned to Léa, but the Copilot button does not appear in Word on her PC. What do you check first?","e":"The app must be signed in with the account that holds the license and be up to date; restarting the app helps it pick up the license. Neither a Copilot+ PC nor Teams Premium is required, and the assignment can take a little time to propagate.","a":["That her PC is a Copilot+ PC with an NPU chip","That Léa also has an active Teams Premium license on her account","That Léa has the Global Administrator role","That Word is up to date, signed in with the work account, then restarted"]},
  "Avec Copilot Chat, même sans licence Microsoft 365 Copilot, tu peux joindre un fichier à la conversation pour qu'il l'analyse. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"With Copilot Chat, even without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license, you can attach a file to the conversation for it to analyze.","e":"True: Copilot Chat can work on a file you provide. Without a Microsoft 365 Copilot license, its access to your work data remains limited (limited grounding exists in Outlook); broad search across your emails, files and meetings via Microsoft Graph is reserved for the paid license."},
  "De quoi se compose principalement un agent déclaratif dans Microsoft 365 Copilot ? ¦ D'un script PowerShell exécuté à chaque question": {"q":"What does a declarative agent in Microsoft 365 Copilot mainly consist of?","e":"A declarative agent describes what it must do (instructions), where it looks for information (knowledge such as SharePoint sites) and what it can execute (actions). It relies on the same engine as Copilot, without retraining a model.","a":["A PowerShell script run on every question","Instructions, knowledge sources and possibly actions","A full copy of the team's mailboxes","An AI model trained on company data"]},
  "Avec Microsoft Graph PowerShell, quelle cmdlet liste les licences (SKU) du tenant pour retrouver le SkuId de Microsoft 365 Copilot ? ¦ Get-MgSubscribedSku": {"q":"With Microsoft Graph PowerShell, which cmdlet lists the tenant's licenses (SKUs) to find the SkuId of Microsoft 365 Copilot?","e":"Get-MgSubscribedSku returns the tenant's subscriptions with their SkuId, their SkuPartNumber and the number of licenses consumed. This SkuId is then used with Set-MgUserLicense.","placeholder":"Verb-Noun…","answers":["Get-MgSubscribedSku"]},
  "L'attribution de la licence Copilot par PowerShell échoue sur des comptes créés par script. Quelle est la cause classique ? ¦ Le compte n'a pas encore de boîte aux lettres Exchange": {"q":"Assigning the Copilot license with PowerShell fails on accounts created by script. What is the classic cause?","e":"A license cannot be assigned to a user without a usage location (UsageLocation), because service availability depends on the country. You set it, for example, with Update-MgUser -UsageLocation. The Exchange mailbox, for its part, is created after the license is assigned.","a":["The account does not have an Exchange mailbox yet","The account is not a member of any Teams team","The UsageLocation property is not set","The account has never signed in to Outlook"]},
  "Tu dois donner la licence Copilot à 200 personnes et suivre les arrivées et départs sans script. Quelle approche est la plus maintenable ? ¦ Attribuer la licence une par une dans Utilisateurs actifs": {"q":"You need to give the Copilot license to 200 people and track joiners and leavers without a script. Which approach is the most maintainable?","e":"With group-based licensing, every group member receives the license and loses it when leaving the group. Combined with a dynamic group or one managed by HR, it is the easiest option to maintain.","a":["Assign the license one by one in Active users","Use group-based licensing in Microsoft Entra ID","Create a mail flow rule in Exchange","Deploy an Intune configuration profile"]},
  "Un utilisateur demande à Copilot de rédiger un nouveau document Word à partir d'un fichier étiqueté « Confidentiel ». Que devient l'étiquette de sensibilité ? ¦ Le nouveau document ne porte aucune étiquette": {"q":"A user asks Copilot to draft a new Word document from a file labeled “Confidential”. What happens to the sensitivity label?","e":"Copilot applies label inheritance: content created from labeled files takes the highest-priority label among the sources. Protection therefore follows the information.","a":["The new document carries no label","The new document receives the tenant's default label","Copilot refuses to create the document","The new document inherits the “Confidential” label"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre les grandes étapes d'un déploiement Microsoft 365 Copilot : ¦ Vérifier les prérequis (licences de base, applications Microsoft 365, comptes)": {"q":"Put the main steps of a Microsoft 365 Copilot deployment in order:","e":"You secure data access before opening up Copilot, test on a small group, then expand and measure. Because Copilot surfaces everything people can already see, cleaning up permissions comes before wider rollout.","items":["Check the prerequisites (base licenses, Microsoft 365 apps, accounts)","Audit and fix oversharing in SharePoint and OneDrive","Launch a pilot with a small group","Assign licenses on a larger scale","Track adoption with usage reports"]},
  "Où un admin consulte-t-il nativement l'utilisation de Microsoft 365 Copilot (utilisateurs actifs, applications utilisées) ? ¦ Centre d'administration Microsoft 365 > Rapports > Utilisation": {"q":"Where does an admin natively view Microsoft 365 Copilot usage (active users, apps used)?","e":"The usage reports in the Microsoft 365 admin center include a report dedicated to Microsoft 365 Copilot. Entra sign-in logs show authentications, not Copilot usage by app.","a":["Microsoft 365 admin center > Reports > Usage","Exchange admin center > Mail flow","Intune admin center > Devices > Compliance","Entra admin center > Sign-in logs"]},
  "Quels outils servent à gouverner les agents créés avec Copilot Studio ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Les règles de transport du centre d'administration Exchange": {"q":"Which tools are used to govern agents built with Copilot Studio? (several answers)","e":"Copilot Studio is built on Power Platform: environments separate agents and DLP policies limit which connectors can be used. Exchange mail flow rules and Windows update rings have no effect on agents.","a":["Mail flow rules in the Exchange admin center","Managed environments in the Power Platform admin center","Power Platform data policies (DLP) on connectors","Windows update rings in Intune"]},
  "Dans le cadre d'une enquête juridique, tu dois retrouver les prompts et réponses Copilot d'un utilisateur. Quel outil utilises-tu ? ¦ Le journal d'activité de SharePoint": {"q":"As part of a legal investigation, you need to retrieve a user's Copilot prompts and responses. Which tool do you use?","e":"Copilot interactions are retained in the service and can be searched, placed on hold and exported with Microsoft Purview eDiscovery, like emails or Teams chats.","a":["The SharePoint activity log","Microsoft Edge history","Microsoft Purview eDiscovery","The Teams admin center"]},
  "Avant d'ouvrir Copilot, tu veux repérer les sites SharePoint surpartagés (liens trop larges, accès à toute l'organisation). Quelle fonctionnalité t'aide à les identifier ? ¦ Les rapports de messages en quarantaine du portail Defender": {"q":"Before opening up Copilot, you want to spot overshared SharePoint sites (links that are too broad, access for the whole organization). Which feature helps you identify them?","e":"Data access governance reports (SharePoint Advanced Management) list, among other things, sites with many sharing links or open to the whole organization. It is a concrete basis for targeting the cleanup.","a":["The quarantined message reports in the Defender portal","SharePoint's data access governance reports","The OneDrive file activity report in the admin center","The Secure Score dashboard and its recommendations"]},
  "Un document est chiffré par une étiquette de sensibilité. Quels droits d'utilisation l'utilisateur doit-il avoir pour que Copilot puisse s'appuyer sur son contenu ? ¦ Uniquement VIEW (Afficher)": {"q":"A document is encrypted by a sensitivity label. Which usage rights must the user have for Copilot to be able to rely on its content?","e":"For encrypted content to be used by Copilot, the user must have the VIEW and EXTRACT rights. A label that removes the copy right therefore prevents Copilot from summarizing the content, even if the user can open it.","a":["Only VIEW","VIEW and EXTRACT (Copy)","EDIT and PRINT","Only OWNER"]},
  "Un document partagé contient du texte caché qui ordonne à l'IA d'ignorer ses consignes et d'exfiltrer des données. Comment appelle-t-on ce type d'attaque ? ¦ injection de prompt": {"q":"A shared document contains hidden text that orders the AI to ignore its instructions and exfiltrate data. What is this type of attack called?","e":"This is prompt injection (called indirect when the malicious instruction is hidden in content processed by the AI). Microsoft builds in protections against these attacks, but the principle of least privilege remains the best limit.","placeholder":"Attack name…","answers":["injection de prompt","prompt injection","injection d'invite","injection de prompt indirecte","injection de prompts","indirect prompt injection","prompt injection attack","prompt injections"]},
  "Microsoft retire Restricted SharePoint Search (plus de nouvelle activation depuis juillet 2026, retrait complet fin janvier 2027). Que doit faire un admin qui l'utilisait pour limiter Copilot ? ¦ Rien : la configuration sera migrée automatiquement": {"q":"Microsoft is retiring Restricted SharePoint Search (no new activations since July 2026, full retirement at the end of January 2027). What should an admin who used it to limit Copilot do?","e":"The configuration is not migrated automatically: without action, content that was previously restricted could become visible again in Copilot. You apply Restricted Content Discovery (SharePoint Advanced Management) to the sensitive sites, and fix permissions in parallel. Read-only does not prevent Copilot from reading a site.","a":["Nothing: the configuration will be migrated automatically","Apply Restricted Content Discovery themselves to the sensitive sites","Remove all Copilot licenses until the full retirement","Set the sites concerned to read-only to hide them from Copilot"]},
  "Lors d'un audit de surpartage avant Copilot, quelle attribution de permission est l'un des signaux les plus fréquents d'exposition trop large ? ¦ Le groupe « Tout le monde sauf les utilisateurs externes »": {"q":"During an oversharing audit before Copilot, which permission assignment is one of the most common signs of overly broad exposure?","e":"“Everyone except external users” gives access to every internal account in the tenant. Since Copilot can surface everything a user can read, these sites should be reviewed first.","a":["The “Everyone except external users” group","The site's “Owners” group, with full control","The members of the Teams team associated with the SharePoint site","A “Specific people” link sent to one colleague"]},
  "Les interactions des utilisateurs avec Microsoft 365 Copilot sont enregistrées dans l'audit de Microsoft Purview et peuvent y être recherchées. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"User interactions with Microsoft 365 Copilot are recorded in the Microsoft Purview audit and can be searched there.","e":"True: the Purview audit logs Copilot interactions (CopilotInteraction activity), with the user, the app and the resources accessed. The content of the prompts and responses, however, is searched with eDiscovery."},
  "Quand Microsoft 365 Copilot s'appuie sur le web pour compléter une réponse, qu'est-ce qui est envoyé au service de recherche Bing ? ¦ Le prompt complet et les fichiers cités": {"q":"When Microsoft 365 Copilot uses the web to complete a response, what is sent to the Bing search service?","e":"Copilot generates a short search query from the prompt and sends it to Bing; the documents and the entire conversation are not transmitted. Admins can also control web access through policy.","a":["The full prompt and the cited files","The entire ongoing conversation","A search query generated from the prompt","Nothing: Copilot never uses the web"]},
  "Tu veux empêcher Copilot de traiter les fichiers portant l'étiquette « Hautement confidentiel », même pour les utilisateurs qui y ont accès. Quelle solution Microsoft Purview utilises-tu ? ¦ Une stratégie de rétention appliquée à l'emplacement Copilot": {"q":"You want to prevent Copilot from processing files carrying the “Highly Confidential” label, even for users who have access to them. Which Microsoft Purview solution do you use?","e":"Purview DLP offers a location dedicated to Microsoft 365 Copilot that lets you exclude content carrying certain labels from responses. Retention and records manage preservation, and Communication Compliance monitors communications: none of them prevents Copilot from using the content.","a":["A retention policy applied to the Copilot location","A Communication Compliance policy on Copilot interactions","A DLP policy with the Microsoft 365 Copilot location","A retention label that declares the file as a record"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre le traitement d'une demande par Microsoft 365 Copilot : ¦ L'utilisateur saisit son prompt dans une application Microsoft 365": {"q":"Put the processing of a request by Microsoft 365 Copilot in order:","e":"Grounding in Graph takes place before the call to the model, and post-processing filters the response before it is displayed. This flow is what ensures the user's permissions are respected.","items":["The user enters their prompt in a Microsoft 365 app","Copilot retrieves, via Microsoft Graph, the data the user has access to (grounding)","The enriched prompt is sent to the large language model","The response goes through post-processing (responsible AI, security and compliance checks)","The response is returned to the app, with its references"]},
  "Avec Microsoft Graph PowerShell, quelle commande retire la licence Copilot ($sku) de l'utilisateur $u ? ¦ Set-MgUserLicense -UserId $u -AddLicenses @() -RemoveLicenses @($sku)": {"q":"With Microsoft Graph PowerShell, which command removes the Copilot license ($sku) from user $u?","e":"Set-MgUserLicense requires both the -AddLicenses and -RemoveLicenses parameters: for a simple removal, you pass an empty array to -AddLicenses. Remove-MgUserLicense does not exist, and AssignedLicenses cannot be modified via Update-MgUser.","a":["Set-MgUserLicense -UserId $u -AddLicenses @() -RemoveLicenses @($sku)","Remove-MgUserLicense -UserId $u -SkuId $sku -Confirm:$false","Set-MgUserLicense -UserId $u -RemoveLicenses @($sku) -Confirm:$false","Update-MgUser -UserId $u -AssignedLicenses @{RemoveLicenses=@($sku)}"]},
  "Un agent Copilot Studio est publié avec l'option « Aucune authentification ». Quelle conséquence dois-tu anticiper ? ¦ L'agent n'est visible que par les administrateurs de l'environnement Power Platform": {"q":"A Copilot Studio agent is published with the “No authentication” option. What consequence should you anticipate?","e":"Without authentication, the agent does not know who is talking to it: it is open to anyone who reaches the channel and cannot query sources that require the user's identity, such as SharePoint. Reserve it for content that is truly public.","a":["The agent is only visible to the administrators of the Power Platform environment","Any user of the channel can use it, with no identity to query SharePoint","The agent automatically inherits its creator's rights on all SharePoint sites","The agent stays blocked until a Copilot license is assigned to each visitor"]},
  "L'accès conditionnel se configure dans… ¦ Microsoft Entra ID": {"q":"Conditional Access is configured in…","e":"Conditional Access (Entra ID) applies rules such as “if sign-in from outside France or on an unmanaged device, then require MFA or block”.","a":["Microsoft Entra ID","Microsoft Purview","Microsoft Defender for Office 365"]},
  "Les « paramètres de sécurité par défaut » d'Entra ID imposent notamment… ¦ L'inscription à la MFA pour tous les utilisateurs": {"q":"Microsoft Entra ID “security defaults” notably enforce…","e":"They turn on a free security baseline: MFA for everyone, blocking of legacy authentication protocols, and protection for admins.","a":["MFA registration for all users","Blocking sign-ins from abroad","Password expiration every 90 days"]},
  "Connexion suspecte depuis un pays inhabituel. Où la vérifier ? ¦ Dans les journaux de connexion d'Entra ID": {"q":"Suspicious sign-in from an unusual country. Where do you check it?","e":"The sign-in logs show the IP, location, device, application, and MFA result for every attempt.","a":["In the Entra ID sign-in logs","In the admin center usage reports","In Exchange message trace"]},
  "Un compte d'accès d'urgence (« break-glass »), c'est… ¦ Un compte admin synchronisé depuis l'AD pour reprendre la main": {"q":"An emergency access (“break-glass”) account is…","e":"It is used if Conditional Access or MFA locks out all admins. It is “cloud-only” (not synced), kept out of everyday use, and every sign-in triggers an alert.","a":["An admin account synced from AD to regain control","A service account without MFA used by scripts","A cloud admin account reserved for emergencies, heavily protected and monitored"]},
  "Le SSPR, c'est… ¦ La réinitialisation du mot de passe en libre-service": {"q":"SSPR is…","e":"Users prove their identity (app, phone…) and reset their own password, without calling support.","a":["Self-service password reset","The Entra ID password expiration policy","Password synchronization with on-premises AD"]},
  "Un groupe dynamique dans Entra ID… ¦ Ajoute et retire ses membres selon leurs attributs (service, site…)": {"q":"A dynamic group in Entra ID…","e":"Example: all users whose department is “Accounting”. A new hire joins the group automatically.","a":["Adds and removes its members based on their attributes (department, site…)","Gets its members by invitation from the group owner","Deletes itself when no longer used (expiration policy)"]},
  "Microsoft Entra Connect sert à… ¦ Synchroniser l'Active Directory local avec Entra ID (identités hybrides)": {"q":"Microsoft Entra Connect is used to…","e":"Users keep the same account for the on-premises network and Microsoft 365.","a":["Synchronize on-premises Active Directory with Entra ID (hybrid identities)","Synchronize users between two Microsoft 365 tenants (cross-tenant)","Connect third-party SaaS applications to Entra ID for SSO"]},
  "Microsoft Entra ID est le nouveau nom de… ¦ Azure Active Directory": {"q":"Microsoft Entra ID is the new name for…","e":"Azure AD was renamed Microsoft Entra ID in 2023. It is the cloud directory that manages identities and access to Microsoft 365.","a":["Azure Active Directory","On-premises Active Directory (AD DS)","Azure Information Protection"]},
  "L'authentification unique (SSO) permet… ¦ De se connecter une fois pour accéder à plusieurs applications": {"q":"Single sign-on (SSO) lets you…","e":"A single sign-in (with MFA) opens Teams, Outlook, SharePoint, and the apps connected to Entra ID. Fewer passwords, fewer risks.","a":["Sign in once to access several applications","Use the same password on all websites","Synchronize your passwords across all your devices"]},
  "La correspondance de nombres dans Microsoft Authenticator (taper le nombre affiché à l'écran) sert à… ¦ Vérifier que tu sais encore lire les chiffres": {"q":"Number matching in Microsoft Authenticator (typing the number shown on screen) is used to…","e":"You can no longer approve a request out of reflex: you have to be in front of the real sign-in page to know the number.","a":["Check that you can still read digits","Counter “MFA fatigue”: you have to see the sign-in screen to approve","Replace the password with a code that changes every 30 seconds"]},
  "Un utilisateur a changé de téléphone et ne reçoit plus ses demandes MFA. L'admin… ¦ Réinitialise son mot de passe pour relancer les notifications": {"q":"A user changed phones and no longer receives MFA requests. The admin…","e":"The user sets up Authenticator again on the new phone. Their identity is verified beforehand through another channel: this is a classic social engineering target.","a":["Resets their password to restart notifications","Requires them to re-register their authentication methods","Excludes them from Conditional Access until further notice"]},
  "Un compte invité (B2B) dans Entra ID permet… ¦ À un partenaire externe d'accéder à des ressources avec son propre compte": {"q":"A guest (B2B) account in Entra ID lets…","e":"The partner keeps their own identity, and you give them only the access they need. Remember to clean up guests regularly.","a":["An external partner access resources with their own account","You create a member account with a paid license for the partner","You merge two tenants into a single Entra ID directory"]},
  "Sur quels signaux une stratégie d'accès conditionnel peut-elle s'appuyer ? ¦ L'utilisateur ou son groupe": {"q":"Which signals can a Conditional Access policy rely on?","e":"You combine who, from which device, from where, to which application, and with what level of risk to decide: allow, require MFA, or block. Conditional Access never reads the content of messages.","a":["The user or their group","Device state (compliant or not)","Location (country, IP address)","The content of the email the user wants to open"]},
  "Pour tester une nouvelle stratégie d'accès conditionnel sans bloquer personne : ¦ Le mode « Rapport uniquement »": {"q":"To test a new Conditional Access policy without blocking anyone:","e":"Report-only mode simulates the policy and shows in the logs who would have been blocked. A disabled policy is not evaluated and leaves no trace.","a":["“Report-only” mode","Turn it on on a Friday evening and cross your fingers","The “Off” state, then reading the sign-in logs"]},
  "Les « emplacements nommés » dans Entra ID servent à… ¦ Définir des adresses IP ou des pays pour les utiliser dans l'accès conditionnel": {"q":"“Named locations” in Entra ID are used to…","e":"Example: allow access without extra MFA from the office IP, and block sign-ins from countries where the company has no activity.","a":["Define IP addresses or countries to use in Conditional Access","Group users from the same site in an administrative unit","Associate a verified domain name with each company office"]},
  "Dans Entra ID Protection, un « utilisateur à risque » est détecté par exemple quand… ¦ Ses identifiants apparaissent dans une fuite de données connue": {"q":"In Entra ID Protection, a “risky user” is detected, for example, when…","e":"Leaked credentials are a typical user risk detection; repeated risky sign-ins (malicious IP, impossible travel…) also raise this risk. A Conditional Access policy based on user risk can then require remediation, for example a secure password change after MFA.","a":["Their credentials appear in a known data leak","They have not yet registered an MFA method","Their Windows PC is marked non-compliant in Intune"]},
  "Quelle méthode est considérée comme résistante au phishing ? ¦ Le code à usage unique reçu par SMS": {"q":"Which method is considered phishing-resistant?","e":"A FIDO2 key and a passkey are bound to the real site: a fake site cannot reuse them. An SMS code can be copied, and even a notification with number matching can be approved on a fake relay page.","a":["A one-time code received by SMS","A FIDO2 security key or a passkey","An Authenticator notification with number matching"]},
  "Quel rôle Entra ID donne tous les droits sur le tenant ? ¦ Administrateur général": {"q":"Which Entra ID role grants full rights over the tenant?","e":"The Global Administrator can do everything. Microsoft recommends having fewer than five, all protected by strong MFA.","placeholder":"Role name","answers":["Administrateur général","Administrateur global","Global Administrator","Global Admin","Admin global","Admin général"]},
  "Quelles méthodes peuvent servir de deuxième facteur (MFA) pour te connecter à ton compte Microsoft professionnel ? ¦ Une notification dans l'application Microsoft Authenticator": {"q":"Which methods can serve as a second factor (MFA) to sign in to your Microsoft work account?","e":"A second factor must be something you have (phone, key) or something you are (biometrics). A second password or a secret question is still “something you know”: it can be guessed or stolen just like the first.","a":["A notification in the Microsoft Authenticator app","A FIDO2 security key or a passkey","A second password, different from the first","The answer to a secret question (your first pet’s name)"]},
  "Le « passe d'accès temporaire » (Temporary Access Pass) d'Entra ID, c'est… ¦ Un mot de passe provisoire que l'utilisateur doit changer à la première connexion": {"q":"The Entra ID “Temporary Access Pass” is…","e":"Ideal for a new hire or after a lost phone: the user signs in with the code, then sets up Authenticator or a passkey. It expires on its own.","a":["A temporary password the user must change at first sign-in","A 24-hour guest access for a contractor external to the tenant","A time-limited code, issued by an admin, to register authentication methods"]},
  "Dans Privileged Identity Management (PIM), un rôle attribué comme « éligible » signifie que l'utilisateur… ¦ Doit l'activer, pour une durée limitée, avant de pouvoir s'en servir": {"q":"In Privileged Identity Management (PIM), a role assigned as “eligible” means the user…","e":"An “active” assignment gives the role continuously; “eligible” leaves it dormant until just-in-time activation, with justification, MFA, or approval depending on the settings. Fewer standing privileges, so less damage if an account is compromised. PIM requires Entra ID P2.","a":["Must activate it, for a limited time, before being able to use it","Has it permanently, but read-only until an admin approves it","Can only use it from a compliant device enrolled in Intune"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet du module Microsoft Graph PowerShell liste les utilisateurs du tenant ? ¦ Get-MgUser": {"q":"Which Microsoft Graph PowerShell cmdlet lists the users in the tenant?","e":"After Connect-MgGraph -Scopes \"User.Read.All\", Get-MgUser -All retrieves all accounts. It replaces Get-MsolUser and Get-AzureADUser from the retired older modules.","placeholder":"Verb-Noun…","answers":["Get-MgUser"]},
  "Quelle adresse ouvre le portail « Mon compte », où tu gères toi-même ton compte professionnel ? ¦ portal.azure.com": {"q":"Which address opens the “My Account” portal, where you manage your own work account?","e":"myaccount.microsoft.com is the user’s My Account portal: security info, password, devices, recent activity. admin.microsoft.com and portal.azure.com are reserved for administrators.","a":["portal.azure.com","admin.microsoft.com","myaccount.microsoft.com","myapps.microsoft.com"]},
  "Le portail « Mes applications » (myapps.microsoft.com) sert à… ¦ installer la suite Office sur ton PC personnel ou pro": {"q":"The “My Apps” portal (myapps.microsoft.com) is used to…","e":"My Apps gathers the work applications published for you (Microsoft 365 and third-party apps connected to Entra ID), often with single sign-on.","a":["install the Office suite on your personal or work PC","find and launch the work apps you have access to","buy approved apps from the Microsoft Store","manage your team’s licenses and access"]},
  "Tu reçois une demande d'approbation dans Microsoft Authenticator alors que tu n'essaies pas de te connecter : tu dois l'approuver pour la faire disparaître. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"You receive an approval request in Microsoft Authenticator while you are not trying to sign in: you should approve it to make it go away.","e":"False: a request you did not trigger means someone may know your password. Deny it, change your password, and notify support or security."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre l'ajout de Microsoft Authenticator comme méthode de connexion : ¦ Ouvrir la page « Informations de sécurité » dans Mon compte": {"q":"Put the steps for adding Microsoft Authenticator as a sign-in method in order:","e":"You start from Security info, the wizard displays a QR code that the app scans, then a test notification confirms everything works.","items":["Open the “Security info” page in My Account","Click “Add sign-in method” and choose Microsoft Authenticator","In the app, add a work or school account","Scan the QR code displayed on screen","Approve the test notification sent to the phone"]},
  "Dans le portail Mon compte, comment s'appelle la page où tu ajoutes ou supprimes tes méthodes de vérification (Authenticator, téléphone…) ? ¦ Informations de sécurité": {"q":"In the My Account portal, what is the name of the page where you add or remove your verification methods (Authenticator, phone…)?","e":"The “Security info” page lists your sign-in methods and lets you add or remove them or change the default method.","placeholder":"Page name","answers":["Informations de sécurité","Informations de securite","Security info"]},
  "Dans Microsoft Authenticator, le code à 6 chiffres affiché sous ton compte professionnel change… ¦ toutes les 30 secondes": {"q":"In Microsoft Authenticator, the 6-digit code shown under your work account changes…","e":"It is a time-based one-time code (TOTP) renewed every 30 seconds: even if intercepted, it quickly becomes unusable.","a":["every 30 seconds","every 5 minutes","every hour","once a day"]},
  "Pourquoi ton entreprise t'impose-t-elle l'authentification multifacteur (MFA) ? ¦ Pour te connecter plus vite grâce à la notification sur ton téléphone": {"q":"Why does your company require multifactor authentication (MFA)?","e":"MFA adds proof that you have (phone, security key) or that you are (biometrics): the password alone is no longer enough to get into your account.","a":["To sign you in faster with the notification on your phone","To be able to do without a password on all websites","To check that you are awake before 9 a.m.","So that a hacker who has your password cannot get in"]},
  "Quelles sont de bonnes pratiques pour ton mot de passe professionnel ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Utiliser une longue phrase de passe difficile à deviner": {"q":"What are good practices for your work password? (several answers)","e":"Length, uniqueness, and confidentiality are the three key reflexes. Support never needs your password, and a sticky note is within anyone’s reach.","a":["Use a long passphrase that is hard to guess","Write it on a sticky note under the keyboard so you don’t forget it","Do not reuse the same password on personal sites","Never share it, even with someone who says they are calling from support"]},
  "Tu connais ton mot de passe actuel et tu veux le changer depuis le web. Où vas-tu ? ¦ Dans Outlook, Fichier > Options": {"q":"You know your current password and want to change it from the web. Where do you go?","e":"The My Account portal (myaccount.microsoft.com) offers a Password tile to change it. The Outlook, Teams, or OneDrive settings do not manage your Entra ID password.","a":["In Outlook, File > Options","In My Account, via the “Password” tile","In Teams, Settings > Privacy","In OneDrive, Settings > Backup"]},
  "Dans Mon compte, la page « Appareils » te permet de voir les appareils liés à ton compte et de désactiver un appareil perdu. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In My Account, the “Devices” page lets you see the devices linked to your account and disable a lost device.","e":"True: the Devices page lists the devices registered or joined with your account and offers to disable a lost or stolen device. Also notify your support team so they can take the other measures."},
  "Un utilisateur pense que quelqu'un s'est connecté à son compte. Dans Mon compte, où peut-il vérifier ses dernières connexions lui-même ? ¦ Organisations": {"q":"A user thinks someone signed in to their account. In My Account, where can they check their latest sign-ins themselves?","e":"The Recent activity page shows recent sign-ins (location, device, application) and lets the user report “This wasn’t me”, which guides them toward securing their account.","a":["Organizations","Recent activity","Settings & Privacy","Subscriptions"]},
  "Le verrouillage intelligent (smart lockout) d'Entra ID… ¦ désactive le compte dans l'AD local après 5 échecs, jusqu'à l'intervention d'un admin": {"q":"Entra ID smart lockout…","e":"Smart lockout temporarily blocks attempts after a series of failures and takes into account where the attempts come from so as not to penalize the real user. The lock lifts on its own after a delay.","a":["disables the account in on-premises AD after 5 failures, until an admin steps in","forces the user to call support for every account unlock","temporarily locks sign-in after too many failures, without penalizing the real user","blocks the attacker’s IP address in the company’s network firewall"]},
  "Quelles informations trouves-tu dans le détail d'une connexion des journaux de connexion d'Entra ID ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ L'adresse IP et l'emplacement approximatif": {"q":"What information do you find in the details of a sign-in in the Entra ID sign-in logs? (several answers)","e":"The log shows IP, location, application, device, error code, and the Conditional Access result. The password is obviously never logged.","a":["The IP address and approximate location","The application the user tried to access","The password entered during a failure","The Conditional Access policies applied and their result"]},
  "Il est recommandé qu'un utilisateur enregistre plusieurs méthodes de vérification, pour ne pas être bloqué s'il perd l'une d'elles. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"It is recommended that a user register several verification methods, so they are not locked out if they lose one.","e":"True: with a single method, a lost or changed phone locks the user out. A second method (another device, security key, phone) avoids a call to support."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre une réinitialisation de mot de passe en libre-service (SSPR) : ¦ Cliquer sur « Mot de passe oublié ? » sur la page de connexion": {"q":"Put a self-service password reset (SSPR) in order:","e":"SSPR first verifies the account, then the identity through the registered methods (Authenticator, SMS, email…), and only then lets you set a new password.","items":["Click “Forgot your password?” on the sign-in page","Enter your user ID and retype the verification characters","Prove your identity with the requested method(s)","Choose a new password","Sign in again with the new password"]},
  "Quelle adresse courte (aka.ms/…) envoie directement un utilisateur vers la réinitialisation de mot de passe en libre-service ? ¦ aka.ms/sspr": {"q":"Which short address (aka.ms/…) takes a user straight to self-service password reset?","e":"aka.ms/sspr leads to the Entra ID self-service password reset page: handy to give to a locked-out user.","placeholder":"aka.ms/…","answers":["aka.ms/sspr","https://aka.ms/sspr","sspr"]},
  "L'« inscription combinée des informations de sécurité » dans Entra ID permet… ¦ de fusionner deux comptes utilisateurs en un seul compte Entra": {"q":"“Combined security information registration” in Entra ID lets you…","e":"With combined registration, the user declares their methods only once (Security info page) and they are used for both MFA and SSPR.","a":["merge two user accounts into a single Entra account","register your MFA and reset methods in one go","share the same MFA method between colleagues","synchronize passwords with on-premises Active Directory"]},
  "Un utilisateur voit une fenêtre « Autorisations demandées » : une application tierce inconnue veut lire ses mails et ses fichiers. Que lui conseilles-tu ? ¦ Accepter : Microsoft a forcément vérifié l'application": {"q":"A user sees a “Permissions requested” window: an unknown third-party app wants to read their emails and files. What do you advise?","e":"This is a classic consent phishing scenario: once accepted, the app accesses the data without a password, and MFA does not stop it. You decline and have it checked.","a":["Accept: Microsoft surely verified the app","Accept, then remove the app later","Decline if in doubt and report the request to support","Accept, because MFA already protects their data"]},
  "Tu veux empêcher les utilisateurs d'accorder eux-mêmes des autorisations à des applications tierces. Où le règles-tu dans le centre d'administration Microsoft Entra ? ¦ Utilisateurs > Paramètres utilisateur > Les utilisateurs peuvent inscrire des applications": {"q":"You want to prevent users from granting permissions to third-party apps themselves. Where do you configure this in the Microsoft Entra admin center?","e":"The user consent settings are under Enterprise applications > Consent and permissions. You can disallow consent there or limit it to verified publishers, and enable the admin consent request workflow. The “Users can register applications” setting concerns creating applications, not consent.","a":["Users > User settings > Users can register applications","Protection > Authentication methods > Policies > Registration settings","Enterprise applications > Consent and permissions > User consent settings","Identity > Applications > App registrations > API permissions"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet du module Microsoft Graph PowerShell ouvre la connexion au tenant, avec par exemple -Scopes \"User.Read.All\" ? ¦ Connect-MgGraph": {"q":"Which Microsoft Graph PowerShell cmdlet opens the connection to the tenant, with for example -Scopes \"User.Read.All\"?","e":"Connect-MgGraph establishes the Microsoft Graph PowerShell session; the -Scopes parameter specifies the requested permissions. Connect-AzureAD and Connect-MsolService belong to retired modules.","placeholder":"Verb-Noun","answers":["Connect-MgGraph"]},
  "Un compte utilisateur est compromis. Quelles actions dans Entra ID sont pertinentes ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Réinitialiser son mot de passe": {"q":"A user account is compromised. Which actions in Entra ID are relevant? (several answers)","e":"Resetting, revoking sessions, and blocking sign-in cut off the attacker’s access. You cannot manually remove a member from a dynamic group: the membership rule decides.","a":["Reset their password","Revoke their sessions to invalidate active tokens","Manually remove them from their dynamic groups","Block their sign-in during the analysis"]},
  "Créer des stratégies d'accès conditionnel nécessite une licence Microsoft Entra ID P1 (incluse par exemple dans Microsoft 365 E3 ou Business Premium) ou supérieure. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Creating Conditional Access policies requires a Microsoft Entra ID P1 license (included for example in Microsoft 365 E3 or Business Premium) or higher.","e":"True: Conditional Access is an Entra ID P1 feature. Tenants without P1 rely on security defaults."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la création d'une stratégie d'accès conditionnel exigeant la MFA : ¦ Ouvrir Accès conditionnel dans le centre d'administration Microsoft Entra et créer une nouvelle stratégie": {"q":"Put the creation of a Conditional Access policy requiring MFA in order:","e":"You first define the assignments (who, which resources), then the access control, and you start in Report-only to measure the impact before enabling. Excluding break-glass accounts avoids locking yourself out.","items":["Open Conditional Access in the Microsoft Entra admin center and create a new policy","Choose the targeted users or groups, excluding emergency accounts","Select the target resources (cloud apps)","Under Grant, check “Require multifactor authentication”","Set “Enable policy” to Report-only, then create"]},
  "Tu veux que seuls certains rôles puissent inviter des utilisateurs externes (B2B). Où se trouve ce réglage ? ¦ Identités externes > Paramètres de collaboration externe": {"q":"You want only certain roles to be able to invite external users (B2B). Where is this setting?","e":"The external collaboration settings (External Identities) define who can invite, guest access restrictions, and allowed or blocked domains. The Invite button simply uses these rules.","a":["External Identities > External collaboration settings","Users > All users > Invite external user","Enterprise applications > Properties","Roles and administrators > Guest"]},
  "Sur un gros tenant, Get-MgUser ne renvoie qu'une partie des utilisateurs. Quel paramètre ajoutes-tu pour tous les récupérer ? ¦ -ResultSize Unlimited": {"q":"On a large tenant, Get-MgUser returns only some of the users. Which parameter do you add to retrieve them all?","e":"Microsoft Graph cmdlets return a single page of results by default; -All follows the pagination to the end. -ResultSize Unlimited is a parameter of Exchange Online cmdlets, not Graph.","a":["-ResultSize Unlimited","-All","-Top 0","-Filter \"*\""]},
  "L'évaluation continue de l'accès (Continuous Access Evaluation, CAE) permet… ¦ de renouveler automatiquement les jetons d'accès toutes les heures pour tous les services": {"q":"Continuous Access Evaluation (CAE) makes it possible to…","e":"With CAE, compatible services (Exchange Online, SharePoint, Teams…) are notified of critical events and can reject a still-valid token, instead of waiting for its natural expiration.","a":["automatically renew access tokens every hour for all services","re-evaluate all Conditional Access policies once a night, on every session","continuously measure sign-in risk (suspicious IP, impossible travel…) with ID Protection","revoke a still-valid token as soon as a critical event occurs (account disabled, password changed…)"]},
  "Dans une stratégie d'accès conditionnel, un utilisateur à la fois inclus (via un groupe) et exclu (via un autre groupe) n'est pas concerné par la stratégie. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In a Conditional Access policy, a user who is both included (via one group) and excluded (via another group) is not affected by the policy.","e":"True: exclusions always take precedence over inclusions. This is what allows you to cleanly exclude emergency accounts from all policies."},
  "Quelles exigences peux-tu imposer à l'activation d'un rôle éligible dans Privileged Identity Management ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Une authentification multifacteur à l'activation": {"q":"Which requirements can you enforce when activating an eligible role in Privileged Identity Management? (several answers)","e":"PIM role settings let you require MFA (or an authentication context), justification, ticket information, and approval, with a maximum activation duration. MSOnline is a retired module, unrelated to PIM.","a":["Multifactor authentication at activation","A justification entered by the user","Approval from one or more designated approvers","Activation possible only through the MSOnline PowerShell module"]},
  "Dans l'accès conditionnel, le contrôle « Exiger la force d'authentification » sert à… ¦ exiger un mot de passe plus long que la stratégie de mot de passe par défaut": {"q":"In Conditional Access, the “Require authentication strength” control is used to…","e":"Authentication strength goes further than “Require MFA”: it restricts the allowed methods (phishing-resistant MFA, FIDO2 keys, Windows Hello for Business…). Risk belongs to Entra ID Protection, and frequency to session controls.","a":["require a longer password than the default password policy","restrict the allowed methods, for example to phishing-resistant MFA","calculate the user’s risk level at each sign-in","enforce a specific re-authentication frequency for each application"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet Microsoft Graph PowerShell révoque toutes les sessions de connexion d'un utilisateur (jetons d'actualisation) ? ¦ Revoke-MgUserSignInSession": {"q":"Which Microsoft Graph PowerShell cmdlet revokes all of a user’s sign-in sessions (refresh tokens)?","e":"Revoke-MgUserSignInSession -UserId invalidates the user’s refresh tokens, so they must re-authenticate. It is the equivalent of “Revoke sessions” in the admin center.","placeholder":"Verb-Noun","answers":["Revoke-MgUserSignInSession"]},
  "Un utilisateur voit ses mails partir vers une adresse inconnue. Premier réflexe ? ¦ Augmenter le niveau du filtre anti-spam entrant": {"q":"A user sees their emails going to an unknown address. First reflex?","e":"A hidden forwarding rule is a classic sign of a compromised account. You delete it, then secure the account.","a":["Raise the level of the inbound anti-spam filter","Add the unknown address to blocked senders","Check the mailbox rules and automatic forwarding"]},
  "Une boîte aux lettres partagée (ex. support@) permet… ¦ À plusieurs personnes de lire et d'envoyer depuis une adresse commune": {"q":"A shared mailbox (e.g., support@) lets you…","e":"Everyone accesses it with their own account, without sharing credentials. Up to 50 GB, it generally doesn’t require a license. Writing to several people without a shared mailbox is a distribution list; the SharePoint site comes with a Microsoft 365 group.","a":["Let several people read and send from a common address","Write to a whole department with a single address, without a shared mailbox","Give a team a shared calendar and SharePoint site"]},
  "Groupe Microsoft 365 ou liste de distribution : quelle différence ? ¦ La liste accepte des membres externes, le groupe seulement des internes": {"q":"Microsoft 365 group or distribution list: what is the difference?","e":"The Microsoft 365 group is the foundation of a Teams team, and it can include guests. The distribution list is just for writing to several people with a single address.","a":["The list accepts external members, the group only internal ones","The group adds a shared mailbox, calendar, and SharePoint site; the list only distributes","The group is only for Teams; the list also shares a calendar"]},
  "Un client affirme ne jamais avoir reçu un mail. L'admin utilise… ¦ Le suivi des messages (message trace) du centre d'admin Exchange": {"q":"A customer claims they never received an email. The admin uses…","e":"Message trace shows whether the email was sent, delivered, quarantined, or rejected.","a":["Message trace in the Exchange admin center","The Entra ID sign-in logs","The mailbox audit log in Purview"]},
  "Pour réserver une salle de réunion depuis Outlook, l'admin crée… ¦ Une boîte aux lettres de ressource (salle)": {"q":"To book a meeting room from Outlook, the admin creates…","e":"The room appears in invitations, accepts or declines based on its availability, and can follow booking rules.","a":["A resource (room) mailbox","A “Room” user account with a license","A shared mailbox named “Room”"]},
  "Un alias de messagerie, c'est… ¦ Une adresse supplémentaire qui arrive dans la même boîte": {"q":"An email alias is…","e":"contact@ and direction@ can arrive in the same mailbox. You can also add one after a name change.","a":["An additional address that arrives in the same mailbox","A distribution list that forwards to several mailboxes","An external contact shown in the global address list"]},
  "Une règle de flux de messagerie (règle de transport) permet par exemple… ¦ D'ajouter un bandeau « Mail externe, prudence » aux messages venant de l'extérieur": {"q":"A mail flow rule (transport rule) makes it possible, for example, to…","e":"Mail flow rules apply to all of the organization’s mail flow: warnings, redirects, blocks, legal disclaimers… Sorting one person’s emails is an inbox rule.","a":["Add an “External email, be careful” banner to messages coming from outside","Sort a single user’s emails into their folders based on the sender","Require MFA when a user opens Outlook away from the office"]},
  "Un mail légitime n'est jamais arrivé et le suivi indique « Quarantaine ». L'admin… ¦ Examine le message en quarantaine et le libère s'il est sûr": {"q":"A legitimate email never arrived and the trace says “Quarantine”. The admin…","e":"Quarantine holds suspicious messages. You check before releasing, and adjust the rules if a trusted sender is blocked by mistake.","a":["Reviews the quarantined message and releases it if it is safe","Allows the sender’s entire domain without opening the message","Asks the sender to resend it from another address"]},
  "L'enregistrement DNS MX d'un domaine indique… ¦ Le serveur qui reçoit les mails du domaine": {"q":"A domain’s MX DNS record indicates…","e":"During a migration to Microsoft 365, switching the MX makes new emails arrive in Exchange Online. The servers allowed to send are defined by SPF (TXT record).","a":["The server that receives the domain’s emails","The servers allowed to send for the domain","The IP address of the domain’s website"]},
  "Par défaut, Exchange Online bloque le transfert automatique des mails vers des adresses externes. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"By default, Exchange Online blocks automatic forwarding of emails to external addresses.","e":"True: it is a protection against data leaks and compromised accounts. The admin can allow it case by case."},
  "L'archivage en ligne, dans Exchange Online… ¦ Ajoute une boîte d'archive pour désengorger la boîte principale": {"q":"Online archiving in Exchange Online…","e":"Old messages are moved there (manually or by policy) and remain accessible from Outlook.","a":["Adds an archive mailbox to relieve the primary mailbox","Exports old emails to a PST file on the computer","Places the mailbox on hold so nothing is lost"]},
  "À quoi sert la découverte automatique (Autodiscover) ? ¦ À configurer automatiquement Outlook à partir de l'adresse mail": {"q":"What is Autodiscover used for?","e":"The user enters their email address, and Outlook finds the server and settings on its own thanks to a DNS record.","a":["To automatically configure Outlook from the email address","To verify the authenticity of incoming emails (SPF, DKIM, DMARC)","To suggest available rooms when sending an invitation"]},
  "Quel outil d'Exchange Online permet de suivre le parcours d'un mail envoyé ou reçu ? ¦ Suivi des messages": {"q":"Which Exchange Online tool lets you track the path of a sent or received email?","e":"In the Exchange admin center: Mail flow > Message trace. You can see whether the email was delivered, quarantined, or rejected. In PowerShell, it is Get-MessageTraceV2.","placeholder":"Tool name","answers":["Suivi des messages","Message trace","Trace des messages","Suivi de message","Suivi du message","Suivi des mails","Message tracing","Trace de message","Mail trace","Message tracking"]},
  "Quel type de boîte permet à toute une équipe de gérer l'adresse contact@, sans licence supplémentaire ? ¦ Boîte aux lettres partagée": {"q":"Which type of mailbox lets a whole team manage the contact@ address, without an extra license?","e":"The shared mailbox doesn’t need a license (up to 50 GB): members access it from their own Outlook.","placeholder":"Mailbox type","answers":["Boîte aux lettres partagée","Boîte partagée","Boite aux lettres partagee","Boite partagee","Boîte mail partagée","Boite mail partagee","Shared mailbox","BAL partagée","BAL partagee","Shared mail box","Shared inbox","Shared email box"]},
  "Sur une boîte partagée, le droit « Envoyer en tant que » (Send As), par rapport à « Envoyer de la part de » : ¦ Le mail semble venir de la boîte partagée, sans mention de l'expéditeur réel": {"q":"On a shared mailbox, the “Send As” permission, compared to “Send on Behalf”:","e":"With “Send As”, the recipient sees only the shared mailbox address. “Send on Behalf” displays both names, which reveals who wrote it.","a":["The email appears to come from the shared mailbox, with no mention of the actual sender","The email shows “First Last on behalf of support@” to the recipient","The email is sent from your own address, with support@ as the reply address"]},
  "Dans quels cas une boîte aux lettres partagée Exchange Online a-t-elle besoin d'une licence ? ¦ Quand elle dépasse 50 Go de stockage": {"q":"In which cases does an Exchange Online shared mailbox need a license?","e":"Without a license, a shared mailbox is limited to 50 GB and cannot be placed on litigation hold. The number of members who access it, however, requires no extra license.","a":["When it exceeds 50 GB of storage","As soon as a second member is added","When it is placed on litigation hold","So that several people can send from the address"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet Exchange Online donne à un utilisateur l'accès total (FullAccess) à une boîte aux lettres ? ¦ Add-MailboxPermission": {"q":"Which Exchange Online cmdlet gives a user full access (FullAccess) to a mailbox?","e":"Add-MailboxPermission -Identity support@contoso.com -User marie@contoso.com -AccessRights FullAccess. For the “Send As” permission, it is Add-RecipientPermission.","placeholder":"Verb-Noun…","answers":["Add-MailboxPermission"]},
  "Activer la signature DKIM pour un domaine personnalisé dans Microsoft 365 : remets les étapes dans l'ordre. ¦ Récupérer les deux enregistrements CNAME (selector1 et selector2) fournis par Microsoft 365": {"q":"Enabling DKIM signing for a custom domain in Microsoft 365: put the steps in order.","e":"If you enable DKIM before the CNAMEs are visible in DNS, enabling fails. Two selectors let Microsoft rotate keys without interruption.","items":["Get the two CNAME records (selector1 and selector2) provided by Microsoft 365","Publish these two CNAMEs in the domain’s DNS zone","Wait for DNS propagation","Enable DKIM signing for the domain (Defender portal or Set-DkimSigningConfig -Enabled $true)"]},
  "Dans le nouvel Outlook, où crées-tu ta signature de mail ? ¦ Paramètres > Comptes > Signatures": {"q":"In the new Outlook, where do you create your email signature?","e":"The signature is managed in Settings > Accounts > Signatures. You can create several and choose which one is added by default to new messages and replies.","a":["Settings > Accounts > Signatures","Settings > General > Appearance","View > Layout > Reading pane","Settings > Calendar > Events"]},
  "Une réponse automatique d'absence peut envoyer un message différent aux personnes externes à ton entreprise. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"An automatic out-of-office reply can send a different message to people outside your company.","e":"Outlook lets you set one message for your colleagues and another for outside people, or even reply only to your external contacts. Handy to avoid giving too many details to strangers."},
  "Tu veux repérer d'un coup d'œil, par une couleur, tous les mails liés au projet Alpha. Dans Outlook, tu utilises… ¦ les catégories": {"q":"You want to spot at a glance, by color, all the emails related to the Alpha project. In Outlook, you use…","e":"Categories associate a name and a color with messages (and appointments): you can then sort or search by category. High importance flags an urgent email to the recipient, without filing anything on your side.","a":["categories","high importance","Focused Inbox","automatic replies"]},
  "On t'a donné accès à la boîte partagée support@. Comment l'afficher dans Outlook sur le web ? ¦ Te déconnecter, puis te reconnecter avec l'identifiant et le mot de passe de support@": {"q":"You have been given access to the shared mailbox support@. How do you display it in Outlook on the web?","e":"In Outlook on the web, right-clicking “Folders” lets you add a shared mailbox you have access to. It then appears in your folder pane, without a separate password.","a":["Sign out, then sign back in with the support@ username and password","Right-click “Folders” > “Add shared folder or mailbox”","Create an inbox rule that forwards support@ emails to you","Ask the admin for a PST export of the mailbox, then open it in Outlook"]},
  "Un mail attendu d'un fournisseur a atterri dans « Courrier indésirable ». Que fais-tu ? ¦ Tu le supprimes et demandes au fournisseur de le renvoyer": {"q":"An expected email from a supplier landed in “Junk Email”. What do you do?","e":"Marking the message as not junk puts it back in the inbox and helps the filter stop classifying this sender as junk. Deleting it does nothing for future emails.","a":["You delete it and ask the supplier to resend it","You forward it to your personal address","You move it to Drafts","You mark it as “Not junk”"]},
  "Quelles actions une règle de boîte de réception Outlook peut-elle faire automatiquement ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Déplacer le message dans un dossier": {"q":"What actions can an Outlook inbox rule perform automatically? (several answers)","e":"A rule can file, mark as read, categorize, or forward a message based on conditions (sender, subject…). It does not rewrite the content of a received email.","a":["Move the message to a folder","Edit the text of the received message","Mark the message as read","Forward the message to someone"]},
  "Tu partages ton calendrier avec un collègue mais il ne doit voir que tes créneaux libres ou occupés. Quelle autorisation choisis-tu ? ¦ Peut modifier": {"q":"You share your calendar with a colleague but they should only see your free or busy slots. Which permission do you choose?","e":"“Can view when I’m busy” shows only availability, with no subject or location. The other levels give access to details, or even editing.","a":["Can edit","Can view when I’m busy","Can view all details","Delegate"]},
  "Tu as le droit d'envoyer depuis support@. Dans un nouveau message Outlook, comment faire ? ¦ Écrire « support@ » au début de l'objet": {"q":"You have permission to send from support@. In a new Outlook message, how do you do it?","e":"The “From” field is not always displayed by default: once visible, you select the shared mailbox address there. Putting support@ in copy does not change the sender.","a":["Type “support@” at the start of the subject","Put support@ in copy of the message","Show the “From” field and choose support@ there","Change your display name in your profile"]},
  "Dans Outlook pour Windows, depuis ta boîte de réception, quel raccourci clavier crée un nouveau message ? ¦ Ctrl+N": {"q":"In Outlook for Windows, from your inbox, which keyboard shortcut creates a new message?","e":"Ctrl+N opens a new item of the current view’s type: a new email from the inbox, a new appointment from the calendar.","placeholder":"E.g.: Ctrl+…","answers":["Ctrl+N","Ctrl + N","Ctrl N","CtrlN"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre les étapes pour activer ta réponse automatique dans le nouvel Outlook : ¦ Ouvrir les Paramètres (roue dentée)": {"q":"Put the steps to turn on your automatic reply in the new Outlook in order:","e":"The automatic reply is set in Settings > Accounts > Automatic replies. By setting a time period, it stops on its own when you return.","items":["Open Settings (gear icon)","Go to Accounts > Automatic replies","Turn on automatic replies","Write the message and, if needed, set the time period","Save"]},
  "Dans Outlook, que fait le bouton « Archiver » sur un mail ? ¦ Il le supprime définitivement": {"q":"In Outlook, what does the “Archive” button do to an email?","e":"“Archive” puts the message in the Archive folder: your inbox stays clean and the email remains viewable and findable through search.","a":["It permanently deletes it","It moves it to the Archive folder, out of the inbox","It moves it to the Exchange Online archive mailbox","It compresses it into a ZIP file to save space"]},
  "Tu as supprimé un mail par erreur ce matin. Où le cherches-tu en premier ? ¦ Dans Brouillons": {"q":"You deleted an email by mistake this morning. Where do you look for it first?","e":"A deleted email first goes to “Deleted Items”, from where you can move it back to the inbox. If it was emptied from that folder, “Recover deleted items” can often still retrieve it.","a":["In Drafts","In Sent Items","In Junk Email","In Deleted Items"]},
  "Une boîte aux lettres partagée a son propre mot de passe, que chaque membre de l'équipe utilise pour s'y connecter. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A shared mailbox has its own password, which each team member uses to sign in to it.","e":"Each member accesses the shared mailbox with their own account, thanks to the permissions granted by the admin. No password is shared, which also preserves traceability."},
  "Dans Outlook sur le web, quelle option te laisse quelques secondes pour annuler un mail juste après avoir cliqué sur « Envoyer » ? ¦ Rappeler ce message": {"q":"In Outlook on the web, which option gives you a few seconds to cancel an email right after you click “Send”?","e":"“Undo send” (Settings > Mail > Compose and reply) holds the message for a few seconds, long enough to click Undo. Recall acts after sending and only within your organization, with no guarantee of success.","a":["Recall this message","Delay delivery","Undo send","Save as draft"]},
  "Un salarié quitte l'entreprise ; son manager doit continuer à consulter ses mails. Bonne pratique courante ? ¦ Réinitialiser son mot de passe et le transmettre au manager": {"q":"An employee leaves the company; their manager needs to keep reading their emails. Common good practice?","e":"Converting the mailbox to a shared mailbox keeps the emails accessible to authorized people, without sharing a password, and often frees up the license (except for needs such as archiving or a specific hold).","a":["Reset their password and give it to the manager","Convert their mailbox to a shared mailbox and give the manager access","Export their mailbox to a PST on the manager’s computer","Delete the account and restore the mailbox later"]},
  "Pour lire facilement les en-têtes d'un mail suspect (serveurs traversés, SPF, DKIM…), quel outil Microsoft utilises-tu ? ¦ L'analyseur d'en-têtes de message (Message Header Analyzer)": {"q":"To easily read the headers of a suspicious email (servers traversed, SPF, DKIM…), which Microsoft tool do you use?","e":"The header analyzer (in Microsoft Remote Connectivity Analyzer or as an Outlook add-in) formats the headers: delays between servers, SPF/DKIM/DMARC results, spam score.","a":["The Message Header Analyzer","Exchange message trace","Exchange mail flow reports","The Support and Recovery Assistant (SaRA)"]},
  "L'admin a donné l'accès total à une boîte partagée via un groupe de sécurité. Elle n'apparaît pas toute seule dans Outlook classique. Pourquoi ? ¦ La boîte partagée n'a pas de licence Exchange Online attribuée": {"q":"The admin gave full access to a shared mailbox through a security group. It does not appear automatically in classic Outlook. Why?","e":"Automapping (AutoMapping) only works for a permission granted directly to the user. Through a group, everyone must add the mailbox manually in Outlook.","a":["The shared mailbox has no Exchange Online license assigned","Classic Outlook only displays shared mailboxes in online mode","Cached Exchange Mode must first be turned off on the computer","Automapping does not apply to access granted through a group"]},
  "Un groupe de contacts que tu crées dans tes contacts Outlook apparaît automatiquement dans la liste d'adresses globale, pour tous tes collègues. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A contact group you create in your Outlook contacts automatically appears in the global address list, for all your colleagues.","e":"False: a contact group is personal and exists only in your contacts. For a list visible to the whole organization, the admin creates a distribution list or a Microsoft 365 group."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la création d'une règle de boîte de réception dans le nouvel Outlook : ¦ Ouvrir Paramètres > Courrier > Règles": {"q":"Put the creation of an inbox rule in the new Outlook in order:","e":"Rules are managed in Settings > Mail > Rules. A rule = a name, at least one condition (sender, subject…), and at least one action (move, forward…).","items":["Open Settings > Mail > Rules","Click “Add new rule”","Name the rule","Set the condition, then the action","Save the rule"]},
  "Dans Outlook pour Windows, quel raccourci clavier bascule directement vers le calendrier ? ¦ Ctrl+2": {"q":"In Outlook for Windows, which keyboard shortcut switches directly to the calendar?","e":"Ctrl+2 opens the calendar, Ctrl+1 goes back to mail, and Ctrl+3 opens contacts. Handy for switching between views without the mouse.","placeholder":"e.g., Ctrl+…","answers":["Ctrl+2","Ctrl + 2","Ctrl 2","Ctrl2"]},
  "Un utilisateur reçoit un rapport de non-remise (NDR) avec le code 5.1.1. Cause la plus probable ? ¦ La boîte aux lettres du destinataire est pleine (quota dépassé)": {"q":"A user receives a non-delivery report (NDR) with code 5.1.1. Most likely cause?","e":"Code 5.1.1 indicates a recipient not found: typo, deleted address, or old autocomplete entry. First thing to do: check the address. A full mailbox or an oversized message gives other codes (5.2.2, 5.3.4).","a":["The recipient’s mailbox is full (quota exceeded)","The recipient’s address is incorrect or does not exist","The attachment exceeds the maximum allowed size","The recipient turned on an out-of-office automatic reply"]},
  "Tu organises une réunion avec six collègues. Quel outil d'Outlook montre leurs disponibilités côte à côte pour trouver un créneau ? ¦ La Boîte de réception Prioritaire": {"q":"You are organizing a meeting with six colleagues. Which Outlook tool shows their availability side by side to find a time slot?","e":"The Scheduling Assistant displays the participants’ (and rooms’) free and busy slots on a single grid, to choose a time that suits everyone.","a":["Focused Inbox","Automatic replies","Delegate access","The Scheduling Assistant"]},
  "En PowerShell Exchange Online, quelle commande convertit la boîte d'un utilisateur en boîte partagée ? ¦ Set-Mailbox -Identity jdupont -Type Shared": {"q":"In Exchange Online PowerShell, which command converts a user’s mailbox to a shared mailbox?","e":"Set-Mailbox with -Type Shared changes the mailbox type without losing its content. The other cmdlets listed do not exist.","a":["Set-Mailbox -Identity jdupont -Type Shared","New-SharedMailbox -From jdupont","Convert-Mailbox -Identity jdupont -Shared","Set-User -Identity jdupont -Mailbox Shared"]},
  "Quels mécanismes DNS aident à lutter contre l'usurpation de ton domaine de messagerie ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ SPF": {"q":"Which DNS mechanisms help fight spoofing of your email domain? (several answers)","e":"SPF lists the servers allowed to send, DKIM signs the messages, DMARC says what to do on failure and sends reports. The MX only indicates where to deliver incoming mail.","a":["SPF","DKIM","MX record","DMARC"]},
  "Ton script Exchange Online tourne dans un runbook Azure Automation, sans mot de passe ni certificat stocké. Quel paramètre de Connect-ExchangeOnline utilise l'identité managée du compte Automation ? ¦ -ManagedIdentity": {"q":"Your Exchange Online script runs in an Azure Automation runbook, with no password or certificate stored. Which Connect-ExchangeOnline parameter uses the Automation account’s managed identity?","e":"Connect-ExchangeOnline -ManagedIdentity -Organization contoso.onmicrosoft.com authenticates with the managed identity (system-assigned or, with -ManagedIdentityAccountId, user-assigned). The identity must have the Exchange.ManageAsApp permission and a suitable Entra role.","placeholder":"-Parameter","answers":["-ManagedIdentity","ManagedIdentity"]},
  "Par défaut, les éléments supprimés récupérables sont conservés 14 jours. Comment passer au maximum autorisé pour une boîte ? ¦ Set-Mailbox -RetainDeletedItemsFor 30": {"q":"By default, recoverable deleted items are kept for 14 days. How do you set it to the maximum allowed for a mailbox?","e":"RetainDeletedItemsFor is set per mailbox (or via Set-MailboxPlan for new ones) with a maximum of 30 days. To keep items longer, you use Microsoft Purview retention or a litigation hold.","a":["Set-Mailbox -RetainDeletedItemsFor 30","Set-Mailbox -RetainDeletedItemsFor 90","Set-MailboxFolder -DeletedItemsRetention 30","Set-OrganizationConfig -DeletedItemRetention 365"]},
  "Tu donnes FullAccess sur une boîte à un utilisateur, mais elle ne doit pas s'ajouter automatiquement à son Outlook. Quelle commande ? ¦ Add-MailboxPermission -Identity support -User jdupont -AccessRights FullAccess -InheritanceType None": {"q":"You give a user FullAccess on a mailbox, but it must not be added automatically to their Outlook. Which command?","e":"The -AutoMapping $false parameter of Add-MailboxPermission prevents automatic addition in classic Outlook. Add-RecipientPermission is for the SendAs permission, and Set-Mailbox has no AutoMapping parameter.","a":["Add-MailboxPermission -Identity support -User jdupont -AccessRights FullAccess -InheritanceType None","Add-MailboxPermission -Identity support -User jdupont -AccessRights FullAccess -AutoMapping $false","Add-RecipientPermission -Identity support -Trustee jdupont -AccessRights FullAccess","Set-Mailbox -Identity support -AutoMapping $false -GrantFullAccess jdupont"]},
  "Dans Exchange Online, le droit « Envoyer en tant que » (SendAs) sur une boîte s'accorde avec Add-RecipientPermission, et non avec Add-ADPermission. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In Exchange Online, the “Send As” (SendAs) permission on a mailbox is granted with Add-RecipientPermission, not Add-ADPermission.","e":"Add-ADPermission is reserved for on-premises Exchange Server. Online, you use Add-RecipientPermission -AccessRights SendAs -Trustee <user>."},
  "Quelle commande donne à jdupont le droit « Envoyer de la part de » sur la boîte support@ ? ¦ Add-RecipientPermission -Identity support -Trustee jdupont -AccessRights SendOnBehalf": {"q":"Which command gives jdupont the “Send on Behalf” permission on the support@ mailbox?","e":"“Send on Behalf” is a property of the mailbox: Set-Mailbox -GrantSendOnBehalfTo, here with the @{Add=…} syntax so as not to overwrite existing delegates. SendOnBehalf is not a valid AccessRights value.","a":["Add-RecipientPermission -Identity support -Trustee jdupont -AccessRights SendOnBehalf","Add-MailboxPermission -Identity support -User jdupont -AccessRights SendOnBehalf","Set-Mailbox -Identity support -GrantSendOnBehalfTo @{Add='jdupont'}","Set-MailboxDelegate -Identity support -SendOnBehalf jdupont"]},
  "Parmi ces cmdlets, lesquelles existent réellement dans Exchange Online PowerShell ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Get-EXOMailbox": {"q":"Among these cmdlets, which ones actually exist in Exchange Online PowerShell? (several answers)","e":"Get-EXOMailbox is the optimized cmdlet from the V3 module, Get-MessageTraceV2 replaces the old Get-MessageTrace, and the automatic reply is set with Set-MailboxAutoReplyConfiguration. Set-MailboxOutOfOffice does not exist.","a":["Get-EXOMailbox","Get-MessageTraceV2","Set-MailboxOutOfOffice","Set-MailboxAutoReplyConfiguration"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre un déploiement DMARC prudent pour un domaine : ¦ Publier SPF et activer DKIM": {"q":"Put a cautious DMARC rollout for a domain in order:","e":"You start in monitoring mode (p=none) to spot misconfigured legitimate senders, then tighten gradually. Going straight to p=reject risks blocking legitimate emails (marketing tools, business apps…).","items":["Publish SPF and enable DKIM","Publish DMARC with p=none and a reporting address (rua)","Analyze the reports and fix the legitimate sources that fail","Switch to p=quarantine","Switch to p=reject"]},
  "Où publie-t-on l'enregistrement DMARC du domaine contoso.com ? ¦ Un TXT sur contoso.com, à côté du SPF": {"q":"Where do you publish the DMARC record for the domain contoso.com?","e":"DMARC is published as a TXT on the _dmarc subdomain (e.g., “v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:…”). The selector1/selector2._domainkey CNAMEs are for DKIM, and the TXT at the root carries SPF.","a":["A TXT on contoso.com, next to the SPF","A CNAME on selector1._domainkey.contoso.com","A secondary MX on dmarc.contoso.com","A TXT on _dmarc.contoso.com"]},
  "Une règle Outlook qui affiche une alerte ou joue un son à l'arrivée d'un mail ne s'exécute que lorsque Outlook est ouvert. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"An Outlook rule that displays an alert or plays a sound when an email arrives only runs when Outlook is open.","e":"Some actions depend on the client (sound, alert, moving to a PST…): the rule becomes “client-only”. Purely server-side rules (move, forward…) run even when Outlook is closed."},
  "Tu veux masquer une boîte aux lettres de la liste d'adresses globale (GAL) sans la supprimer. Quelle commande ? ¦ Set-Mailbox -Identity compta -HiddenFromAddressListsEnabled $true": {"q":"You want to hide a mailbox from the global address list (GAL) without deleting it. Which command?","e":"HiddenFromAddressListsEnabled $true removes the mailbox from the GAL and address lists: it still receives emails. The other parameters and cmdlets listed do not exist in Exchange Online.","a":["Set-Mailbox -Identity compta -HiddenFromAddressListsEnabled $true","Set-Mailbox -Identity compta -GALVisible $false","Set-Recipient -Identity compta -ShowInAddressBook None","Remove-AddressListMember -Identity compta -List GAL"]},
  "Pour envoyer un gros fichier à un collègue, le mieux c'est… ¦ Le mettre en pièce jointe d'un mail": {"q":"To send a large file to a colleague, the best option is…","e":"A link avoids duplicates and overloaded mailboxes: everyone works on the same version.","a":["Attach it to an email","Share a OneDrive link","Compress it into a ZIP and send it by email"]},
  "Où ranger tes fichiers de travail personnels, pas encore partagés ? ¦ Sur le bureau du PC": {"q":"Where should you store your personal work files that are not yet shared?","e":"OneDrive is your personal space, backed up and accessible everywhere. The PC desktop disappears along with the PC.","a":["On the PC desktop","In the General channel in Teams","In your OneDrive"]},
  "Pourquoi partager un lien plutôt qu'une pièce jointe ? ¦ Tout le monde travaille sur la même version": {"q":"Why share a link rather than an attachment?","e":"One version, reversible permissions, less storage. It's the attachment that leaves the recipient with a copy you can no longer take back.","a":["Everyone works on the same version","You can change or remove access afterwards","It lightens mailboxes","The recipient keeps their copy even after access is removed"]},
  "Un fichier supprimé de OneDrive peut être récupéré pendant un certain temps. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A file deleted from OneDrive can be recovered for a certain period of time.","e":"True: it goes to the recycle bin (93 days by default for a work account). After that, you need a backup."},
  "La différence entre OneDrive et SharePoint ? ¦ OneDrive = espace d'équipe, SharePoint = espace perso": {"q":"What is the difference between OneDrive and SharePoint?","e":"OneDrive is for your own files, SharePoint for team files (it's also what stores the files of Teams teams).","a":["OneDrive = team space, SharePoint = personal space","OneDrive = personal space, SharePoint = team space","OneDrive = sync on the PC, SharePoint = web access only"]},
  "Lien OneDrive « Toute personne disposant du lien » : le risque ? ¦ Seuls les comptes de ton organisation pourront l'ouvrir": {"q":"OneDrive “Anyone with the link” link: what is the risk?","e":"Once forwarded or leaked, this link opens the file to anyone. For sensitive content, choose “Specific people”.","a":["Only accounts in your organization will be able to open it","The file becomes editable by your whole department","Anyone who has the link opens the file, without signing in"]},
  "Un collègue a écrasé ton document Word sur OneDrive. Tu… ¦ Restaures une version précédente via l'historique des versions": {"q":"A colleague overwrote your Word document on OneDrive. You…","e":"OneDrive and SharePoint keep version history: right-click the file, then “Version history”. The recycle bin, on the other hand, only contains deleted files, not old versions.","a":["Restore a previous version via version history","Retrieve the old version from the OneDrive recycle bin","Ask support for a backup restore"]},
  "Partager un fichier OneDrive de façon sécurisée : ¦ Sélectionner le fichier": {"q":"Sharing a OneDrive file securely:","e":"The link setting is made before sending: “Specific people” ensures that only the chosen recipients can open the file.","items":["Select the file","Click “Share”","Set the link to “Specific people”","Enter the recipient and send"]},
  "Deux personnes peuvent modifier en même temps un document Word enregistré dans OneDrive ou SharePoint. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Two people can edit a Word document saved in OneDrive or SharePoint at the same time.","e":"True: this is co-authoring. Everyone sees the others' changes live, no more need to send each other versions."},
  "Synchroniser OneDrive sur ton PC permet… ¦ De retrouver tes fichiers dans l'Explorateur, synchronisés avec le cloud": {"q":"Syncing OneDrive on your PC lets you…","e":"You work as in a regular folder, and every change is sent to OneDrive automatically.","a":["Find your files in File Explorer, synchronized with the cloud","Back up your entire PC, including system and applications","Speed up your Internet connection (the cloud pushes from behind)"]},
  "Un fichier OneDrive « disponible à la demande » (icône nuage)… ¦ Est visible, mais n'est téléchargé qu'à l'ouverture": {"q":"A OneDrive file that is “available on demand” (cloud icon)…","e":"You see all your files without them taking up disk space. They download when you open them.","a":["Is visible, but is only downloaded when opened","Is on your PC, but not yet uploaded to the cloud","Is downloaded and available even without a connection"]},
  "Le lien de partage « Personnes de ton organisation »… ¦ Fonctionne pour tous les collègues qui ont le lien": {"q":"The “People in your organization” sharing link…","e":"Handy internally, but any colleague who receives the forwarded link can open the file. Guests, however, don't have access. For sensitive content: “Specific people”.","a":["Works for all colleagues who have the link","Works for colleagues and guests of the tenant","Works only for the colleagues you named"]},
  "Ajouter une date d'expiration à un lien de partage permet… ¦ De couper l'accès au lien automatiquement après cette date": {"q":"Adding an expiration date to a sharing link makes it possible to…","e":"Ideal for one-off sharing with an external person: no need to remember to remove access.","a":["Cut off access through the link automatically after that date","Delete the shared file on that date","Send the recipient a reminder before that date"]},
  "Tu as supprimé par erreur un fichier d'un site SharePoint. Tu regardes d'abord… ¦ Dans la corbeille du site SharePoint": {"q":"You accidentally deleted a file from a SharePoint site. You first look…","e":"The site recycle bin keeps deleted items. If they have been emptied from there, an admin can still look in the second-stage recycle bin.","a":["In the SharePoint site recycle bin","In your OneDrive recycle bin","In the file's version history"]},
  "Quelles sont de bonnes pratiques pour nommer ses fichiers ? ¦ Un nom explicite (projet, objet)": {"q":"Which are good practices for naming files?","e":"Clear name, sortable date (with DD-MM-YYYY, files sort by day rather than by date), versions managed by OneDrive/SharePoint.","a":["An explicit name (project, subject)","The date in YYYY-MM-DD format for easy sorting","Relying on version history rather than “v2, final, final2”","The date in DD-MM-YYYY format for easy reading"]},
  "Tous tes fichiers OneDrive ont été abîmés (ransomware, erreur de masse). Tu peux… ¦ Restaurer ton OneDrive à une date antérieure, dans les 30 derniers jours": {"q":"All your OneDrive files have been damaged (ransomware, mass error). You can…","e":"The “Restore your OneDrive” feature rolls the whole space back to an earlier state, within the limit of the last 30 days. The recycle bin only contains deleted files, not encrypted or modified ones.","a":["Restore your OneDrive to an earlier date, within the last 30 days","Restore your OneDrive to an earlier date, up to 1 year back","Retrieve the healthy versions from your OneDrive recycle bin"]},
  "Donner des droits différents à une seule bibliothèque SharePoint, c'est… ¦ Casser l'héritage des autorisations, à faire avec parcimonie": {"q":"Giving different permissions to a single SharePoint library means…","e":"It's possible, but multiplying exceptions makes permissions unreadable. It's better to structure sites and groups.","a":["Breaking permission inheritance, to be done sparingly","Modifying the site Members group, the only possible option","Applying a Conditional Access policy to the library"]},
  "Site de communication ou site d'équipe SharePoint ? ¦ Communication pour diffuser largement (intranet), équipe pour collaborer": {"q":"SharePoint communication site or team site?","e":"The team site is linked to a Microsoft 365 group (and often to a Teams team). The communication site is used to publish: news, procedures, HR pages…","a":["Communication to broadcast widely (intranet), team to collaborate","Team to broadcast widely (intranet), communication to collaborate","Communication for external users, team reserved for internal users"]},
  "Les fichiers d'un canal privé Teams sont stockés dans le même site SharePoint que les autres canaux. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Files in a Teams private channel are stored in the same SharePoint site as the other channels.","e":"False: each private (and shared) channel has its own SharePoint site, so that only its members have access."},
  "Deux flèches bleues qui tournent sur l'icône OneDrive, ça veut dire… ¦ Synchronisation en cours": {"q":"Two blue arrows spinning on the OneDrive icon mean…","e":"The arrows indicate that OneDrive is uploading or downloading changes. A green check mark means everything is up to date.","a":["Sync in progress","File available offline","OneDrive going for a jog"]},
  "Une croix rouge sur un fichier OneDrive signale… ¦ Un fichier uniquement disponible en ligne": {"q":"A red cross on a OneDrive file indicates…","e":"Name too long, forbidden character, file open elsewhere, storage full… Clicking the OneDrive icon shows the cause.","a":["A file only available online","A sync problem","A file deleted from the cloud, still on the PC"]},
  "L'option « Toujours conserver sur cet appareil » dans OneDrive… ¦ Télécharge le fichier pour qu'il soit disponible même hors connexion": {"q":"The “Always keep on this device” option in OneDrive…","e":"Handy before a trip without a network. “Free up space” does the opposite: the file goes back to available on demand.","a":["Downloads the file so it's available even offline","Prevents it from being deleted by colleagues who have access to it","Downloads it to all your devices connected to OneDrive"]},
  "« Extraire » (check-out) un document dans SharePoint sert à… ¦ Le déplacer de la bibliothèque vers ton OneDrive": {"q":"“Check out” a document in SharePoint is used to…","e":"The document is reserved until it is checked in. With co-authoring, it's needed less, but it's useful for tightly controlled documents.","a":["Move it from the library to your OneDrive","Prevent others from editing it while you work on it","Publish a major version visible to all readers"]},
  "Dans une bibliothèque SharePoint, les colonnes de métadonnées permettent… ¦ De classer et filtrer les documents sans empiler les sous-dossiers": {"q":"In a SharePoint library, metadata columns make it possible to…","e":"Client, year, status… You filter in one click instead of digging through a ten-level folder tree.","a":["Sort and filter documents without piling up subfolders","Encrypt documents according to their confidentiality level","Block the upload of certain file types (.exe, .zip)"]},
  "Supprimer un fichier synchronisé dans l'Explorateur le supprime aussi dans OneDrive en ligne. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Deleting a file synced in File Explorer also deletes it in OneDrive online.","e":"True: sync works both ways. It goes to the OneDrive recycle bin, from where it can still be restored."},
  "Pour retrouver une bibliothèque d'équipe directement dans l'Explorateur de fichiers, sans la synchroniser à part : ¦ « Ajouter un raccourci à Mon OneDrive »": {"q":"To find a team library directly in File Explorer, without syncing it separately:","e":"The shortcut appears in your OneDrive and syncs with it, on all your devices.","a":["“Add shortcut to My files”","“Pin to top” the library on the site","“Follow” the site from the SharePoint page"]},
  "Quel est l'espace OneDrive généralement inclus par utilisateur dans les offres Microsoft 365 professionnelles ? ¦ 5 Go": {"q":"How much OneDrive storage is generally included per user in business Microsoft 365 plans?","e":"Most business subscriptions include 1 TB per user. The administrator can adjust this quota.","a":["5 GB","1 TB","Unlimited"]},
  "Par défaut, combien de temps un élément supprimé reste-t-il récupérable dans les corbeilles SharePoint (premier et second niveau) ? ¦ 30 jours au total": {"q":"By default, how long does a deleted item remain recoverable in the SharePoint recycle bins (first and second stage)?","e":"93 days from the original deletion, site recycle bin then site collection recycle bin. After that, only a Purview retention policy or a backup lets you recover it.","a":["30 days in total","93 days in total","180 days in total"]},
  "Pour interdire les liens « Toute personne disposant du lien » sur l'ensemble du tenant, on règle… ¦ Le partage externe au niveau de l'organisation, dans le Centre d'administration SharePoint": {"q":"To forbid “Anyone with the link” links across the whole tenant, you configure…","e":"The organization-level sharing setting in SharePoint sets the ceiling: no site can be more permissive. Teams guest access and Entra external collaboration don't manage anonymous links.","a":["External sharing at the organization level, in the SharePoint admin center","Guest access at the organization level, in the Teams admin center","External collaboration settings, in the Microsoft Entra admin center"]},
  "Pour retrouver tous les fichiers que des collègues ont partagés avec toi, tu ouvres… ¦ La section « Récents »": {"q":"To find all the files that colleagues have shared with you, you open…","e":"The “Shared” view lists what others have shared with you (and what you have shared). “Recent” only shows recently opened files.","a":["The “Recent” section","The OneDrive “Shared” view","The OneDrive recycle bin"]},
  "Tu veux savoir qui a accès à un fichier OneDrive et retirer un lien de partage oublié. Tu utilises… ¦ « Gérer l'accès » sur le fichier": {"q":"You want to know who has access to a OneDrive file and remove a forgotten sharing link. You use…","e":"“Manage access” shows the people and links that give access to the file, and lets you delete a link or remove someone in one click.","a":["“Manage access” on the file","“Properties” in Windows Explorer","Version history"]},
  "Un projet est terminé : quelle commande SharePoint Online Management Shell passe son site en lecture seule ? ¦ Set-SPOSite -Identity $url -Status Archived": {"q":"A project is finished: which SharePoint Online Management Shell command sets its site to read-only?","e":"The -LockState parameter accepts Unlock, ReadOnly or NoAccess. ReadOnly keeps the content viewable but blocks any modification; SharingCapability only controls external sharing.","a":["Set-SPOSite -Identity $url -Status Archived","Set-SPOSite -Identity $url -SharingCapability Disabled","Set-SPOSite -Identity $url -LockState ReadOnly"]},
  "Tu veux qu'un collègue puisse lire ton document sans pouvoir le modifier. Dans la fenêtre de partage, tu choisis… ¦ Peut modifier": {"q":"You want a colleague to be able to read your document without being able to edit it. In the sharing window, you choose…","e":"“Can view” gives read-only access. “Can edit” allows changes, while “Owner” and “Member” are site or group roles, not options of a sharing link.","a":["Can edit","Can view","Owner","Member"]},
  "Tu peux ouvrir et modifier un fichier Word stocké dans OneDrive directement depuis ton navigateur, même sans avoir Office installé sur le PC. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"You can open and edit a Word file stored in OneDrive directly from your browser, even without Office installed on the PC.","e":"True: the Office for the web apps (Word, Excel, PowerPoint online) open in the browser from OneDrive or SharePoint, without installation."},
  "Un fichier de ton OneDrive doit rejoindre la bibliothèque du site SharePoint de ton équipe. Quelle commande utilises-tu ? ¦ Renommer": {"q":"A file in your OneDrive must join the document library of your team's SharePoint site. Which command do you use?","e":"“Move to” (or “Copy to”) sends the file to another Microsoft 365 location, such as a team site's library. Download only copies it to your PC.","a":["Rename","Download","Move to","Embed"]},
  "Tu supprimes le compte d'un utilisateur parti de l'entreprise. Que devient son OneDrive par défaut ? ¦ Il est conservé 93 jours dans la corbeille, sans accès possible": {"q":"You delete the account of a user who has left the company. What happens to their OneDrive by default?","e":"The default retention of an orphaned OneDrive is 30 days (configurable in the SharePoint admin center), and access can be delegated automatically to the manager defined in Entra ID. After that period, the OneDrive goes to the site recycle bin.","a":["It is kept for 93 days in the recycle bin, with no access possible","It is converted into a team SharePoint site attached to the manager","It is moved to the global administrator's OneDrive","It is kept for 30 days, and their manager can be given access to it"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet ouvre la session SharePoint Online Management Shell vers l'URL d'administration du tenant (https://contoso-admin.sharepoint.com) ? ¦ Connect-SPOService": {"q":"Which cmdlet opens the SharePoint Online Management Shell session to the tenant's admin URL (https://contoso-admin.sharepoint.com)?","e":"Connect-SPOService -Url https://<tenant>-admin.sharepoint.com is the first command to run before any *-SPO* cmdlet.","placeholder":"Cmdlet name","answers":["Connect-SPOService","Connect-SPOService -Url"]},
  "Quels groupes SharePoint sont créés par défaut sur un site d'équipe ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Propriétaires de <site>": {"q":"Which SharePoint groups are created by default on a team site? (several answers)","e":"Each site has the Owners (full control), Members (edit) and Visitors (read) groups. There is no “Guests” group by default: guests are added to one of these groups.","a":["Owners of <site>","Members of <site>","Guests of <site>","Visitors of <site>"]},
  "Sur un site d'équipe connecté à un groupe Microsoft 365, ajouter quelqu'un comme membre du groupe lui donne… ¦ un accès en modification, via le groupe Membres du site": {"q":"On a team site connected to a Microsoft 365 group, adding someone as a group member gives them…","e":"Microsoft 365 group members inherit the SharePoint Members group (edit), and group owners inherit the Owners group. Managing group membership is the best practice.","a":["edit access, via the site Members group","read-only access, via the site Visitors group","full control, via the site Owners group","no access until an owner adds them to the site"]},
  "Le Centre d'administration SharePoint permet de n'autoriser la synchronisation OneDrive que sur les PC joints à des domaines précis. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"The SharePoint admin center lets you allow OneDrive sync only on PCs joined to specific domains.","e":"True: under Settings > Sync, the option “Allow syncing only on computers joined to specific domains” expects the GUID of the Active Directory domain."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre les étapes pour restaurer un site SharePoint supprimé par erreur : ¦ Ouvrir le Centre d'administration SharePoint": {"q":"Put the steps in order to restore a SharePoint site deleted by mistake:","e":"Deleted sites remain for 93 days in “Deleted sites”, from where the administrator can restore them with their content and permissions.","items":["Open the SharePoint admin center","Go to Sites > Deleted sites","Select the site concerned","Click Restore"]},
  "Quelle fonctionnalité OneDrive redirige automatiquement Bureau, Documents et Images vers OneDrive, et peut être imposée par stratégie de groupe ou Intune ? ¦ Fichiers à la demande": {"q":"Which OneDrive feature automatically redirects Desktop, Documents and Pictures to OneDrive, and can be enforced by Group Policy or Intune?","e":"Known Folder Move protects these Windows folders in OneDrive. Files On-Demand handles downloading, and Personal Vault is a folder protected by stronger authentication.","a":["Files On-Demand","Known Folder Move","Personal Vault","Differential sync"]},
  "Comment est calculé le stockage SharePoint mutualisé d'un tenant Microsoft 365 entreprise ? ¦ 1 To par utilisateur licencié, partagé entre tous les sites": {"q":"How is the pooled SharePoint storage of a Microsoft 365 enterprise tenant calculated?","e":"The tenant receives a base 1 TB plus 10 GB per eligible license. This SharePoint storage is separate from the OneDrive storage assigned to each user.","a":["1 TB per licensed user, shared across all sites","25 GB per site, regardless of the tenant size","1 TB + 10 GB per eligible license","10 GB + 1 TB per eligible license"]},
  "Quel paramètre de Set-SPOTenant change le type de lien proposé par défaut quand un utilisateur clique sur « Partager » ? ¦ -SharingCapability": {"q":"Which Set-SPOTenant parameter changes the default link type offered when a user clicks “Share”?","e":"-DefaultSharingLinkType (None, Direct, Internal, AnonymousAccess) sets the default link type. -DefaultLinkPermission only sets the default permission (view or edit), -SharingCapability the allowed sharing level.","a":["-SharingCapability","-DefaultLinkPermission","-DefaultSharingLinkType","-FileAnonymousLinkType"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet SharePoint Online Management Shell restaure un site encore présent dans la corbeille des sites ? ¦ Restore-SPODeletedSite": {"q":"Which SharePoint Online Management Shell cmdlet restores a site that is still in the deleted sites recycle bin?","e":"Restore-SPODeletedSite -Identity <URL> restores the deleted site. Get-SPODeletedSite lists recoverable sites, Remove-SPODeletedSite permanently purges them.","placeholder":"Cmdlet name","answers":["Restore-SPODeletedSite"]},
  "Tu veux que tous les liens « Toute personne disposant du lien » expirent automatiquement après 30 jours. Quel paramètre de Set-SPOTenant utilises-tu ? ¦ -ExternalUserExpireInDays": {"q":"You want all “Anyone with the link” links to expire automatically after 30 days. Which Set-SPOTenant parameter do you use?","e":"-RequireAnonymousLinksExpireInDays enforces an expiration on anonymous links. -ExternalUserExpireInDays concerns the expiration of guest access, -EmailAttestationReAuthDays the code re-verification of external users.","a":["-ExternalUserExpireInDays","-RequireAnonymousLinksExpireInDays","-EmailAttestationReAuthDays","-AnonymousLinkExpirationDays"]},
  "Avec Set-SPOSite -SharingCapability, tu ne peux pas rendre un site plus permissif que le niveau de partage défini au niveau du tenant. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"With Set-SPOSite -SharingCapability, you cannot make a site more permissive than the sharing level set at the tenant level.","e":"True: the tenant setting is a ceiling. A site can be more restrictive than the organization, never more open."},
  "Quelles valeurs sont valides pour le paramètre -SharingCapability de Set-SPOTenant ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ ExistingExternalUserSharingOnly": {"q":"Which values are valid for the -SharingCapability parameter of Set-SPOTenant? (several answers)","e":"The valid values are Disabled, ExistingExternalUserSharingOnly, ExternalUserSharingOnly and ExternalUserAndGuestSharing (the latter allows anonymous links). AnonymousLinkSharing and OrganizationOnly do not exist: internal-only sharing corresponds to Disabled.","a":["ExistingExternalUserSharingOnly","AnonymousLinkSharing","ExternalUserAndGuestSharing","OrganizationOnly"]},
  "Pour que les appareils non gérés n'aient qu'un accès web limité (sans téléchargement ni synchronisation) à SharePoint et OneDrive, quelle valeur donnes-tu à Set-SPOTenant -ConditionalAccessPolicy ? ¦ AllowFullAccess": {"q":"For unmanaged devices to have only limited web access (no download or sync) to SharePoint and OneDrive, which value do you give to Set-SPOTenant -ConditionalAccessPolicy?","e":"AllowLimitedAccess enables limited web access, enforced via a Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access policy. BlockAccess blocks entirely, and WebOnlyAccess is not an existing value.","a":["AllowFullAccess","BlockAccess","WebOnlyAccess","AllowLimitedAccess"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la mise en place d'un site hub et le rattachement d'un premier site : ¦ Connect-SPOService -Url https://contoso-admin.sharepoint.com": {"q":"Put in order the setup of a hub site and the association of a first site:","e":"You connect, create the communication site (template SITEPAGEPUBLISHING#0, with a mandatory storage quota), register it as a hub with Register-SPOHubSite, and only then associate sites with it using Add-SPOHubSiteAssociation.","items":["Connect-SPOService -Url https://contoso-admin.sharepoint.com","New-SPOSite -Url <URL du hub> -Template SITEPAGEPUBLISHING#0 -Owner <UPN> -StorageQuota 1024 -Title \"Hub\"","Register-SPOHubSite -Site <URL du hub>","Add-SPOHubSiteAssociation -Site <URL du site> -HubSite <URL du hub>"]},
  "Pour que SharePoint et OneDrive traitent le contenu des fichiers Office chiffrés par une étiquette de confidentialité (coédition, recherche, eDiscovery), tu actives… ¦ Set-SPOTenant -EnableAIPIntegration $true": {"q":"For SharePoint and OneDrive to process the content of Office files encrypted by a sensitivity label (co-authoring, search, eDiscovery), you enable…","e":"-EnableAIPIntegration enables sensitivity label support for Office files in SharePoint and OneDrive. EnableMIPLabels is for container labels (groups, sites), and the PDF parameter only concerns PDFs.","a":["Set-SPOTenant -EnableAIPIntegration $true","Set-SPOTenant -EnableSensitivityLabelforPDF $true","EnableMIPLabels in the Entra ID group settings","Set-SPOSite -SensitivityLabel on each site"]},
  "Pour supprimer en masse les anciennes versions déjà existantes des fichiers d'un site et récupérer du stockage, tu utilises… ¦ Set-SPOSite -MajorVersionLimit 100": {"q":"To bulk-delete the existing old versions of a site's files and reclaim storage, you use…","e":"New-SPOSiteFileVersionBatchDeleteJob starts a job that deletes existing versions. The version limit parameters of Set-SPOSite apply to future versions and do not purge the history already stored.","a":["Set-SPOSite -MajorVersionLimit 100","New-SPOSiteFileVersionBatchDeleteJob","Set-SPOSite -EnableAutoExpirationVersionTrim $true","Remove-SPOFileVersion -All"]},
  "Quel paramètre de Set-SPOTenant allonge la durée de conservation du OneDrive d'un utilisateur supprimé ? ¦ -OrphanedPersonalSitesRetentionPeriod": {"q":"Which Set-SPOTenant parameter extends how long a deleted user's OneDrive is retained?","e":"-OrphanedPersonalSitesRetentionPeriod (in days, from 30 to 3650) sets how long a deleted user's OneDrive is kept. It matches the retention setting in the SharePoint admin center. -OneDriveRequestFilesLinkExpirationInDays concerns “Request files” links.","a":["-OrphanedPersonalSitesRetentionPeriod","-OneDriveRequestFilesLinkExpirationInDays","-DeletedPersonalSitesRetentionDays","-DeletedUserPersonalSiteRetention"]},
  "Un PC portable géré par Intune est volé. Que peut faire l'admin ? ¦ Retirer sa licence Intune pour couper la gestion": {"q":"A laptop managed by Intune is stolen. What can the admin do?","e":"Intune lets you lock, reset or wipe the device remotely as soon as it reconnects. Deleting the device object or the license wipes nothing on the disk. You also revoke the user's sessions.","a":["Remove its Intune license to cut off management","Delete the device from the list in Entra ID","Launch a remote wipe from Intune"]},
  "Intune sert principalement à… ¦ Gérer et sécuriser les appareils (configuration, applications, conformité)": {"q":"Intune is mainly used to…","e":"Intune deploys settings, apps and security rules to PCs, smartphones and tablets, even away from the office.","a":["Manage and secure devices (configuration, applications, compliance)","Manage identities and users' Conditional Access","Protect mailboxes against phishing and malware"]},
  "Combiner la conformité Intune et l'accès conditionnel permet… ¦ De bloquer l'accès depuis un appareil non conforme (non chiffré, pas à jour…)": {"q":"Combining Intune compliance and Conditional Access makes it possible to…","e":"Only devices that meet the security rules can access company data.","a":["Block access from a non-compliant device (unencrypted, not up to date…)","Install missing patches on the device (Windows Update, drivers…)","Remotely wipe a device that connects from abroad"]},
  "« BYOD » signifie… ¦ Apporter son propre appareil (Bring Your Own Device)": {"q":"“BYOD” stands for…","e":"Using your personal phone for work. Intune then protects business data without taking control of the whole device.","a":["Bring Your Own Device","Bring Your Own Donuts","Backup Your Office Data"]},
  "Windows Autopilot permet… ¦ De préparer un PC neuf automatiquement dès la première connexion de l'utilisateur": {"q":"Windows Autopilot makes it possible to…","e":"The PC is delivered straight to the user, who signs in with their work account: settings, apps and security rules install themselves, with no master image to maintain.","a":["Set up a new PC automatically as soon as the user first signs in","Fly the drone that delivers the PC to the user","Reinstall existing PCs from a master image (imaging)"]},
  "Endpoint Privilege Management (EPM) d'Intune permet… ¦ D'autoriser un utilisateur standard à lancer une appli précise avec élévation, sans être admin local": {"q":"Intune's Endpoint Privilege Management (EPM) makes it possible to…","e":"With EPM, the user stays a standard user: elevation rules (automatic, user-confirmed or subject to support approval) allow only the intended apps. Remote control is the job of Remote Help.","a":["Let a standard user run a specific app with elevation, without being a local admin","Temporarily give local admin rights to all members of a group","Take remote control of a user's PC to assist them"]},
  "Une stratégie de conformité Intune définit… ¦ Les exigences qu'un appareil doit respecter (chiffrement, version d'OS…)": {"q":"An Intune compliance policy defines…","e":"A non-compliant device can then be blocked by Conditional Access until it is fixed. Pushing settings is the role of configuration profiles.","a":["The requirements a device must meet (encryption, OS version…)","The settings to push to the device (Wi-Fi, VPN, wallpaper…)","The applications to install automatically (Teams, Outlook…)"]},
  "BitLocker, c'est… ¦ Le chiffrement de disque de Windows": {"q":"BitLocker is…","e":"A stolen PC stays unreadable. With Intune, the recovery key is backed up in Entra ID for support.","a":["Windows disk encryption","The antivirus built into Windows","The Windows session lock"]},
  "L'application « Portail d'entreprise » sert à l'utilisateur pour… ¦ Inscrire son appareil et installer les applications mises à disposition par l'entreprise": {"q":"The “Company Portal” app is used by the user to…","e":"It's the company's “app store”, and the place where you can see whether your device is compliant.","a":["Enroll their device and install the applications made available by the company","Reset their password and manage their authentication methods","Access SharePoint sites and the company intranet"]},
  "Un salarié quitte l'entreprise avec son téléphone personnel. Quelle action Intune choisir ? ¦ L'effacement complet de l'appareil (retour aux paramètres d'usine)": {"q":"An employee leaves the company with their personal phone. Which Intune action should you choose?","e":"Retire (selective wipe) respects privacy: personal photos and apps stay, work data disappears.","a":["Full device wipe (factory reset)","Retire, which removes only company data and apps","Remote lock, until they return the phone"]},
  "Dans Intune, les « anneaux de mise à jour » Windows permettent… ¦ De déployer les mises à jour par vagues (groupe pilote, puis tout le monde)": {"q":"In Intune, Windows “update rings” make it possible to…","e":"A test group receives updates first: if a problem appears, you pause before it affects the whole company. Targeting a specific version is the role of feature update policies.","a":["Deploy updates in waves (pilot group, then everyone)","Choose the WSUS server from which each PC downloads its updates","Enforce a specific Windows version (e.g. 24H2) on all PCs"]},
  "Les stratégies de protection des applications Intune (MAM) permettent… ¦ D'effacer entièrement le téléphone perso au départ du salarié": {"q":"Intune app protection policies (MAM) make it possible to…","e":"Ideal for BYOD: you protect Outlook, Teams or OneDrive (PIN, encryption, copy-paste blocked to a personal app, selective wipe) without taking control of the personal phone.","a":["Fully wipe the personal phone when the employee leaves","Protect work data at the app level, even without enrolling the device","Enforce encryption and a passcode on the whole device, once enrolled"]},
  "Quand tu inscris ton téléphone personnel dans Intune, l'entreprise peut lire tes SMS et voir tes photos. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"When you enroll your personal phone in Intune, the company can read your text messages and see your photos.","e":"False: on a personal device, Intune sees neither text messages, nor photos, nor browsing history. It checks compliance (passcode, OS version) and manages work apps and data."},
  "Pour inscrire soi-même un PC Windows dans Intune avec son compte professionnel, on passe par… ¦ Paramètres > Comptes > Vos informations > Se connecter avec un compte Microsoft": {"q":"To enroll a Windows PC in Intune yourself with your work account, you go through…","e":"“Access work or school” > “Connect” links the PC to the organization and enrolls it in Intune if automatic enrollment is configured. “Your info” adds a personal account, and “Domain” joins the on-premises AD. For a new fleet, Autopilot is preferred.","a":["Settings > Accounts > Your info > Sign in with a Microsoft account instead","Settings > Accounts > Access work or school","Control Panel > System > Computer Name > Domain"]},
  "Pour déployer une application Win32 (installateur .exe) avec Intune, il faut d'abord la convertir au format… ¦ .msixbundle": {"q":"To deploy a Win32 app (.exe installer) with Intune, you must first convert it to the format…","e":"The Microsoft Win32 Content Prep Tool (IntuneWinAppUtil.exe) packages the installer and its files as .intunewin. You then define the install command and a detection rule. .intunemac was the former format for macOS apps, and MSIX is not used to package an .exe.","a":[".msixbundle",".intunemac",".intunewin"]},
  "Déployer un PC neuf avec Windows Autopilot : remets les étapes dans l'ordre. ¦ Récupérer le hash matériel du PC (ou le faire enregistrer par le revendeur)": {"q":"Deploying a new PC with Windows Autopilot: put the steps in order.","e":"Without the imported hash, the PC doesn't know it belongs to the organization. Without an assigned profile, it starts like a consumer PC. After that, everything happens with no technician intervention.","items":["Get the PC's hardware hash (or have the reseller register it)","Import the device into Intune (Windows devices > Enrollment > Windows Autopilot)","Assign an Autopilot deployment profile to the group containing the device","The user turns on the PC and signs in with their work account","The PC joins Entra ID, enrolls in Intune and receives apps and policies"]},
  "Le Portail d'entreprise indique que ton téléphone est « non conforme ». Quelle est la cause la plus probable ? ¦ Ton forfait mobile n'est pas un forfait pro": {"q":"The Company Portal says your phone is “not compliant”. What is the most likely cause?","e":"Compliance checks security rules set by the company: lock code, OS version, encryption… The mobile plan or the Wi-Fi network used don't come into play.","a":["Your mobile plan is not a business plan","Your phone is connected to your personal home router's Wi-Fi","Your phone doesn't have the required lock code","You installed too many personal apps"]},
  "Tu as perdu ton téléphone sur lequel tu consultes tes mails pro. Quel est le bon réflexe ? ¦ Prévenir tout de suite le support informatique": {"q":"You lost the phone on which you check your work email. What is the right reflex?","e":"The sooner support is told, the sooner it can lock the device or remotely wipe company data with Intune.","a":["Tell IT support right away","Wait a few days for it to turn up","Change your Teams background so you go unnoticed","Uninstall Outlook from your PC to cut off access"]},
  "Si ton appareil est non conforme, l'entreprise peut te bloquer l'accès à ta messagerie professionnelle tant que le problème n'est pas corrigé. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"If your device is non-compliant, the company can block your access to your work email until the problem is fixed.","e":"Thanks to Conditional Access, the company can require a compliant device to access Outlook, Teams or SharePoint. Once the problem is fixed, access comes back."},
  "« Inscrire » son appareil dans Intune, ça veut dire… ¦ Le faire réparer gratuitement par le service informatique": {"q":"“Enrolling” your device in Intune means…","e":"Enrollment links the device to Intune: the company can then apply security rules to it and provide it with work apps.","a":["Having IT fix it for free","Declaring it to the company so that it can manage it","Registering your warranty with the manufacturer through the company","Connecting it to the company Wi-Fi with your work account"]},
  "Quels éléments peuvent rendre ton téléphone non conforme ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Un système (Android ou iOS) trop ancien, pas mis à jour": {"q":"Which items can make your phone non-compliant? (several answers)","e":"Compliance rules cover security: OS version, lock code, unlocked device… Customizing your screen has no impact.","a":["An operating system (Android or iOS) that is too old and not updated","A wallpaper with a photo of your cat","No lock code configured","A “jailbroken” or “rooted” phone"]},
  "Tu viens d'ajouter un code de verrouillage sur ton téléphone, mais le Portail d'entreprise affiche toujours « non conforme ». Que fais-tu ? ¦ Tu désinstalles le Portail d'entreprise": {"q":"You just added a lock code to your phone, but the Company Portal still shows “not compliant”. What do you do?","e":"The compliance status isn't updated instantly: rerunning the check from the Company Portal forces a new evaluation. Resetting the phone is pointless.","a":["You uninstall the Company Portal","You reset your phone to factory settings","You change your work account password","You rerun the check from the Company Portal"]},
  "Que signifie le sigle « MDM » qu'on croise souvent avec Intune ? ¦ Mobile Device Management (gestion des appareils mobiles)": {"q":"What does the acronym “MDM”, often seen alongside Intune, stand for?","e":"MDM = Mobile Device Management: the organization's management of devices (PCs, phones, tablets). Intune is Microsoft's MDM solution.","a":["Mobile Device Management","Microsoft Data Monitoring","Multi-Device Messaging","Managed Domain Membership"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre l'inscription de ton téléphone Android personnel : ¦ Installer l'application Portail d'entreprise depuis le Google Play Store": {"q":"Put the enrollment of your personal Android phone in order:","e":"You first install the Company Portal, sign in with your work account, then the wizard creates a separate space (work profile). Once the device is deemed compliant, the work apps can be used.","items":["Install the Company Portal app from the Google Play Store","Sign in with your work account","Follow the wizard that creates the work profile","Wait for the device compliance to be checked","Use your work apps in the work profile"]},
  "Quel est le nom de l'application Microsoft à installer pour inscrire ton téléphone dans Intune ? ¦ Portail d'entreprise": {"q":"What is the name of the Microsoft app to install to enroll your phone in Intune?","e":"The Company Portal is used to enroll the device, check its compliance and install the apps made available by the company.","placeholder":"App name","answers":["Portail d'entreprise","Company Portal","Portail d entreprise","Intune Portail d'entreprise","Intune Company Portal","company portal","intune company portal"]},
  "Sur un téléphone Android personnel avec un profil professionnel, les applis pro se reconnaissent à la petite mallette affichée sur leur icône. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"On a personal Android phone with a work profile, work apps can be recognized by the small briefcase shown on their icon.","e":"The Android work profile separates work apps from personal apps; work apps carry a briefcase-shaped badge."},
  "Tu essaies de copier un passage d'un mail Outlook pro pour le coller dans ton appli de notes personnelle, et c'est refusé. Pourquoi ? ¦ Le presse-papiers de ton téléphone est saturé et doit être vidé": {"q":"You try to copy a passage from a work Outlook email to paste it into your personal notes app, and it's refused. Why?","e":"Intune app protection policies (MAM) can block copy-paste of work data to unmanaged apps, to prevent leaks.","a":["Your phone's clipboard is full and needs to be emptied","An (Intune) app protection policy forbids it","Outlook mobile disables copy-paste in all emails","Your notes app rejects formatted text"]},
  "Un utilisateur ne trouve pas une application dans son Portail d'entreprise alors que ses collègues la voient. Cause la plus probable ? ¦ Son compte n'a pas le rôle Administrateur Intune requis": {"q":"A user can't find an app in their Company Portal while their colleagues can see it. Most likely cause?","e":"An app only appears in the Company Portal if it is assigned (as Available or Required) to a group that includes the user or their device. So you check group membership.","a":["Their account doesn't have the required Intune Administrator role","They must first download it from the publisher's website","The app isn't assigned as “Available” to one of their groups","The Company Portal only displays Microsoft apps"]},
  "Une application affectée en « Requis » dans Intune s'installe automatiquement sur l'appareil, sans que l'utilisateur ait besoin de passer par le Portail d'entreprise. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"An app assigned as “Required” in Intune installs automatically on the device, without the user needing to go through the Company Portal.","e":"“Required” forces installation; “Available for enrolled devices” lets the user install it on demand from the Company Portal."},
  "Sur un PC Windows géré, où l'utilisateur peut-il forcer lui-même une synchronisation avec Intune ? ¦ Panneau de configuration > Centre de synchronisation > Synchroniser": {"q":"On a managed Windows PC, where can the user force a sync with Intune themselves?","e":"In Access work or school, the Sync button (via Info) triggers an immediate check of policies and apps. On the admin side, the “Sync” action also exists in the Intune admin center.","a":["Control Panel > Sync Center > Sync","Settings > Accounts > Access work or school > account > Info > Sync","Settings > Windows Update > Advanced options > Sync policies","Settings > Accounts > Sync your settings > Sync now"]},
  "Quels contrôles peut contenir une stratégie de conformité Intune pour Windows ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Une version minimale du système d'exploitation": {"q":"Which checks can an Intune compliance policy for Windows contain? (several answers)","e":"Compliance checks the device's security state (OS version, encryption, password…). Intune does not collect browsing history.","a":["A minimum operating system version","The user's browsing history","BitLocker encryption required","A password required to unlock the device"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre le dépannage d'un appareil signalé non conforme : ¦ Ouvrir l'appareil dans le centre d'administration Intune": {"q":"Put the troubleshooting of a device reported as non-compliant in order:","e":"You start from the device's page, drill down to the faulty setting, fix it, then sync so that compliance is reevaluated.","items":["Open the device in the Intune admin center","Review its compliance status by policy","Identify the failing setting","Fix the problem on the device","Sync the device and check the new status"]},
  "Quelle est l'adresse web (sans https://) du centre d'administration Microsoft Intune ? ¦ intune.microsoft.com": {"q":"What is the web address (without https://) of the Microsoft Intune admin center?","e":"The Intune admin center is at intune.microsoft.com; the old address endpoint.microsoft.com redirects to it.","placeholder":"example.microsoft.com","answers":["intune.microsoft.com","https://intune.microsoft.com","endpoint.microsoft.com"]},
  "Dans les « Actions en cas de non-conformité » d'une stratégie, laquelle permet de prévenir l'utilisateur avant qu'il perde l'accès ? ¦ Mettre l'appareil hors service": {"q":"Among a policy's “Actions for noncompliance”, which one lets you warn the user before they lose access?","e":"“Send email to end user” uses a notification template. Combined with a grace period before marking the device as noncompliant, it gives time to fix the problem.","a":["Retire the noncompliant device","Reset the device","Remove the user from Microsoft Entra ID","Send email to end user"]},
  "Outlook peut exiger un code PIN à l'ouverture sur un iPhone personnel grâce à une stratégie de protection d'applications, même si ce téléphone n'est pas inscrit dans Intune. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Outlook can require a PIN on opening on a personal iPhone thanks to an app protection policy, even if that phone is not enrolled in Intune.","e":"App protection policies (MAM) apply to the app and the work account, with or without device enrollment: it's the classic BYOD scenario."},
  "Un utilisateur a égaré son téléphone pro mais pense le retrouver demain au bureau. Quelle action Intune est la plus adaptée pour l'instant ? ¦ Verrouillage à distance": {"q":"A user has misplaced their work phone but thinks they will find it tomorrow at the office. Which Intune action is the most appropriate for now?","e":"Remote lock protects the device without erasing anything. Wiping or retiring would delete data, which would be excessive if the device is probably just misplaced.","a":["Remote lock","Wipe","Retire","Delete the device from Intune"]},
  "Quel script PowerShell (PowerShell Gallery) est couramment utilisé pour récupérer le hachage matériel d'un PC afin de l'enregistrer dans Windows Autopilot ? ¦ Get-WindowsAutopilotInfo": {"q":"Which PowerShell script (PowerShell Gallery) is commonly used to retrieve a PC's hardware hash in order to register it in Windows Autopilot?","e":"Get-WindowsAutopilotInfo exports the hardware hash to a CSV to import into Intune (or sends it directly with the -Online parameter).","placeholder":"Script name","answers":["Get-WindowsAutopilotInfo","Get-WindowsAutopilotInfo.ps1"]},
  "À quoi servent les « filtres » d'affectation dans Intune ? ¦ À masquer des stratégies dans le centre d'administration": {"q":"What are assignment “filters” used for in Intune?","e":"A filter is added to a group assignment to include or exclude devices based on their properties (model, OS version, ownership…), for example only corporate devices or a specific model.","a":["To hide policies in the admin center","To refine an assignment based on device properties","To sort compliance reports by date or status","To filter the alerts sent to non-compliant devices"]},
  "Quel type de profil de configuration Intune permet de rechercher et configurer des milliers de paramètres Windows ou macOS précis par leur nom ? ¦ Modèles d'administration uniquement": {"q":"Which type of Intune configuration profile lets you search for and configure thousands of specific Windows or macOS settings by name?","e":"The settings catalog lists the available settings with search; it is the recommended type. OMA-URI is still possible but forces you to enter the CSP paths by hand.","a":["Administrative templates only","OMA-URI custom profile","Device restrictions","Settings catalog"]},
  "Une restriction de plateforme d'appareil dans Intune permet de bloquer l'inscription des appareils Android personnels tout en autorisant les appareils Android d'entreprise. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A device platform restriction in Intune can block enrollment of personal Android devices while allowing corporate Android devices.","e":"Platform restrictions let you, for each platform, allow or block enrollment and specifically block personal devices."},
  "Quels éléments sont nécessaires pour l'inscription automatique des PC Windows joints à Microsoft Entra dans Intune ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Un serveur WSUS local": {"q":"Which items are required for automatic enrollment of Microsoft Entra joined Windows PCs in Intune? (several answers)","e":"Automatic enrollment relies on Entra ID P1, an Intune license for the user and the MDM user scope (All or a group). WSUS has nothing to do with enrollment.","a":["An on-premises WSUS server","A license that includes Intune assigned to the user","Microsoft Entra ID P1 (or a plan that includes it)","An MDM user scope that includes the user"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la mise en place de l'inscription automatisée des appareils Apple (ADE) : ¦ Configurer le certificat push MDM Apple dans Intune": {"q":"Put the setup of Apple automated device enrollment (ADE) in order:","e":"Without an MDM push certificate, Intune can't manage any Apple device. You then establish the relationship with Apple Business Manager via the token, then create and assign the enrollment profile.","items":["Configure the Apple MDM push certificate in Intune","Download the public key from Intune and create the MDM server in Apple Business Manager","Import into Intune the token obtained from Apple Business Manager","Create an ADE enrollment profile","Assign the profile to the synced devices"]},
  "Les « Correctifs » (Remediations) d'Intune reposent sur… ¦ Deux scripts PowerShell planifiés : un de détection, un de correction": {"q":"Intune “Remediations” are based on…","e":"The detection script reports a problem through its exit code; the remediation script only runs in that case. Scheduling lets you recheck regularly.","a":["Two scheduled PowerShell scripts: one for detection, one for remediation","A single PowerShell script run at device startup","Packages .intunewin redeployed automatically on each failure","Compliance policies that repair the non-compliant device"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet Microsoft Graph PowerShell (v1.0) force la synchronisation d'un appareil géré par Intune ? ¦ Sync-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice": {"q":"Which Microsoft Graph PowerShell (v1.0) cmdlet forces the sync of an Intune-managed device?","e":"Sync-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice -ManagedDeviceId <id> sends the sync action, like the “Sync” button in the admin center.","placeholder":"Verb-Noun","answers":["Sync-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice","Sync-MgBetaDeviceManagementManagedDevice"]},
  "Avec Microsoft Graph PowerShell, quelle cmdlet liste les appareils gérés par Intune (et non les objets appareils de l'annuaire) ? ¦ Get-MgDevice": {"q":"With Microsoft Graph PowerShell, which cmdlet lists the devices managed by Intune (and not the directory's device objects)?","e":"Get-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice queries deviceManagement/managedDevices (Intune). Get-MgDevice returns Microsoft Entra device objects, which are not necessarily managed by Intune.","a":["Get-MgDevice","Get-MgUserOwnedDevice","Get-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice","Get-MgDirectoryDeviceLocalCredential"]},
  "Microsoft recommande de régler le paramètre « Marquer les appareils sans stratégie de conformité affectée comme » sur « Non conforme ». ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Microsoft recommends setting “Mark devices with no compliance policy assigned as” to “Not compliant”.","e":"Otherwise, a device with no policy assigned at all is considered compliant and passes Conditional Access. Setting it to Not compliant closes this gap."},
  "Quelle est la principale différence de la « préparation des appareils Windows Autopilot » (device preparation) par rapport au déploiement Autopilot classique ? ¦ Elle ne fonctionne que pour les appareils joints à un domaine local": {"q":"What is the main difference of Windows Autopilot device preparation compared with classic Autopilot deployment?","e":"With device preparation, the device is added during deployment to a device security group defined in the policy, with no prior registration of the hardware hash.","a":["It only works for devices joined to an on-premises domain","It requires importing the hardware hash via a signed CSV","It replaces Intune with Configuration Manager","It doesn't require registering the device's hardware hash beforehand"]},
  "Quelles conditions peut-on configurer dans le « lancement conditionnel » d'une stratégie de protection d'applications ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Blocage des appareils jailbreakés ou rootés": {"q":"Which conditions can be configured in the “conditional launch” of an app protection policy? (several answers)","e":"Conditional launch checks the device, the app and the account (jailbreak, app or OS version, offline period…). IP location falls under Entra Conditional Access named locations.","a":["Blocking jailbroken or rooted devices","Offline grace period","The user's public IP address","Minimum app version"]},
  "Dans Intune, où configure-t-on Windows LAPS (mot de passe de l'administrateur local) ? ¦ Profils de configuration > Restrictions d'appareil": {"q":"In Intune, where do you configure Windows LAPS (local administrator password)?","e":"Windows LAPS is configured via an account protection policy in Endpoint security; the device action “Rotate local admin password” then allows on-demand rotation.","a":["Configuration profiles > Device restrictions","Endpoint security > Account protection","Compliance > Compliance settings","Apps > App configuration policies"]},
  "En cogestion Configuration Manager / Intune, basculer la charge de travail « Stratégies de conformité » sur Intune signifie que… ¦ Configuration Manager et Intune évaluent la conformité en parallèle et on garde le pire résultat": {"q":"In Configuration Manager / Intune co-management, switching the “Compliance policies” workload to Intune means that…","e":"Each workload can be left with Configuration Manager, switched to “Pilot Intune” for a group, or handed over entirely to Intune, which then becomes its authority. The ConfigMgr client stays installed.","a":["Configuration Manager and Intune evaluate compliance in parallel and the worst result is kept","Devices are unenrolled from Configuration Manager","Intune becomes the authority for this workload on the targeted devices","Only Windows Server devices are evaluated by Intune"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre ce qui se passe pour un appareil qui échoue à une stratégie de conformité avec e-mail immédiat et délai de grâce : ¦ L'appareil s'enregistre et sa conformité est évaluée": {"q":"Put in order what happens to a device that fails a compliance policy configured with an immediate email and a grace period:","e":"During the grace period, the device is “in grace period” and is still treated as compliant by Conditional Access. Blocking only happens once the device is marked non-compliant.","items":["The device registers and its compliance is evaluated","A failing setting is detected","The user receives the notification email","The grace period expires and the device is marked non-compliant","Conditional Access blocks access to resources"]},
  "À quoi sert la « Page d'état d'inscription » (Enrollment Status Page) lors d'un déploiement Windows ? ¦ À empêcher l'utilisation de l'appareil tant que les applications et stratégies bloquantes ne sont pas installées": {"q":"What is the “Enrollment Status Page” used for during a Windows deployment?","e":"The Enrollment Status Page tracks the installation of apps and profiles during setup and can block access to the desktop until the required items are in place.","a":["To prevent use of the device until the blocking apps and policies are installed","To display the list of the user's enrolled devices in the Company Portal","To choose the language and keyboard during OOBE","To send an enrollment report by email to the manager"]},
  "Power Automate permet… ¦ D'automatiser des tâches entre applications (ex. enregistrer les pièces jointes dans SharePoint)": {"q":"Power Automate lets you…","e":"“Flows” start on their own: when an email arrives, every day at 9 a.m., when a file is added…","a":["Automate tasks between applications (e.g. save attachments to SharePoint)","Build business apps without coding (e.g. an equipment request)","Create interactive dashboards (e.g. sales tracking in Teams)"]},
  "Un flux Power Automate démarre grâce à… ¦ Un déclencheur (un mail reçu, une heure précise, un fichier ajouté…)": {"q":"A Power Automate flow starts thanks to…","e":"A trigger, then actions: “when a form is filled in, create a task in Planner and notify the team in Teams”.","a":["A trigger (a received email, a specific time, an added file…)","A connection, created for each service used (Outlook, Teams…)","An action placed at the start of the flow (send an email, create a file…)"]},
  "Power Apps permet… ¦ De créer des applications métier avec peu ou pas de code": {"q":"Power Apps lets you…","e":"An equipment request form, an inventory app on a phone… connected to SharePoint, Dataverse or other sources.","a":["Build business applications with little or no code","Create interactive reports and dashboards","Automate tasks between applications without intervention"]},
  "Un flux Power Automate « planifié » s'exécute… ¦ À heure fixe ou à intervalle régulier": {"q":"A “scheduled” Power Automate flow runs…","e":"Automated: on an event. Instant: on a click. Scheduled: on a timetable, for example every Monday at 8 a.m.","a":["At a fixed time or at regular intervals","Only when someone clicks a button","As soon as an event occurs, such as a received email"]},
  "Dans Power Automate, les connecteurs servent à… ¦ Relier le flux à des services comme Outlook, SharePoint, Teams ou Excel": {"q":"In Power Automate, connectors are used to…","e":"There are hundreds of connectors, from Microsoft or third parties. Each one is used with the permissions of the account that creates the flow.","a":["Link the flow to services such as Outlook, SharePoint, Teams or Excel","Group several actions to run them as a single block","Store variables and data between two runs"]},
  "Power BI sert principalement à… ¦ Créer des tableaux de bord et visualiser des données": {"q":"Power BI is mainly used to…","e":"Power BI connects to Excel, SharePoint, databases… and produces interactive reports that can be shared in Teams.","a":["Create dashboards and visualize data","Build business applications without writing code","Manage and secure mobile devices"]},
  "Une stratégie DLP de la Power Platform permet par exemple… ¦ D'interdire qu'un même flux mélange des connecteurs professionnels et des services personnels": {"q":"A Power Platform DLP policy lets you, for example…","e":"For example, it prevents a flow from automatically copying files from SharePoint to a personal Dropbox. Who can create flows is controlled with the environment's security roles.","a":["Prevent a single flow from mixing business connectors with personal services","Automatically encrypt the data that passes through cloud flows","Limit who is allowed to create flows in a given environment"]},
  "Dans Power Automate, un flux déclenché tout seul par un événement (par exemple un nouveau mail reçu) est un flux… ¦ Instantané": {"q":"In Power Automate, a flow that is triggered on its own by an event (for example a new email received) is a(n)… flow.","e":"Automated: triggered by an event. Instant: started manually (button). Scheduled: run at a fixed time.","a":["Instant","Scheduled","Automated"]},
  "Dans une stratégie DLP de la Power Platform, dans quel groupe atterrit par défaut un connecteur nouvellement ajouté au catalogue, si tu ne changes pas ce réglage ? ¦ Non professionnel": {"q":"In a Power Platform DLP policy, which group does a connector newly added to the catalog land in by default, if you don't change that setting?","e":"By default, every new connector is classified as “Non-business”: it can therefore be used, but not together with your business connectors. You can change this default group in the policy, for example to “Blocked” so that nothing gets through without approval.","a":["Non-business","Business","Blocked"]},
  "Pour créer un flux Power Automate simple, il faut savoir programmer. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"To create a simple Power Automate flow, you need to know how to program.","e":"False: Power Automate is a “low-code” tool. You start from a template or assemble a trigger and actions in a few clicks, without writing code."},
  "Dans Power Automate, un flux « instantané » démarre… ¦ Selon un horaire fixe défini dans le flux, par exemple la nuit": {"q":"In Power Automate, an “instant” flow starts…","e":"An instant flow is triggered on demand: a button in the mobile app, in Teams, or on a selected SharePoint file. A scheduled flow follows a timetable, and an automated flow reacts to an event.","a":["On a fixed schedule defined in the flow, for example at night","When the user launches it themselves, for example with a button","As soon as an event occurs, for example the arrival of an email"]},
  "Quel outil Microsoft 365 sert à automatiser des tâches répétitives, comme enregistrer les pièces jointes d'un mail dans OneDrive ? ¦ Power Apps": {"q":"Which Microsoft 365 tool is used to automate repetitive tasks, such as saving an email's attachments to OneDrive?","e":"Power Automate automatically chains actions across services. Power Apps is used to build applications, and Power BI to analyze data.","a":["Power Apps","Power Automate","Power BI","Microsoft Forms"]},
  "Dans un flux Power Automate, les étapes qui suivent le déclencheur (envoyer un mail, créer un fichier…) s'appellent des… ¦ connecteurs": {"q":"In a Power Automate flow, the steps that follow the trigger (send an email, create a file…) are called…","e":"A flow = a trigger followed by actions. Connectors, for their part, are the “bridges” to the services that provide triggers and actions.","a":["connectors","environments","actions","columns"]},
  "Que veut dire « low-code », un terme souvent associé à la Power Platform ? ¦ Un langage de programmation simplifié à apprendre avant de commencer": {"q":"What does “low-code” mean, a term often associated with the Power Platform?","e":"Low-code means you build mostly with visual tools, by drag and drop and configuration, with a few formulas when needed, without being a developer.","a":["A simplified programming language to learn before getting started","A very short script to type in PowerShell to automate everything","Building apps visually with little or no code","A free, limited version of the Power Platform tools"]},
  "Sur quel site web crées-tu et gères-tu tes flux Power Automate ? ¦ make.powerautomate.com": {"q":"On which website do you create and manage your Power Automate flows?","e":"The Power Automate maker portal is make.powerautomate.com. admin.microsoft.com is the Microsoft 365 admin center.","a":["make.powerautomate.com","admin.microsoft.com","portal.azure.com","outlook.office.com"]},
  "Dans Power Automate, à quoi sert un modèle ? ¦ À acheter une licence premium pour débloquer des connecteurs": {"q":"In Power Automate, what is a template for?","e":"Templates are prebuilt flows for common scenarios: you pick one, connect your accounts, and adjust it in a few clicks.","a":["Buying a premium license to unlock connectors","Starting from a ready-to-use flow that you adapt","Viewing the run history of your flows","Blocking a connector considered risky in your environment"]},
  "Ton flux n'a pas fait ce que tu attendais. Où regardes-tu en premier ? ¦ Dans le centre d'administration Exchange": {"q":"Your flow didn't do what you expected. Where do you look first?","e":"The run history shows each run, its status and the step that failed, with the inputs and outputs of each action.","a":["In the Exchange admin center","In the OneDrive recycle bin","In the flow's run history","In the Teams settings"]},
  "Quel outil installe-t-on sur un PC Windows pour automatiser des clics et saisies dans des applications de bureau ? ¦ Power BI Desktop": {"q":"Which tool do you install on a Windows PC to automate clicks and data entry in desktop applications?","e":"Power Automate for desktop creates desktop flows (RPA) that drive Windows applications and websites like a human would. Task Scheduler launches programs at a fixed time, but can't click or type for you.","a":["Power BI Desktop","Power Apps Studio","Windows Task Scheduler","Power Automate for desktop"]},
  "Une liste SharePoint peut servir de source de données à une application Power Apps. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A SharePoint list can be used as a data source for a Power Apps application.","e":"True: SharePoint is one of the most commonly used sources for canvas apps, and Power Apps can even generate an app directly from a list."},
  "Quels sont les trois types de flux cloud proposés à la création dans Power Automate ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Automatisé": {"q":"What are the three types of cloud flows offered when you create a flow in Power Automate? (several answers)","e":"A cloud flow is automated (triggered by an event), instant (launched manually) or scheduled (at a fixed time). “Shared” is not a flow type.","a":["Automated","Instant","Scheduled","Shared"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la création d'un flux automatisé simple : ¦ Ouvrir make.powerautomate.com et cliquer sur « Créer »": {"q":"Put the creation of a simple automated flow in order:","e":"You always start with the flow type, then the trigger, then the actions. Testing lets you check the run in the history.","items":["Open make.powerautomate.com and click “Create”","Choose “Automated cloud flow”","Select the trigger, for example “When a new email arrives”","Add the desired actions","Save, then test the flow"]},
  "Quel connecteur utilises-tu pour déclencher un flux à l'arrivée d'un mail dans ta boîte professionnelle ? (nom du connecteur) ¦ Office 365 Outlook": {"q":"Which connector do you use to trigger a flow when an email arrives in your work mailbox? (connector name)","e":"The Office 365 Outlook connector offers the “When a new email arrives” trigger for Exchange Online mailboxes.","placeholder":"Connector name","answers":["Office 365 Outlook","Outlook","Office365 Outlook"]},
  "Tu veux qu'un flux envoie une demande de validation à ton manager et attende sa réponse avant de continuer. Quelle action utilises-tu ? ¦ Envoyer un e-mail (V2)": {"q":"You want a flow to send an approval request to your manager and wait for their response before continuing. Which action do you use?","e":"“Start and wait for an approval” (Approvals connector) pauses the flow until the response arrives, which is also visible in the Approvals app in Teams.","a":["Send an email (V2)","Start and wait for an approval","Post message in a chat or channel","Delay"]},
  "Quel contrôle d'un flux répète des actions pour chaque élément renvoyé, par exemple chaque ligne de « Obtenir les éléments » ? ¦ Branche parallèle": {"q":"Which flow control repeats actions for each item returned, for example each row from “Get items”?","e":"“Apply to each” loops through an array. “Do until” repeats until a condition is met, a parallel branch runs actions at the same time, and Switch is used for branching.","a":["Parallel branch","Do until","Apply to each","Switch"]},
  "Qu'est-ce qui distingue une app canevas d'une app pilotée par modèle dans Power Apps ? ¦ Dans une app canevas, tu dessines toi-même chaque écran": {"q":"What distinguishes a canvas app from a model-driven app in Power Apps?","e":"A canvas app gives total layout freedom, screen by screen, and connects to many sources. A model-driven app generates the interface from Dataverse data.","a":["In a canvas app, you design each screen yourself","A canvas app only works on mobile","A canvas app necessarily requires Dataverse","A canvas app cannot connect to SharePoint"]},
  "Tu partages ton app canevas basée sur une liste SharePoint, mais un collègue obtient une erreur d'accès aux données. Cause la plus probable ? ¦ Son navigateur n'est pas Microsoft Edge": {"q":"You share your canvas app based on a SharePoint list, but a colleague gets a data access error. Most likely cause?","e":"Sharing an app does not grant access to the data: the user must also have permissions on the source SharePoint list.","a":["Their browser isn't Microsoft Edge","The app must be republished every day","They have no permissions on the SharePoint list itself","They must be a co-owner of the app to open it"]},
  "Dans Power Apps, que fait la formule SubmitForm(EditForm1) ? ¦ Elle vide les champs sans rien enregistrer": {"q":"In Power Apps, what does the formula SubmitForm(EditForm1) do?","e":"SubmitForm validates and sends the form's changes to the data source, without changing screens. To clear the form, use ResetForm.","a":["It clears the fields without saving anything","It saves the form data to the source","It validates the fields then opens the next screen","It deletes the selected item from the source"]},
  "Dans Copilot Studio, comment appelle-t-on les exemples de phrases qui permettent à l'agent de reconnaître une rubrique ? ¦ Des invites système": {"q":"In Copilot Studio, what are the example phrases that let the agent recognize a topic called?","e":"A topic starts when the user's question resembles its trigger phrases; with generative orchestration, its description also plays this role.","a":["System prompts","Connectors","Global variables","Trigger phrases"]},
  "Un flux instantané peut être partagé en « exécution seule » : les utilisateurs peuvent le lancer sans pouvoir le modifier. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"An instant flow can be shared as “run only”: users can launch it without being able to edit it.","e":"True: run-only users launch the flow without seeing or editing its definition, unlike co-owners."},
  "Parmi ces connecteurs, lesquels sont des connecteurs standard (pas de licence premium) ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ SharePoint": {"q":"Which of these connectors are standard connectors (no premium license)? (several answers)","e":"SharePoint and Office 365 Outlook are standard. SQL Server and HTTP are premium and require a Power Apps or Power Automate Premium license.","a":["SharePoint","Office 365 Outlook","SQL Server","HTTP"]},
  "Dans Power Apps, quelle fonction permet de passer d'un écran à un autre ? ¦ Navigate": {"q":"In Power Apps, which function lets you move from one screen to another?","e":"Navigate(Screen2) displays another screen, with an optional transition. Back() returns to the previous screen.","placeholder":"Function name","answers":["Navigate","Navigate()"]},
  "Dans quel centre d'administration gères-tu les environnements et les stratégies de données (DLP) de la Power Platform ? ¦ Le centre d'administration Microsoft 365": {"q":"In which admin center do you manage Power Platform environments and data policies (DLP)?","e":"Environments, DLP policies, capacity and analytics are managed in the Power Platform admin center (admin.powerplatform.microsoft.com). Purview DLP policies concern other data.","a":["The Microsoft 365 admin center","The Power Platform admin center","The Azure portal","The Microsoft Purview portal"]},
  "Quelle affirmation sur l'environnement par défaut de la Power Platform est exacte ? ¦ Seuls les administrateurs peuvent y créer des flux": {"q":"Which statement about the Power Platform default environment is correct?","e":"Every tenant has a default environment where all users are makers. That is why it is protected with strict DLP policies.","a":["Only administrators can create flows in it","It must be created manually after purchasing licenses","All users in the tenant can create apps and flows in it","It can never contain a Dataverse database"]},
  "Tu veux passer une app et ses flux d'un environnement de développement vers la production proprement. Que fais-tu ? ¦ Tu partages le lien de l'app aux utilisateurs de production": {"q":"You want to cleanly move an app and its flows from a development environment to production. What do you do?","e":"Solutions are the application lifecycle management (ALM) mechanism: you generally export a managed solution to production.","a":["You share the app link with production users","You export the SharePoint list to CSV, then reimport it","You create a custom connector to production","You put them in a solution, which you export then import"]},
  "Une app canevas filtre une liste SharePoint volumineuse et affiche un avertissement de délégation. Qu'est-ce que ça implique ? ¦ Le filtre s'exécute en local, sur les premières lignes seulement": {"q":"A canvas app filters a large SharePoint list and shows a delegation warning. What does that imply?","e":"SharePoint does not run a non-delegable formula: it is evaluated locally on the first rows only, up to the data row limit (500 by default, 2,000 maximum). Results may be incomplete with no visible error.","a":["The filter runs locally, on the first rows only","The user doesn't have permission to read the whole SharePoint list","The filter will be handed off to Power Automate, which slows the app down","The list must be converted to an Excel table to be filtered"]},
  "Quelle est la valeur maximale de la « limite de lignes de données » pour les requêtes non délégables dans une app canevas ? ¦ 500": {"q":"What is the maximum value of the “data row limit” for non-delegable queries in a canvas app?","e":"The default is 500 and it can be raised to 2,000 in the app settings. Beyond that, you need delegable formulas.","a":["500","1,000","2,000","5,000"]},
  "Un flux de bureau doit tourner la nuit sur une machine sans session utilisateur ouverte. Quel mode d'exécution faut-il ? ¦ Le mode avec assistance (attended)": {"q":"A desktop flow must run overnight on a machine with no open user session. Which run mode is needed?","e":"Unattended mode signs in to the registered machine by itself. Attended mode requires an active session, and unattended runs require a suitable license (Process plan).","a":["Attended mode","Unattended mode","Recorder mode","Debug mode"]},
  "Dans une stratégie DLP, un connecteur du groupe « Professionnel » (Business) peut échanger des données avec un connecteur du groupe « Non professionnel » dans le même flux. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In a DLP policy, a connector in the “Business” group can exchange data with a connector in the “Non-business” group in the same flow.","e":"False: an app or flow cannot combine connectors from the Business and Non-business groups. Blocked connectors cannot be used at all."},
  "Quels rôles de sécurité Dataverse existent par défaut dans un environnement ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Administrateur système": {"q":"Which Dataverse security roles exist by default in an environment? (several answers)","e":"System Administrator, System Customizer and Environment Maker are environment roles. Exchange Administrator is a Microsoft Entra role.","a":["System Administrator","System Customizer","Environment Maker","Exchange Administrator"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la création d'une stratégie DLP limitée à un environnement : ¦ Ouvrir la section des stratégies de données dans le centre d'administration Power Platform": {"q":"Put the creation of a DLP policy scoped to one environment in order:","e":"The wizard follows this order: name, connector classification, scope then environments, and finally review.","items":["Open the data policies section in the Power Platform admin center","Create a new policy and give it a name","Classify the connectors: Business, Non-business or Blocked","Define the scope and add the targeted environment","Review the summary and create the policy"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet du module d'administration Power Apps exécutes-tu pour te connecter avant d'utiliser Get-AdminPowerApp ? ¦ Add-PowerAppsAccount": {"q":"Which Power Apps administration module cmdlet do you run to sign in before using Get-AdminPowerApp?","e":"Add-PowerAppsAccount opens the session on the tenant; after that, Get-AdminPowerApp, Get-AdminFlow or Get-AdminPowerAppEnvironment become usable.","placeholder":"Cmdlet name","answers":["Add-PowerAppsAccount"]},
  "Tu essaies de placer « Initialiser la variable » à l'intérieur d'une boucle « Appliquer à chacun ». Que se passe-t-il ? ¦ La variable est réinitialisée à chaque itération": {"q":"You try to place “Initialize variable” inside an “Apply to each” loop. What happens?","e":"“Initialize variable” is only allowed at the top level of the flow, not in a loop, a condition or a scope. Inside the loop, you use “Set variable”.","a":["The variable is reset on each iteration","It's impossible: initialization must be done at the top level of the flow","It only works if the loop's concurrency is disabled","The variable becomes local to the loop"]},
  "Tu actives la simultanéité sur une boucle « Appliquer à chacun » qui utilise « Définir la variable » à chaque itération, puis relit cette variable. Quel est le risque ? ¦ Le flux bascule automatiquement en connecteur premium": {"q":"You enable concurrency on an “Apply to each” loop that uses “Set variable” on each iteration, then read that variable back. What is the risk?","e":"Variables are global to the flow: in parallel, an iteration may read back a value written by another. Keep the loop sequential or use Compose actions, which are specific to each iteration. Only “Increment variable” and “Decrement variable” remain reliable in parallel.","a":["The flow automatically switches to a premium connector","The loop stops after the first iteration, with no error","Unpredictable values, because iterations overwrite the variable at the same time","The variable becomes read-only during the loop"]},
  "Pour reproduire un bloc try/catch dans Power Automate, tu combines… ¦ un Commutateur sur le code de statut et une variable booléenne": {"q":"To reproduce a try/catch block in Power Automate, you combine…","e":"A “Try” Scope contains the actions; a “Catch” Scope, whose “Configure run after” is set to “has failed” or “has timed out”, handles the error. A loop with Delay only retries.","a":["a Switch on the status code and a Boolean variable","Scopes and “Configure run after”","an “Until” loop and the Delay action (retry)","parallel branches and the Terminate action"]},
  "Un flux déclenché à chaque modification d'un élément SharePoint ne doit démarrer que si la colonne Statut vaut « Validé », sans créer d'exécutions inutiles. Que configures-tu ? ¦ Une condition de déclencheur dans les paramètres du déclencheur": {"q":"A flow triggered on every change to a SharePoint item must only start if the Status column equals “Approved”, without creating unnecessary runs. What do you configure?","e":"A trigger condition prevents the flow from starting if the expression is false. A Condition action, on the other hand, lets the flow run on every change.","a":["A trigger condition in the trigger settings","A Condition action placed right after the trigger","A filter on the list's default view","A DLP policy on the SharePoint connector"]},
  "Le créateur d'une app canevas critique quitte l'entreprise. Quelle cmdlet permet de réaffecter l'app à un nouveau propriétaire ? ¦ Set-PowerAppOwner": {"q":"The creator of a critical canvas app leaves the company. Which cmdlet lets you reassign the app to a new owner?","e":"Set-AdminPowerAppOwner (Microsoft.PowerApps.Administration.PowerShell module) takes -AppName, -EnvironmentName and -AppOwner. The Mg cmdlets target Entra ID applications, not Power Apps.","a":["Set-PowerAppOwner","Grant-PowerAppOwnership","Update-MgApplicationOwner","Set-AdminPowerAppOwner"]},
  "Deux stratégies DLP couvrent le même environnement : l'une classe un connecteur en Non professionnel, l'autre le bloque. Quel est le résultat ? ¦ La stratégie créée en dernier l'emporte": {"q":"Two DLP policies cover the same environment: one classifies a connector as Non-business, the other blocks it. What is the result?","e":"When several policies apply, they add up and the most restrictive wins. There is no priority by date or by level.","a":["The most recently created policy wins","The environment-level policy takes precedence over the tenant-level one","The connector is blocked: the most restrictive combination applies","The connector remains usable as Non-business"]},
  "Dans une stratégie DLP, comment autoriser le connecteur HTTP uniquement vers certains domaines ? ¦ Avec le filtrage des points de terminaison": {"q":"In a DLP policy, how do you allow the HTTP connector only to certain domains?","e":"Endpoint filtering allows or denies specific URLs for certain connectors (HTTP, SQL Server…). Action control blocks actions, not destinations.","a":["With endpoint filtering","With connector action control","With tenant isolation","With a Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access policy"]},
  "Dans une stratégie DLP, n'importe quel connecteur peut être placé dans le groupe « Bloqué ». ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In a DLP policy, any connector can be placed in the “Blocked” group.","e":"False: some essential Microsoft connectors, such as SharePoint or Microsoft Dataverse, cannot be blocked; they can only be classified as Business or Non-business."},
  "Quels composants d'une solution permettent de déployer un flux dans un autre environnement sans modifier sa définition ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Les variables d'environnement": {"q":"Which solution components let you deploy a flow to another environment without changing its definition? (several answers)","e":"Environment variables externalize values (site URL, list ID) and connection references decouple the flow from connections, which are linked at import.","a":["Environment variables","Connection references","DLP policies","Microsoft Entra ID security groups"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre le déplacement d'une solution avec Power Platform CLI : ¦ S'authentifier sur l'environnement source avec pac auth create": {"q":"Put in order the steps to move a solution with the Power Platform CLI:","e":"pac auth manages connection profiles; you export from the source, switch profiles, then import the .zip file into the target.","items":["Authenticate to the source environment with pac auth create","Export the solution with pac solution export","Select the target environment's profile with pac auth select","Import the solution with pac solution import"]},
  "Quel module PowerShell fournit les cmdlets Get-AdminFlow et Get-AdminPowerApp ? ¦ Microsoft.PowerApps.Administration.PowerShell": {"q":"Which PowerShell module provides the Get-AdminFlow and Get-AdminPowerApp cmdlets?","e":"Microsoft.PowerApps.Administration.PowerShell is the administration module; Microsoft.PowerApps.PowerShell covers the maker-side cmdlets.","placeholder":"Module name","answers":["Microsoft.PowerApps.Administration.PowerShell"]},
  "Quelle fonction moderne remplace RECHERCHEV dans Excel ? ¦ RECHERCHEH": {"q":"Which modern function replaces VLOOKUP in Excel?","e":"XLOOKUP searches in any direction, handles “not found”, and breaks less when you add columns.","a":["HLOOKUP","XLOOKUP","XMATCH"]},
  "Dans Excel, une formule commence toujours par… ¦ Le signe =": {"q":"In Excel, a formula always starts with…","e":"Without the = sign, Excel assumes you are typing text.","a":["The = sign","The $ sign","The word “Abracadabra”"]},
  "Que calcule =SOMME(A1:A10) ? ¦ La moyenne de A1 et A10": {"q":"What does =SUM(A1:A10) calculate?","e":"The colon defines a range: from A1 to A10 inclusive.","a":["The average of A1 and A10","The total of the cells from A1 to A10","The number of filled cells"]},
  "Pour garder la ligne d'en-tête visible quand tu fais défiler un grand tableau : ¦ Affichage, puis Figer les volets": {"q":"To keep the header row visible when you scroll through a large table:","e":"“Freeze Top Row” keeps your column headings always visible on screen. “Print Titles” only repeats them on printed pages.","a":["View, then Freeze Panes","Page Layout, then Print Titles","I zoom to 10% to see everything at once"]},
  "Dans une formule Excel, $A$1 est une référence… ¦ Absolue : elle ne bouge pas quand on recopie la formule": {"q":"In an Excel formula, $A$1 is a(n)… reference.","e":"The $ locks the column and/or the row. Press F4 to quickly switch between reference types.","a":["Absolute: it doesn't move when you copy the formula","Mixed: only the row stays fixed when copied","Relative: it shifts when copied"]},
  "Un tableau croisé dynamique sert à… ¦ Résumer et analyser rapidement un grand volume de données": {"q":"A PivotTable is used to…","e":"In a few drag-and-drops: total sales by month and by salesperson, number of tickets by category…","a":["Quickly summarize and analyze a large volume of data","Merge several workbooks into one sheet","Copy a formula down all the rows of a range"]},
  "Que renvoie =SI(A2>=10;\"Admis\";\"Recalé\") si A2 vaut 12 ? ¦ Recalé": {"q":"What does =IF(A2>=10,\"Pass\",\"Fail\") return if A2 is 12?","e":"IF(condition, value if true, value if false). 12 is greater than or equal to 10: the condition is true.","a":["Fail","Pass","12"]},
  "La mise en forme conditionnelle permet… ¦ De colorer automatiquement des cellules selon leur valeur": {"q":"Conditional formatting lets you…","e":"Example: turn stock levels below a threshold red, or goals that are met green.","a":["Automatically color cells based on their value","Hide rows that don't meet a criterion","Display a message if the entry is invalid"]},
  "Que calcule =NB.SI(B:B;\"Paris\") ? ¦ La somme des montants de la colonne B liés à « Paris »": {"q":"What does =COUNTIF(B:B,\"Paris\") calculate?","e":"COUNTIF counts the cells that meet a condition. Its cousin SUMIF adds up conditionally.","a":["The sum of the amounts in column B linked to “Paris”","The number of cells in column B that contain “Paris”","The number of non-empty cells in column B"]},
  "Créer un tableau croisé dynamique dans Excel : ¦ Sélectionner les données": {"q":"Create a PivotTable in Excel:","e":"Tip: first format your data as a table (Ctrl+T); the PivotTable will update more easily when you add rows.","items":["Select the data","Insert, then PivotTable","Choose the location of the table","Drag the fields into Rows, Columns and Values"]},
  "Une RECHERCHEX renvoie #N/A. Cela signifie en général… ¦ Que la valeur cherchée est introuvable": {"q":"An XLOOKUP returns #N/A. This generally means…","e":"XLOOKUP has a 4th argument to display a message instead, for example “Not found”. Ranges of different sizes give #VALUE!, and an occupied spill range gives #SPILL!.","a":["The lookup value cannot be found","The lookup and return ranges are not the same size","The result spills over cells that are already filled"]},
  "Dans Word, le « suivi des modifications » permet… ¦ De voir qui a modifié quoi, et d'accepter ou refuser chaque changement": {"q":"In Word, “Track Changes” lets you…","e":"Essential for reviewing a contract or a procedure with several people: every addition and deletion stays visible.","a":["See who changed what, and accept or reject each change","Go back to a previously saved version on OneDrive","Add comments in the margin for reviewers"]},
  "Le « mode Présentateur » de PowerPoint affiche… ¦ Les notes et la diapositive suivante, visibles seulement par toi": {"q":"PowerPoint's “Presenter View” displays…","e":"The audience sees the slide; you also see your notes, a timer and what comes next.","a":["The notes and the next slide, visible only to you","The slides as thumbnails so you can rearrange them","The slide text as an outline, without the images"]},
  "L'enregistrement automatique s'active quand le fichier est stocké sur OneDrive ou SharePoint. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"AutoSave is enabled when the file is stored on OneDrive or SharePoint.","e":"True: every change is saved as you go, and version history lets you go back."},
  "Dans Excel, le raccourci Ctrl+T sert à… ¦ Mettre une plage de données sous forme de tableau": {"q":"In Excel, the Ctrl+T shortcut is used to…","e":"A table expands on its own when you add rows, and makes sorting, filters, formulas… and the use of Copilot easier.","a":["Format a data range as a table","Insert a PivotTable from the range","Open the Format Cells dialog box"]},
  "Pour générer une table des matières automatique dans Word : ¦ J'utilise les styles de titre (Titre 1, Titre 2…)": {"q":"To generate an automatic table of contents in Word:","e":"Word builds the table from the heading styles, and updates it in one click when the document changes.","a":["I use heading styles (Heading 1, Heading 2…)","I type the page numbers by hand","I make each heading bold and in a larger size"]},
  "Pour créer une liste déroulante dans une cellule Excel : ¦ Validation des données": {"q":"To create a drop-down list in an Excel cell:","e":"Data tab, then Data Validation, then “List”. Entries stay consistent, and no more “Yes”, “yes” and “YES”.","a":["Data Validation","Conditional Formatting","Freeze Panes"]},
  "Que renvoie la fonction UNIQUE dans Excel ? ¦ La liste des valeurs distinctes d'une plage": {"q":"What does the UNIQUE function return in Excel?","e":"=UNIQUE(A2:A100) lists each value only once. Combined with SORT or FILTER, it replaces a lot of manual work.","a":["The list of distinct values in a range","The number of distinct values in a range","The duplicates in a range, highlighted"]},
  "Le raccourci Ctrl+H dans Excel ou Word ouvre… ¦ Rechercher et remplacer": {"q":"The Ctrl+H shortcut in Excel or Word opens…","e":"Replacing “Co.” with “Company” in 500 cells takes two seconds.","a":["Find and Replace","Find (without replacing)","Go to a page or a cell"]},
  "Quelle fonction Excel renvoie la position d'une valeur dans une plage (souvent combinée avec INDEX) ? ¦ EQUIV": {"q":"Which Excel function returns the position of a value in a range (often combined with INDEX)?","e":"INDEX(range, MATCH(value, column, 0)) was the go-to combination before XLOOKUP. XMATCH is its modern version.","placeholder":"Function name","answers":["EQUIV","MATCH","EQUIVX","XMATCH"]},
  "Pour annuler ta dernière action dans Word, Excel ou PowerPoint : ¦ Ctrl+Z": {"q":"To undo your last action in Word, Excel or PowerPoint:","e":"Ctrl+Z undoes, Ctrl+Y redoes. Ctrl+A selects everything and Ctrl+P opens printing.","a":["Ctrl+Z","Ctrl+Y","Shout “Undo!” very loudly at your screen"]},
  "Dans Excel, que renvoie =FILTRE(A2:C100;C2:C100>1000) ? ¦ La somme des valeurs de la colonne C supérieures à 1000": {"q":"In Excel, what does =FILTER(A2:C100,C2:C100>1000) return?","e":"FILTER extracts the rows that meet the condition and automatically “spills” them into the neighboring cells. If the data changes, the result updates by itself.","a":["The sum of the values in column C greater than 1000","All the rows from A to C where column C exceeds 1000","The number of rows from A to C where column C exceeds 1000"]},
  "Une formule Excel moderne affiche l'erreur #PROPAGATION! (#SPILL! en anglais). La cause la plus fréquente ? ¦ Le fichier n'est pas enregistré sur OneDrive": {"q":"A modern Excel formula displays the #SPILL! error. The most common cause?","e":"Dynamic array functions (FILTER, UNIQUE, SORT…) need a free area to spread their result. You clear the blocking cells, and the formula spills out.","a":["The file isn't saved on OneDrive","The formula contains an indirect circular reference","Some cells in the spill range are not empty"]},
  "Dans PowerPoint, tu veux que les puces d'une diapositive apparaissent une par une pendant le diaporama. Tu utilises… ¦ l'onglet Transitions": {"q":"In PowerPoint, you want the bullets on a slide to appear one by one during the slide show. You use…","e":"Animations apply to the elements of a slide (text, images) and control how they appear. Transitions, on the other hand, handle the move from one slide to the next.","a":["the Transitions tab","the Animations tab","the slide master","Presenter View"]},
  "Dans Word, le raccourci Ctrl+Entrée insère un saut de page. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In Word, the Ctrl+Enter shortcut inserts a page break.","e":"Ctrl+Enter inserts a page break: the following text starts at the top of the next page. It's cleaner than chaining line breaks, which shift everything as soon as you edit the text above."},
  "Dans Excel, une cellule affiche #DIV/0!. Que se passe-t-il ? ¦ La colonne est trop étroite pour afficher le nombre": {"q":"In Excel, a cell displays #DIV/0!. What is happening?","e":"#DIV/0! signals a division by zero (or by an empty cell). A column that is too narrow displays #####, a misspelled function name gives #NAME?, and a deleted reference gives #REF!.","a":["The column is too narrow to display the number","The formula contains a typo in the function name","The formula is trying to divide by zero or by an empty cell","The cell refers to a deleted sheet"]},
  "Dans PowerPoint, quelle touche du clavier lance le diaporama depuis la première diapositive ? ¦ F5": {"q":"In PowerPoint, which keyboard key starts the slide show from the first slide?","e":"F5 starts the slide show from the beginning. Shift+F5 starts it from the displayed slide.","placeholder":"Key name","answers":["F5"]},
  "Dans PowerPoint, le « masque des diapositives » sert à… ¦ Définir une mise en forme commune à toutes les diapositives": {"q":"In PowerPoint, the “slide master” is used to…","e":"The slide master (View > Slide Master) defines the layout and style (fonts, logo, colors) of all slides at once. To hide a slide, you use “Hide Slide”, which has nothing to do with it.","a":["Define a common format for all slides","Hide a slide during the slide show without deleting it from the file","Protect the presentation with a password when opening it","Display the speaker notes on your screen during the presentation"]},
  "Quelles extensions correspondent aux formats de fichier actuels de Word, Excel et PowerPoint ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ .docx": {"q":"Which extensions match the current file formats of Word, Excel and PowerPoint? (several answers)","e":".docx, .xlsx and .pptx are the modern Office formats (XML-based). .pdf is an export format for distributing a fixed document, not the native format of an Office app.","a":[".docx",".pdf",".xlsx",".pptx"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre les étapes pour restaurer une version précédente d'un document Word stocké sur OneDrive : ¦ Ouvrir le document dans Word": {"q":"Put in order the steps to restore a previous version of a Word document stored on OneDrive:","e":"For a file stored on OneDrive or SharePoint, version history keeps the previous states. You open the desired version to check it, then restore it: it becomes the current version, and the replaced version stays in the history.","items":["Open the document in Word","Go to File > Info > Version History","Open the desired earlier version to check it","Click “Restore”"]},
  "Dans Word, où lances-tu le vérificateur d'accessibilité ? ¦ Onglet Insertion > Vérifier l'accessibilité": {"q":"In Word, where do you run the accessibility checker?","e":"The checker is in the Review tab. It flags, for example, images without alt text, insufficient contrast or tables without a header row.","a":["Insert tab > Check Accessibility","View tab > Read Mode","Review tab > Check Accessibility","Layout tab > Accessibility"]},
  "Dans Excel, quel raccourci insère la date du jour (valeur fixe) dans la cellule active ? ¦ Ctrl+;": {"q":"In Excel, which shortcut inserts today's date (fixed value) into the active cell?","e":"Ctrl+; inserts today's date as a fixed value that will no longer change. By contrast, the =TODAY() function recalculates every day.","placeholder":"E.g.: Ctrl+…","answers":["Ctrl+;","Ctrl+point-virgule","Ctrl ;","Ctrl + ;"]},
  "Le texte de remplacement (alt text) ajouté à une image sert surtout à la décrire aux personnes qui utilisent un lecteur d'écran. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"The alt text added to an image is mainly used to describe it to people who use a screen reader.","e":"Alt text is read by screen readers to describe the image to visually impaired people. A purely decorative image can be marked “Decorative” so that it is ignored."},
  "Tu dois déployer les Apps Microsoft 365 en choisissant les applications, la langue et le canal de mise à jour. Quel outil Microsoft utilises-tu ? ¦ Le Programme d'installation Windows (msiexec) avec un fichier .msi": {"q":"You need to deploy Microsoft 365 Apps by choosing the applications, the language and the update channel. Which Microsoft tool do you use?","e":"The Office Deployment Tool (setup.exe) reads a configuration.xml file that describes the applications, the language, the architecture and the channel. Microsoft 365 Apps are installed with Click-to-Run, not via an .msi.","a":["Windows Installer (msiexec) with an .msi file","The Office Deployment Tool (ODT) with a configuration.xml file","The Microsoft Support and Recovery Assistant (SaRA)","The Microsoft Entra admin center, Applications section"]},
  "Quel outil web de Microsoft (config.office.com) permet de générer graphiquement le fichier configuration.xml de l'ODT ? ¦ Office Customization Tool": {"q":"Which Microsoft web tool (config.office.com) lets you graphically generate the ODT's configuration.xml file?","e":"The Office Customization Tool, accessible from config.office.com, generates the configuration.xml file from a form. It is safer than writing the XML by hand.","placeholder":"Tool name","answers":["Office Customization Tool","Outil de personnalisation d'Office","OCT"]},
  "Quels canaux de mise à jour existent pour les Apps Microsoft 365 for enterprise ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Canal actuel": {"q":"Which update channels exist for Microsoft 365 Apps for enterprise? (several answers)","e":"Microsoft 365 Apps offer the Current Channel and the Monthly Enterprise Channel (plus preview channels). Since version 2606 (July 2026), the Semi-Annual Enterprise Channel has been unified with the Monthly Enterprise Channel. LTSC applies to Office LTSC, a perpetual version, and the Windows Insider channel applies to Windows, not Office.","a":["Current Channel","Monthly Enterprise Channel","Long-Term Servicing Channel (LTSC)","Windows Insider Dev Channel"]},
  "Tu veux empêcher les utilisateurs d'installer eux-mêmes les apps Office de bureau depuis leur portail. Où le configures-tu ? ¦ Centre d'administration Microsoft Entra > Applications d'entreprise > Paramètres utilisateur": {"q":"You want to prevent users from installing the desktop Office apps themselves from their portal. Where do you configure this?","e":"In the Microsoft 365 admin center, the Microsoft 365 installation options (Org settings > Services) let you choose which apps users can install themselves. You can then deploy the apps yourself, with Intune or the ODT for example.","a":["Microsoft Entra admin center > Enterprise applications > User settings","Microsoft Purview portal > Information protection > Labels","Microsoft Intune admin center > Devices > Device compliance","Microsoft 365 admin center > Org settings > Installation options"]},
  "Quel service applique des stratégies Office (paramètres Word, Excel, etc.) aux utilisateurs, même sur des appareils personnels non joints au domaine ? ¦ Les stratégies de groupe (GPO) avec les modèles ADMX Office": {"q":"Which service applies Office policies (Word, Excel settings, etc.) to users, even on personal devices not joined to the domain?","e":"The Cloud Policy service (config.office.com) applies Office policies to the user as soon as they sign in with their work account, regardless of the device. GPOs require machines joined to Active Directory, and Intune compliance policies assess the device's state without configuring the Office apps.","a":["Group Policy (GPO) with the Office ADMX templates","The Cloud Policy service of the Microsoft 365 Apps admin center","Intune compliance policies","Microsoft Purview DLP policies"]},
  "Avec une licence incluant les Apps Microsoft 365, chaque utilisateur peut installer les apps de bureau sur jusqu'à 5 PC ou Mac, 5 tablettes et 5 smartphones. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"With a license that includes Microsoft 365 Apps, each user can install the desktop apps on up to 5 PCs or Macs, 5 tablets and 5 smartphones.","e":"Each licensed user can install the apps on 5 PCs or Macs, 5 tablets and 5 smartphones. For shared machines (RDS, Azure Virtual Desktop), you use shared computer activation."},
  "Quelle fonction Excel permet de nommer des résultats intermédiaires à l'intérieur d'une formule pour éviter de les recalculer ? ¦ LAMBDA": {"q":"Which Excel function lets you name intermediate results inside a formula to avoid recalculating them?","e":"LET assigns names to values or calculations in the formula, for example =LET(x,A1*2,x+x). The formula becomes more readable and faster. LAMBDA is used to create reusable custom functions.","a":["LAMBDA","CHOOSE","INDIRECT","LET"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre un déploiement des Apps Microsoft 365 avec l'Outil de déploiement d'Office : ¦ Télécharger et extraire l'Outil de déploiement d'Office": {"q":"Put a Microsoft 365 Apps deployment with the Office Deployment Tool in order:","e":"You first get setup.exe, then describe the installation in configuration.xml. The /download mode pre-downloads the files to a local share, and the /configure mode starts the installation according to that file.","items":["Download and extract the Office Deployment Tool","Create the configuration.xml file (for example with the Office Customization Tool)","Run setup.exe /download configuration.xml to download the sources","Run setup.exe /configure configuration.xml to install"]},
  "Quel commutateur de setup.exe (Outil de déploiement d'Office) lance l'installation selon le fichier configuration.xml ? ¦ /configure": {"q":"Which setup.exe switch (Office Deployment Tool) starts the installation according to the configuration.xml file?","e":"setup.exe /configure configuration.xml installs (or modifies) the Apps according to the file. /download only downloads the sources, and /packager is used to create an App-V package.","placeholder":"E.g.: /…","answers":["/configure","configure"]},
  "Dans configuration.xml, comment exclus-tu Access d'une installation des Apps Microsoft 365 ? ¦ <RemoveApp ID=\"Access\" /> à la racine de <Configuration>": {"q":"In configuration.xml, how do you exclude Access from a Microsoft 365 Apps installation?","e":"The ExcludeApp element, placed inside Product, prevents a specific application (Access, OneNote, Teams, etc.) from being installed. The other elements listed do not exist in the ODT schema.","a":["<RemoveApp ID=\"Access\" /> at the root of <Configuration>","<Disable App=\"Access\" /> in the <Updates> element","<ExcludeApp ID=\"Access\" /> in the <Product> element","<Exclude Product=\"Access\" /> in the <Add> element"]},
  "Quel Product ID indiques-tu dans configuration.xml pour installer Microsoft 365 Apps for enterprise ? ¦ O365BusinessRetail": {"q":"Which Product ID do you specify in configuration.xml to install Microsoft 365 Apps for enterprise?","e":"Microsoft 365 Apps for enterprise corresponds to the Product ID O365ProPlusRetail, inherited from the former name “Office 365 ProPlus”. O365BusinessRetail corresponds to Microsoft 365 Apps for business, and ProPlus2024Volume to Office LTSC Professional Plus 2024.","a":["O365BusinessRetail","O365ProPlusRetail","M365EnterpriseRetail","ProPlus2024Volume"]},
  "Depuis la version 2606 (juillet 2026), les postes configurés sur le Canal Entreprise semi-annuel reçoivent chaque mois les mêmes mises à jour que le Canal Entreprise mensuel. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Since version 2606 (July 2026), devices configured on the Semi-Annual Enterprise Channel receive the same updates every month as the Monthly Enterprise Channel.","e":"True: Microsoft has unified the Semi-Annual Enterprise Channel with the Monthly Enterprise Channel. Devices receive new features and fixes every month (on the 2nd Tuesday) and show up as Monthly Enterprise Channel in File > Account. The January/July cadence has ended."},
  "Quelles affirmations sur l'activation d'ordinateurs partagés des Apps Microsoft 365 sont exactes ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Elle s'active dans configuration.xml avec la propriété SharedComputerLicensing à 1": {"q":"Which statements about shared computer activation for Microsoft 365 Apps are correct? (several answers)","e":"Shared computer activation (<Property Name=\"SharedComputerLicensing\" Value=\"1\" />) lets several licensed users use the same machine without consuming their installations. Business Basic does not include the desktop apps, so that license is not enough.","a":["It is enabled in configuration.xml with the SharedComputerLicensing property set to 1","It targets RDS and Azure Virtual Desktop environments, among others","It works with a Microsoft 365 Business Basic license","It does not count toward the user's installation limit"]},
  "Dans RECHERCHEX, quelle valeur du 5e argument (mode_correspondance) active les caractères génériques * et ? ? ¦ -1": {"q":"In XLOOKUP, which value of the 5th argument (match_mode) enables the wildcard characters * and ?","e":"Mode 2 enables wildcard characters. 0 (the default) requires an exact match, -1 accepts the exact value or the next smaller item, and 1 the exact value or the next larger item.","a":["-1","1","2","0"]},
  "Un classeur créé dans une ancienne version d'Excel s'ouvre dans Excel pour Microsoft 365 et certaines formules affichent un @ devant une référence. Que signifie ce @ ? ¦ La formule est protégée et ne peut pas être modifiée": {"q":"A workbook created in an older version of Excel opens in Excel for Microsoft 365 and some formulas show an @ in front of a reference. What does this @ mean?","e":"With dynamic arrays, Excel adds @ to preserve the old implicit intersection behavior, which returns only one value instead of spilling an array. Without @, the formula could spill over several cells.","a":["The formula is protected and cannot be modified","Implicit intersection: the formula returns only a single value, as in older Excel","The reference points to a colleague mention in a comment","The formula is a legacy array formula to be confirmed with Ctrl+Shift+Enter"]},
  "Des utilisateurs ne peuvent pas co-éditer en temps réel des documents chiffrés par une étiquette de confidentialité. Quelle action d'admin règle ce problème ? ¦ Accorder le droit Copropriétaire à tous dans l'étiquette": {"q":"Users cannot co-author documents encrypted by a sensitivity label in real time. Which admin action fixes this problem?","e":"Microsoft Purview offers a tenant-level setting that enables co-authoring and AutoSave for files encrypted by a label. The Apps versions must support it. Widening the label's permissions or changing the update channel does not unlock co-authoring.","a":["Grant the Co-owner permission to everyone in the label","Enable co-authoring for files encrypted with a label in Purview","Disable AutoSave in the Cloud Policy service","Move all devices to the Semi-Annual Enterprise Channel"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la création d'une configuration dans le service Cloud Policy : ¦ Se connecter au centre d'administration Microsoft 365 Apps (config.office.com)": {"q":"Put the creation of a configuration in the Cloud Policy service in order:","e":"A Cloud Policy configuration targets a group of users, then you enable the settings in it. The Apps periodically retrieve the policies for the signed-in account, without the machine needing to be joined to the domain.","items":["Sign in to the Microsoft 365 Apps admin center (config.office.com)","Open policy management and create a policy configuration","Name the configuration and choose its scope (user group)","Search for and configure the desired policy settings","Save the configuration so that it applies to users"]},
  "Dans configuration.xml, quelle valeur de l'attribut Channel correspond au Canal Entreprise mensuel ? ¦ Monthly": {"q":"In configuration.xml, which Channel attribute value corresponds to Monthly Enterprise Channel?","e":"The recommended values are Current, MonthlyEnterprise and SemiAnnual (the latter has followed the monthly cadence since the July 2026 unification). Monthly and Broad are legacy names, still accepted but best avoided in a new configuration. EnterpriseMonthly does not exist.","a":["Monthly","EnterpriseMonthly","MonthlyEnterprise","Broad"]},
  "Tu as écrit une fonction LAMBDA et tu veux l'appeler par son nom partout dans le classeur. Que fais-tu ? ¦ Tu l'enregistres comme macro dans un module VBA": {"q":"You wrote a LAMBDA function and want to call it by name anywhere in the workbook. What do you do?","e":"A LAMBDA is named in Name Manager (Formulas > Name Manager). You then call it like a built-in function, for example =MyFunction(A2), with no VBA.","a":["Save it as a macro in a VBA module","Put it in a hidden cell and reference it with INDIRECT","Add it as an .xlam add-in in the Excel options","Define it as a name in Name Manager"]},
  "Obligation légale de conserver les mails pendant plusieurs années : ¦ On active l'archivage en ligne illimité sur chaque boîte": {"q":"Legal requirement to keep emails for several years:","e":"A retention policy keeps items even if the user deletes them. Online archiving frees up space, but does not prevent deletion.","a":["You enable unlimited online archiving on every mailbox","You export mailboxes to PST every month","You create a retention policy in Microsoft Purview"]},
  "À quoi sert Microsoft Secure Score ? ¦ À mesurer la conformité aux réglementations (RGPD, ISO 27001)": {"q":"What is Microsoft Secure Score used for?","e":"It scores your configuration and lists the improvements to make, with their impact. Regulatory compliance is the job of Purview Compliance Manager, user risk that of Entra ID Protection.","a":["Measuring compliance with regulations (GDPR, ISO 27001)","Measuring the tenant's security posture and suggesting actions","Rating the risk level of each user"]},
  "Les étiquettes de confidentialité (Microsoft Purview) permettent… ¦ De classer un document et de le protéger (chiffrement, filigrane), même hors de l'entreprise": {"q":"Sensitivity labels (Microsoft Purview) allow you to…","e":"Protection travels with the file: an encrypted “Confidential” document stays unreadable to an unauthorized person. Keeping a document for X years is the role of retention labels; blocking a send is that of DLP.","a":["Classify a document and protect it (encryption, watermark), even outside the company","Keep a document for a set period (3 years, 10 years…) before it is deleted","Block the sending of an email containing credit card numbers"]},
  "Une stratégie DLP (prévention des pertes de données) sert à… ¦ Détecter et bloquer le partage de données sensibles (numéros de carte, données de santé…)": {"q":"A DLP (data loss prevention) policy is used to…","e":"Example: blocking the sending of a file containing credit card numbers outside the company, or warning the user before they do it.","a":["Detect and block the sharing of sensitive data (card numbers, health data…)","Add a “Confidential” watermark to documents based on their sensitivity","Keep sensitive data for the time required by law (legal retention)"]},
  "Pour savoir qui a supprimé un fichier sur un site SharePoint, on consulte… ¦ Le journal d'audit (Microsoft Purview)": {"q":"To find out who deleted a file on a SharePoint site, you check…","e":"The audit log tracks the actions of users and admins: who, what, when, from which IP address.","a":["The audit log (Microsoft Purview)","The file's version history","The SharePoint usage reports in the admin center"]},
  "Les « liens fiables » (Safe Links) de Defender pour Office 365… ¦ Vérifient une URL au moment où l'utilisateur clique dessus": {"q":"The “Safe Links” feature of Defender for Office 365…","e":"A link can be harmless when received and booby-trapped an hour later: checking at click time protects against this technique.","a":["Checks a URL at the moment the user clicks it","Scans links only on receipt, before delivery","Blocks links to domains that are not on an allow list"]},
  "Les « pièces jointes fiables » (Safe Attachments)… ¦ Ouvrent les pièces jointes dans un bac à sable pour observer leur comportement": {"q":"“Safe Attachments”…","e":"The attachment is “detonated” in a sandbox before it reaches the mailbox: unknown malware is spotted by its behavior.","a":["Open attachments in a sandbox to observe their behavior","Compare attachments against a database of known antivirus signatures","Systematically block .exe and .zip attachments (file type filter)"]},
  "La formation par simulation d'attaque de Defender permet… ¦ D'envoyer de faux phishing aux salariés pour les entraîner": {"q":"Defender's attack simulation training lets you…","e":"Those who click receive a short training. The goal is not to trap people, but to improve their reflexes, just like on Power Up!","a":["Send fake phishing emails to employees to train them","Have an external penetration test (pentest) of the tenant carried out","Replay a past attack to test Defender's detections"]},
  "Microsoft Purview eDiscovery sert à… ¦ Rechercher, conserver et exporter des contenus pour une enquête ou un litige": {"q":"Microsoft Purview eDiscovery is used to…","e":"Emails, files, Teams chats: you find and preserve what is needed, with full traceability.","a":["Search, preserve and export content for an investigation or a legal dispute","Spot cloud apps used without authorization (shadow IT)","Automatically label the company's sensitive documents"]},
  "La conservation pour litige (litigation hold) sur une boîte mail… ¦ Préserve tout son contenu, même ce que l'utilisateur supprime": {"q":"A litigation hold on a mailbox…","e":"The user keeps working normally, but nothing really disappears as long as the hold is active.","a":["Preserves all of its content, even what the user deletes","Blocks the user's sign-in during the procedure","Moves emails older than two years to the archive"]},
  "Le portail unifié de Microsoft Defender XDR se trouve à l'adresse… ¦ security.microsoft.com": {"q":"The unified Microsoft Defender XDR portal is found at the address…","e":"It brings together alerts and incidents from devices, email, identities and cloud apps in one place.","a":["security.microsoft.com","compliance.microsoft.com","intune.microsoft.com"]},
  "Quelles données une stratégie DLP de Microsoft Purview peut-elle repérer ? ¦ Des numéros de carte bancaire": {"q":"What data can a Microsoft Purview DLP policy detect?","e":"Purview provides ready-made sensitive information types, to warn or block before the data leaves the company. Sender spoofing falls under Defender's anti-phishing.","a":["Credit card numbers","IBANs","Social security numbers","Emails with a spoofed sender (spoofing)"]},
  "Dans Microsoft Defender XDR, un « incident »… ¦ Regroupe plusieurs alertes liées à une même attaque": {"q":"In Microsoft Defender XDR, an “incident”…","e":"Instead of 30 scattered alerts (booby-trapped email, infected device, suspicious sign-in), the analyst sees a single attack story.","a":["Groups several alerts related to the same attack","Is a standalone alert raised by a single product","Is a Microsoft outage shown in Service health"]},
  "Comment s'appellent les étiquettes Microsoft Purview qui classent et protègent un document (Public, Confidentiel…) ? ¦ Étiquettes de confidentialité": {"q":"What are the Microsoft Purview labels that classify and protect a document (Public, Confidential…) called?","e":"A sensitivity label can encrypt the document, add a watermark and block external sharing, even when the file leaves the company.","placeholder":"… labels","answers":["Étiquettes de confidentialité","Étiquette de confidentialité","de confidentialité","confidentialité","Étiquettes de sensibilité","Étiquette de sensibilité","sensibilité","Sensitivity labels","Sensitivity label","sensitivity labels","sensitivity label","labels"]},
  "En survolant un lien dans un mail professionnel, tu vois une adresse contenant « safelinks.protection.outlook.com ». Ça signifie… ¦ Que le lien a été réécrit par Defender pour être vérifié au moment du clic": {"q":"When hovering over a link in a work email, you see an address containing “safelinks.protection.outlook.com”. This means…","e":"Safe Links in Defender for Office 365 rewrite links to check the destination at every click. It does not vouch for the site: keep your reflexes with suspicious emails.","a":["The link was rewritten by Defender so it can be checked at click time","The site has already been checked and declared safe by Microsoft","The destination site is hosted by Microsoft"]},
  "La purge automatique « zéro heure » (ZAP) d'Exchange Online… ¦ Bloque dès la réception les malwares encore inconnus des antivirus (zero-day)": {"q":"Zero-hour auto purge (ZAP) in Exchange Online…","e":"An email can look harmless on arrival and then be identified as malicious a few minutes later. ZAP will then move it to Junk Email or quarantine, even if it is already in the mailbox. Nothing to do with “zero-day” vulnerabilities.","a":["Blocks, on receipt, malware still unknown to antivirus (zero-day)","Removes, after the fact, already delivered emails once they are recognized as phishing, spam or malware","Purges recoverable deleted items from mailboxes every night"]},
  "Un PDF protégé par une étiquette de confidentialité avec chiffrement est transféré par son destinataire autorisé à une personne non autorisée. Que se passe-t-il ? ¦ Le fichier s'ouvre, mais en lecture seule et avec un filigrane": {"q":"A PDF protected by a sensitivity label with encryption is forwarded by its authorized recipient to an unauthorized person. What happens?","e":"Microsoft Purview Information Protection encryption travels with the file: when it is opened, the service checks identity and rights. A person who is not in the permissions cannot read it, even with a copy.","a":["The file opens, but read-only and with a watermark","The label and its encryption are dropped as soon as the file leaves the tenant","They cannot open it: the encryption follows the file"]},
  "Un mail de phishing a été livré à 200 boîtes. Pour le retrouver et le supprimer de toutes les boîtes en une seule opération, l'admin utilise… ¦ L'Explorateur de menaces de Defender pour Office 365 (Plan 2)": {"q":"A phishing email was delivered to 200 mailboxes. To find it and remove it from all mailboxes in a single operation, the admin uses…","e":"Threat Explorer lets you search for all copies of an email and launch a bulk remediation (move, delete). Message trace only tracks, and a mail flow rule only acts on future emails.","a":["Threat Explorer in Defender for Office 365 (Plan 2)","Message trace in the Exchange admin center, then deletion mailbox by mailbox","A mail flow (transport) rule that deletes this message"]},
  "Tu reçois un mail « de la DSI » qui te demande de confirmer ton mot de passe via un lien. Quel est le bon réflexe dans Outlook ? ¦ Cliquer sur le lien pour vérifier s'il est vrai": {"q":"You receive an email “from IT” asking you to confirm your password via a link. What is the right reflex in Outlook?","e":"Outlook's “Report” button sends the message to the security team (and to Microsoft depending on the configuration) and removes it from your mailbox. Replying or clicking confirms to the attacker that your address is active.","a":["Click the link to check whether it is genuine","Use the “Report” button then choose “Report phishing”","Reply to the sender to ask whether it is legitimate","Simply move it to a “To check” folder"]},
  "Quand tu repères un mail d'hameçonnage, le mieux est de le transférer à tous tes collègues pour les prévenir. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"When you spot a phishing email, the best thing to do is forward it to all your colleagues to warn them.","e":"Forwarding a booby-trapped email spreads it and risks a colleague clicking. Report it with the “Report” button: the security team can then remove it from all mailboxes."},
  "Un client t'assure avoir envoyé un mail, mais il n'est ni dans ta boîte de réception ni dans le courrier indésirable. Où peut-il être ? ¦ Dans le dossier Archive, classé par Outlook": {"q":"A customer assures you they sent an email, but it is neither in your inbox nor in your junk email folder. Where could it be?","e":"Messages deemed suspicious (spam, phishing, malware) can be placed in quarantine by Microsoft 365 instead of being delivered. Depending on your company's policy, you can view them in the quarantine portal or request their release.","a":["In the Archive folder, filed by Outlook","In your calendar, if it mentioned an appointment","In quarantine, held by the security filters","In your drafts, waiting to be read"]},
  "Tu appliques l'étiquette « Confidentiel » à un document Word. Qu'est-ce que ça peut faire, selon la configuration de ton entreprise ? ¦ Le protéger (chiffrement, droits) même s'il sort de l'entreprise": {"q":"You apply the “Confidential” label to a Word document. What can this do, depending on your company's configuration?","e":"A Microsoft Purview sensitivity label can add a header or watermark and encrypt the file: the protection travels with the document, wherever it is copied.","a":["Protect it (encryption, permissions) even if it leaves the company","Automatically delete it after 30 days on OneDrive","Prevent only printing, and only from your device","Nothing, it is just a color displayed in File Explorer"]},
  "Tu cliques sur un lien dans un mail et une page Microsoft t'indique que le site a été classé comme malveillant. Que s'est-il passé ? ¦ Ton navigateur est mal configuré et bloque tous les liens externes": {"q":"You click a link in an email and a Microsoft page tells you the site has been classified as malicious. What happened?","e":"Defender for Office 365 checks links when you click, not only on receipt: a site that turned malicious after the email was sent is therefore blocked. Do not try to bypass the warning; notify support instead.","a":["Your browser is misconfigured and blocks all external links","The site is under maintenance at its host for a few hours","Your account was suspended by the administrator after a click","Safe Links blocked the address at the moment of the click"]},
  "Quels indices doivent te faire soupçonner un mail d'hameçonnage ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Un ton urgent ou menaçant (« ton compte sera fermé aujourd'hui »)": {"q":"Which clues should make you suspect a phishing email? (several answers)","e":"Urgency, an imitated domain and a misleading link are classic signals. A logo can be copied in two seconds: it is never proof of authenticity.","a":["An urgent or threatening tone (“your account will be closed today”)","A sender address that imitates a known domain with one letter changed","A signature with the company's official logo","A link whose real address, when hovered over, does not match the displayed text"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre les étapes pour signaler un mail suspect dans Outlook : ¦ Sélectionner le mail suspect sans cliquer sur ses liens ni ses pièces jointes": {"q":"Put the steps for reporting a suspicious email in Outlook in the right order:","e":"The report goes to the security team and the message is removed from your mailbox. Above all, do not open links or attachments before reporting.","items":["Select the suspicious email without clicking its links or attachments","Click the “Report” button on the ribbon","Choose “Report phishing”","Confirm sending the report"]},
  "Quel est le nom du bouton intégré à Outlook qui permet de déclarer un mail comme hameçonnage ou courrier indésirable ? ¦ Signaler": {"q":"What is the name of the built-in Outlook button used to report an email as phishing or junk?","e":"The “Report” button is built into the Outlook ribbon (new Outlook, Outlook on the web, classic Outlook). It replaces the old reporting add-ins.","placeholder":"Button name","answers":["Signaler","Report","Signaler le message","Report message"]},
  "Dans Outlook, tu choisis « Chiffrer » puis « Ne pas transférer » avant d'envoyer un mail. Que peut faire le destinataire ? ¦ Le transférer à qui il veut, mais chiffré": {"q":"In Outlook, you choose “Encrypt” then “Do Not Forward” before sending an email. What can the recipient do?","e":"The “Do Not Forward” option encrypts the message and prevents the recipient from forwarding it, printing it or copying its content. The “Encrypt” option alone protects the message without these restrictions.","a":["Forward it to anyone they want, but encrypted","Read it, but not forward it, print it or copy its content","Read it only for 24 hours","Nothing, they must first install a special application"]},
  "Le bandeau « Vous ne recevez pas souvent de courrier de… » en haut d'un mail t'avertit que tu échanges peut-être pour la première fois avec cet expéditeur. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"The banner “You don't often get email from…” at the top of an email warns you that you may be corresponding with this sender for the first time.","e":"This is the first-contact safety tip. It does not say the email is dangerous, but invites you to verify the sender, especially if the request is unusual."},
  "En rédigeant un mail contenant un numéro de carte bancaire, un bandeau t'avertit que le message contient des informations sensibles. D'où vient ce message ? ¦ De l'Éditeur Microsoft intégré à Outlook": {"q":"While writing an email containing a credit card number, a banner warns you that the message contains sensitive information. Where does this message come from?","e":"It is a DLP (data loss prevention) policy tip from Microsoft Purview: it warns you before sending. Depending on the configuration, the email may be blocked or sent with a justification.","a":["From Microsoft Editor built into Outlook","From an alert from the antivirus installed on your device","From a DLP policy defined by your company","From the recipient's server spam filter"]},
  "Tu reçois un mail dont la pièce jointe est remplacée par un message indiquant qu'elle est en cours d'analyse. Que faut-il faire ? ¦ Patienter : la vraie pièce jointe arrivera si l'analyse la juge sûre": {"q":"You receive an email whose attachment is replaced by a message saying it is being scanned. What should you do?","e":"This is Safe Attachments “Dynamic Delivery”: the email body arrives immediately and the attachment is reinserted once the scan is complete. If it is malicious, it will not be delivered to you.","a":["Wait: the real attachment will arrive if the scan deems it safe","Ask the sender to resend it as a ZIP file","Forward the email to your personal mailbox to open it","Delete the email, it is necessarily dangerous"]},
  "Un utilisateur veut passer un document de « Confidentiel » à « Général » et Word lui demande une justification. Pourquoi ? ¦ Son abonnement ne lui permet pas de retirer une étiquette appliquée": {"q":"A user wants to change a document from “Confidential” to “General” and Word asks them for a justification. Why?","e":"The label publishing policy can require a justification to remove a label or replace it with a less restrictive one. This action is recorded in the audit log.","a":["Their subscription does not allow them to remove an applied label","The document is read-only in their OneDrive space","Word requires a justification for every change to the file","The labeling policy requires a justification to lower the level"]},
  "Word refuse d'enregistrer un nouveau document tant que l'utilisateur n'a pas choisi d'étiquette de confidentialité. Quel paramètre de stratégie est en cause ? ¦ L'étiquetage automatique côté service": {"q":"Word refuses to save a new document until the user has chosen a sensitivity label. Which policy setting is responsible?","e":"With mandatory labeling, the user must choose a label before saving or sending. A default label, on the other hand, would be applied automatically without asking anything.","a":["Service-side auto-labeling","Mandatory labeling","The default label","Double key encryption"]},
  "Appliquer une étiquette de confidentialité à une équipe Teams (étiquette de conteneur) étiquette automatiquement tous les fichiers stockés dans cette équipe. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Applying a sensitivity label to a Teams team (container label) automatically labels all the files stored in that team.","e":"A container label controls group or site settings (public/private privacy, external sharing, access from unmanaged devices), but does not label the files it contains."},
  "Où les liens fiables (Safe Links) de Defender pour Office 365 peuvent-ils protéger les clics ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Dans les mails reçus dans Outlook": {"q":"Where can Safe Links in Defender for Office 365 protect clicks? (several answers)","e":"Safe Links covers email, Teams and supported Office apps, depending on the policy. Text messages on a personal phone do not go through Microsoft 365.","a":["In emails received in Outlook","In Microsoft Teams chats and channels","In text messages received on a personal phone","In supported Office apps (Word, Excel, PowerPoint…)"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre le parcours d'un utilisateur qui récupère un mail légitime placé en quarantaine (stratégie autorisant la demande de libération) : ¦ Recevoir la notification de quarantaine ou ouvrir le portail de quarantaine": {"q":"Put in order the steps a user follows to retrieve a legitimate email placed in quarantine (policy allowing release requests):","e":"Depending on the quarantine policy, the user can release the message themselves or only request its release; in the latter case, an administrator approves before delivery.","items":["Receive the quarantine notification or open the quarantine portal","Find the message and check its sender and subject","Click “Request release”","The administrator reviews and approves the request","The message is delivered to the inbox"]},
  "À quelle adresse un utilisateur peut-il consulter ses messages mis en quarantaine par Microsoft 365 ? ¦ https://security.microsoft.com/quarantine": {"q":"At which address can a user view their messages quarantined by Microsoft 365?","e":"The Quarantine page of the Microsoft Defender portal shows users their own held messages; they do not see other people's.","placeholder":"https://…","answers":["https://security.microsoft.com/quarantine","security.microsoft.com/quarantine","https://security.microsoft.com/quarantine/"]},
  "Un utilisateur voit en quarantaine un mail classé « logiciel malveillant » mais ne peut ni le libérer ni en demander la libération. Pourquoi ? ¦ Sa boîte aux lettres est pleine et ne peut plus recevoir ce message": {"q":"A user sees in quarantine an email classified as “malware” but can neither release it nor request its release. Why?","e":"The default quarantine policy for malware (AdminOnlyAccessPolicy) reserves release for administrators. The same applies by default to high confidence phishing.","a":["Their mailbox is full and can no longer receive this message","They must first report the email as “not junk” in Outlook","By default, only admins can release malware from quarantine","Quarantined messages remain read-only for everyone, admins included"]},
  "Un mail légitime atterrit régulièrement dans le courrier indésirable d'un utilisateur. Que doit-il faire en priorité dans Outlook ? ¦ Utiliser « Signaler » puis « Non indésirable » sur ce message": {"q":"A legitimate email regularly lands in a user's junk email folder. What should they do first in Outlook?","e":"The “Not junk” report moves the message and sends a false positive back to the security team and Microsoft, which helps correct the filtering.","a":["Use “Report” then “Not junk” on this message","Turn off the Junk Email folder","Create a rule that deletes the sender's emails","Ask the sender to change their email address"]},
  "Dans Outlook, la photo de l'expéditeur est remplacée par un point d'interrogation. Qu'est-ce que ça indique ? ¦ L'expéditeur n'a pas encore ajouté de photo à son profil": {"q":"In Outlook, the sender's photo is replaced by a question mark. What does this indicate?","e":"The “?” indicates an unverified sender: the message did not pass the authentication checks. It is not necessarily an attack, but you should be extra careful.","a":["The sender has not yet added a photo to their profile","The email contains an attachment that Defender has not scanned","The sender is on your blocked senders list","Microsoft 365 could not authenticate the sender (SPF, DKIM, DMARC)"]},
  "Tu veux améliorer le Secure Score de ton organisation. Où trouves-tu la liste des mesures recommandées ? ¦ Dans le centre d'administration Exchange, onglet « Flux de courrier »": {"q":"You want to improve your organization's Secure Score. Where do you find the list of recommended actions?","e":"Each recommended action shows the points it earns, its impact on users and the implementation steps.","a":["In the Exchange admin center, “Mail flow” tab","In the “Recommended actions” tab of Secure Score (Defender portal)","In the privacy settings of each Office app","In Windows Event Viewer, Security log"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet permet de se connecter à Security & Compliance PowerShell (Microsoft Purview) avec le module ExchangeOnlineManagement ? ¦ Connect-IPPSSession": {"q":"Which cmdlet connects you to Security & Compliance PowerShell (Microsoft Purview) with the ExchangeOnlineManagement module?","e":"Connect-IPPSSession opens a session to Security & Compliance PowerShell (compliance searches, labels, DLP…). Connect-ExchangeOnline, on the other hand, connects to Exchange Online.","placeholder":"Cmdlet name","answers":["Connect-IPPSSession"]},
  "Tu veux appliquer rapidement la configuration recommandée par Microsoft pour l'anti-spam, l'anti-hameçonnage, Safe Links et Safe Attachments, sans régler chaque stratégie à la main. Tu utilises… ¦ Des règles de flux de courrier Exchange appliquées à tout le tenant": {"q":"You want to quickly apply Microsoft's recommended configuration for anti-spam, anti-phishing, Safe Links and Safe Attachments, without setting each policy by hand. You use…","e":"Preset security policies (Standard and Strict) apply the recommended settings and are updated by Microsoft. Secure Score only recommends actions. Built-in protection enables Safe Links and Safe Attachments by default for Defender for Office 365 licenses.","a":["Exchange mail flow rules applied to the whole tenant","The improvement actions in the Secure Score report","The Standard or Strict preset security policies","The Tenant Allow/Block List (TABL)"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la création d'une stratégie DLP dans le portail Microsoft Purview : ¦ Choisir un modèle (ex. données financières) ou une stratégie personnalisée": {"q":"Put in order the creation of a DLP policy in the Microsoft Purview portal:","e":"Starting in simulation mode lets you measure the impact (false positives) before actually blocking users.","items":["Choose a template (e.g. financial data) or a custom policy","Name the policy and define its scope","Select the locations (Exchange, SharePoint, OneDrive, Teams…)","Define the rules: conditions, actions and policy tips","Run in simulation mode, analyze, then turn on"]},
  "Quelles affirmations sur les stratégies d'étiquetage automatique côté service (Microsoft Purview) sont vraies ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Elles peuvent être exécutées d'abord en mode simulation": {"q":"Which statements about service-side auto-labeling policies (Microsoft Purview) are true? (several answers)","e":"Service-side auto-labeling runs in the cloud, on data at rest and emails in transit, without the user opening anything. It is client-side labeling that acts during editing in Office apps.","a":["They can be run in simulation mode first","They apply to Exchange, SharePoint and OneDrive locations","They only work if the user opens the file in an Office app","They label data at rest without any user action"]},
  "Dans Microsoft Secure Score, quels statuts d'une action d'amélioration te rapportent quand même les points sans l'appliquer via le contrôle Microsoft ? ¦ « Résolu par un tiers » et « Résolu par une atténuation alternative »": {"q":"In Microsoft Secure Score, which improvement action statuses still earn you the points without applying it through the Microsoft control?","e":"If a third-party solution or another measure covers the risk, these statuses award the points. “Risk accepted” earns none, and “Planned” only tracks the action.","a":["“Resolved through third party” and “Resolved through alternate mitigation”","“Planned” and “To address”","“Risk accepted” only","None: only controls detected by Microsoft count"]},
  "Avec Audit (Standard) de Microsoft Purview, combien de temps les enregistrements d'audit sont-ils conservés par défaut ? ¦ 30 jours": {"q":"With Microsoft Purview Audit (Standard), how long are audit records kept by default?","e":"Since late 2023, Audit (Standard) keeps records for 180 days. Audit (Premium) goes further (one year by default for some workloads, up to 10 years with an add-on).","a":["30 days","90 days","180 days","10 years"]},
  "Search-UnifiedAuditLog ne renvoie aucun résultat et Get-AdminAuditLogConfig affiche UnifiedAuditLogIngestionEnabled à False. Quelle commande corrige le problème ? ¦ Set-OrganizationConfig -UnifiedAuditLogIngestionEnabled $true": {"q":"Search-UnifiedAuditLog returns no results and Get-AdminAuditLogConfig shows UnifiedAuditLogIngestionEnabled as False. Which command fixes the problem?","e":"Set-AdminAuditLogConfig -UnifiedAuditLogIngestionEnabled $true, run in Exchange Online PowerShell, enables ingestion into the unified audit log. This parameter does not exist on Set-OrganizationConfig, whose -AuditDisabled only manages mailbox auditing at the organization level. Set-Mailbox -AuditEnabled only concerns auditing of a single mailbox.","a":["Set-OrganizationConfig -UnifiedAuditLogIngestionEnabled $true","Set-AdminAuditLogConfig -UnifiedAuditLogIngestionEnabled $true","Set-OrganizationConfig -AuditDisabled $false","Get-Mailbox | Set-Mailbox -AuditEnabled $true"]},
  "Un même document est couvert par plusieurs stratégies de rétention Microsoft Purview contradictoires. Quels principes de résolution s'appliquent ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ La rétention l'emporte sur la suppression": {"q":"The same document is covered by several conflicting Microsoft Purview retention policies. Which resolution principles apply? (several answers)","e":"The retention principles are ranked: retention before deletion, longest retention, explicit inclusion over implicit, then shortest deletion period. The policy's creation date plays no role.","a":["Retention wins over deletion","The longest retention period wins","An explicit scope wins over an implicit scope","The most recently created policy wins"]},
  "En chasse avancée (Microsoft Defender XDR), quelle table KQL contient les informations sur l'envoi et la livraison des mails (expéditeur, destinataire, verdict, action de livraison) ? ¦ EmailEvents": {"q":"In advanced hunting (Microsoft Defender XDR), which KQL table contains information about email sending and delivery (sender, recipient, verdict, delivery action)?","e":"EmailEvents gathers the email events processed by Defender for Office 365. The EmailUrlInfo, EmailAttachmentInfo and EmailPostDeliveryEvents tables complete the details on links, attachments and post-delivery actions (ZAP, remediation).","placeholder":"Table name","answers":["EmailEvents"]},
  "Tu dois bloquer une URL malveillante pour tout le locataire via la liste d'autorisation/blocage du locataire en PowerShell. Quelle commande utilises-tu ? ¦ Set-AtpPolicyForO365 -Identity Default -BlockUrls <url>": {"q":"You need to block a malicious URL for the entire tenant using the Tenant Allow/Block List in PowerShell. Which command do you use?","e":"New-TenantAllowBlockListItems manages the Tenant Allow/Block List (URLs, senders, files). The old BlockUrls list of Set-AtpPolicyForO365 has been abandoned in favor of this list.","a":["Set-AtpPolicyForO365 -Identity Default -BlockUrls <url>","New-SafeLinksPolicy -Name BlocageURL -BlockedUrls <url>","Set-HostedContentFilterPolicy -Identity Default -BlockedUrls <url>","New-TenantAllowBlockListItems -ListType Url -Block -Entries <url>"]},
  "Une fois qu'un élément est marqué comme enregistrement réglementaire par une étiquette de rétention, même un administrateur général ne peut plus retirer l'étiquette de cet élément. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Once an item is marked as a regulatory record by a retention label, even a Global Administrator can no longer remove the label from that item.","e":"This is what distinguishes a regulatory record from a simple record: the label can no longer be removed and its retention period cannot be shortened. Microsoft recommends testing before using it, because it is irreversible."},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la purge d'un mail malveillant dans toutes les boîtes via Security & Compliance PowerShell : ¦ Connect-IPPSSession -EnableSearchOnlySession": {"q":"Put in order the purge of a malicious email from all mailboxes via Security & Compliance PowerShell:","e":"Since ExchangeOnlineManagement module 3.9.0, these cmdlets require a session opened with -EnableSearchOnlySession. Always check the number of items found before purging, because an overly broad query would delete legitimate emails. -PurgeType SoftDelete leaves items recoverable by the user, HardDelete does not. The purge removes at most 10 items per mailbox.","items":["Connect-IPPSSession -EnableSearchOnlySession","New-ComplianceSearch with -ExchangeLocation All and a precise -ContentMatchQuery","Start-ComplianceSearch","Check the results with Get-ComplianceSearch","New-ComplianceSearchAction -Purge -PurgeType HardDelete"]},
  "Où discute-t-on avec toute son équipe autour d'un projet ? ¦ Dans un canal de l'équipe Teams": {"q":"Where do you chat with your whole team about a project?","e":"The channel keeps the project's conversations, files and meetings in one place, visible to the whole team.","a":["In a Teams team channel","In an Outlook distribution list","Around the coffee machine, hoping everyone drops by"]},
  "Quelle application gère ton agenda et tes invitations de réunion ? ¦ Microsoft To Do": {"q":"Which application manages your calendar and meeting invitations?","e":"Outlook combines email and calendar. Teams meetings are also scheduled there.","a":["Microsoft To Do","Microsoft Planner","Outlook"]},
  "Pour interpeller directement quelqu'un dans un message Teams : ¦ J'utilise # suivi de son nom": {"q":"To address someone directly in a Teams message:","e":"The @ mention sends the person a notification. @team or @channel notifies everyone, to be used sparingly.","a":["I use # followed by their name","I use @ followed by their name","I write their name three times, like Beetlejuice"]},
  "Le message d'absence se configure dans Outlook, via les réponses automatiques. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"The out-of-office message is set up in Outlook, through automatic replies.","e":"True: Settings, then Automatic replies. You can set a different message for your external contacts."},
  "Un fichier posté dans un canal Teams est stocké… ¦ Dans le OneDrive de celui qui l'a posté": {"q":"A file posted in a Teams channel is stored…","e":"Channel = the team's SharePoint. Channel messages are copied to the group's Exchange mailbox, but not the files. And a file sent in a private chat goes to the sender's OneDrive.","a":["In the OneDrive of the person who posted it","In the team's Exchange mailbox","In the team's SharePoint site"]},
  "Tu veux que les mails d'un client arrivent tout seuls dans un dossier dédié : ¦ Je crée une règle Outlook": {"q":"You want a client's emails to land automatically in a dedicated folder:","e":"A rule sorts automatically based on the sender, subject or keywords. Focused Inbox and categories, on the other hand, don't file anything into a folder.","a":["I create an Outlook rule","I turn on Focused Inbox","I add a color category"]},
  "Un collègue quitte le projet. Pour lui retirer l'accès aux fichiers de l'équipe : ¦ On le retire de la liste de distribution Outlook du projet": {"q":"A colleague is leaving the project. To remove their access to the team's files:","e":"Permissions follow group membership: removing them from the team removes their access to the associated SharePoint.","a":["Remove them from the project's Outlook distribution list","Remove them from the Teams team members","Hide the team in their Teams app"]},
  "Réunion avec des externes : où choisir qui peut contourner la salle d'attente ? ¦ Dans les options de la réunion": {"q":"Meeting with external participants: where do you choose who can bypass the lobby?","e":"Meeting options let you choose who enters directly, who can present, and lock the meeting.","a":["In the meeting options","In Teams Settings > Privacy","In the Teams team settings"]},
  "Dans les options d'une réunion Teams, l'organisateur peut… ¦ Choisir qui contourne la salle d'attente": {"q":"In the options of a Teams meeting, the organizer can…","e":"Meeting options manage access and roles. You can allow or block cameras, but you cannot force someone to turn theirs on.","a":["Choose who bypasses the lobby","Choose who can present","Allow or block participants' microphones","Force all participants to turn their camera on"]},
  "Le statut « Ne pas déranger » dans Teams… ¦ Coupe les notifications, sauf pour les contacts prioritaires": {"q":"The “Do not disturb” status in Teams…","e":"Handy for focusing or presenting: messages still arrive, you'll read them later.","a":["Mutes notifications, except for priority contacts","Makes you appear offline to your colleagues","Sends an automatic out-of-office reply to every message"]},
  "Pour retrouver facilement un mail à traiter plus tard dans Outlook : ¦ Je le supprime, je m'en souviendrai bien": {"q":"To easily find an email to deal with later in Outlook:","e":"The flag adds the email to your task list, with a due date if you want.","a":["I delete it, I'll remember it","I move it to the Archive folder","I mark it with a flag"]},
  "On peut toujours rappeler un mail envoyé dans Outlook, même lu et même envoyé à l'extérieur. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"You can always recall a sent email in Outlook, even if it has been read and even if it was sent externally.","e":"False: recall only works in certain cases, generally with recipients in the same organization. It is better to reread before sending, or to enable an undo-send delay."},
  "Tu écris à 30 clients qui ne se connaissent pas. Tu mets leurs adresses en… ¦ À, séparées par des points-virgules": {"q":"You are writing to 30 clients who don't know each other. You put their addresses in…","e":"With Bcc (blind carbon copy), everyone receives the email without seeing the other addresses: this is more respectful of their personal data (GDPR). In To as in Cc, all addresses are visible to everyone.","a":["To, separated by semicolons","Cc, to keep everyone informed","Bcc, with your own address in To"]},
  "Dans Teams, la différence entre une conversation et un canal ? ¦ Conversation : limitée à deux personnes ; canal : sans limite de membres": {"q":"In Teams, what is the difference between a chat and a channel?","e":"Chat for exchanging quickly between two or a few people. Channel so the whole team can follow a topic, with its files and history.","a":["Chat: limited to two people; channel: no limit on members","Chat: directly between people; channel: a team, organized by topic","Chat: deleted after 30 days; channel: history kept"]},
  "Une réunion Teams hors canal est enregistrée. Où se trouve l'enregistrement ? ¦ Dans le OneDrive de la personne qui a cliqué sur Enregistrer": {"q":"A Teams meeting held outside a channel is recorded. Where is the recording?","e":"For a regular meeting, the recording goes to the organizer's OneDrive (Recordings folder), even if another participant clicked Record. For a channel meeting, it goes to the team's SharePoint; for a call (1:1 or group), to the OneDrive of the person who records.","a":["In the OneDrive of the person who clicked Record","In the OneDrive of the meeting organizer","In the SharePoint site of the organizer's team"]},
  "Quelles pratiques rendent une réunion plus efficace ? ¦ Envoyer un ordre du jour": {"q":"Which practices make a meeting more effective?","e":"A clear objective, the right people, written decisions. Inviting “just in case” wastes everyone's time, and a 25-minute meeting is often enough.","a":["Sending an agenda","Inviting only the people who are needed","Sharing minutes with the decisions","Inviting widely, in case someone has an opinion"]},
  "Tu veux qu'un mail parte demain à 8 h. Dans Outlook, tu utilises… ¦ La fonction « Planifier l'envoi » (ou « Différer la livraison »)": {"q":"You want an email to go out tomorrow at 8 a.m. In Outlook, you use…","e":"Handy to avoid sending emails late at night: the email goes out at the chosen time. A reminder alerts you, but sends nothing.","a":["The “Schedule send” feature (or “Delay delivery”)","A follow-up flag with a reminder tomorrow at 8 a.m.","Automatic replies, scheduled from 8 a.m."]},
  "Dans Teams, un « invité », par rapport à l'« accès externe » : ¦ L'accès externe ouvre les canaux et fichiers ; l'invité peut seulement discuter et appeler": {"q":"In Teams, a “guest” compared to “external access”:","e":"External access (federation) lets you communicate with people from other organizations. The guest, on the other hand, has a guest account in your tenant and works inside the team.","a":["External access opens channels and files; the guest can only chat and call","The guest joins a team (channels, files); external access is for chatting and calling","The guest consumes a license from your tenant; external access consumes none"]},
  "Pour garder une conversation Teams importante tout en haut de ta liste : ¦ Je l'épingle": {"q":"To keep an important Teams chat at the very top of your list:","e":"Right-click (or “…”) the chat, then “Pin”. It stays at the top, even when other messages come in.","a":["I pin it","I mark it as unread","I rename it “DO NOT FORGET”"]},
  "En réunion Teams, « lever la main » sert à… ¦ Prouver que tu es encore réveillé": {"q":"In a Teams meeting, “raising your hand” is used to…","e":"The organizer sees the order of raised hands and can give everyone the floor in turn. Very useful in large meetings.","a":["Prove that you're still awake","Ask to speak without interrupting","Report a sound problem to the organizer"]},
  "En réunion Teams, on peut flouter ou remplacer son arrière-plan. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In a Teams meeting, you can blur or replace your background.","e":"True: handy when working from home to protect your privacy… and to avoid showing a whiteboard full of confidential information!"},
  "Équipe Teams publique ou privée : quelle différence ? ¦ Publique : ouverte aux invités externes ; privée : aux seuls internes": {"q":"Public or private Teams team: what's the difference?","e":"“Public” means open to the whole organization, never to the Internet. For a sensitive project, choose a private team.","a":["Public: open to external guests; private: internal people only","Public: any colleague can join; private: by invitation or approval","Public: created by the IT department; private: created by a user"]},
  "Un canal privé dans une équipe Teams permet… ¦ De réserver un canal à une partie des membres de l'équipe": {"q":"A private channel in a Teams team lets you…","e":"Only the members added to the private channel can see its messages and files, which have their own SharePoint site. Other team members can't see it.","a":["Reserve a channel for some of the team's members","Chat with people outside the organization without an account","Hide the entire team from other colleagues"]},
  "Les salles pour petits groupes, dans une réunion Teams, servent à… ¦ Diviser les participants en sous-groupes de travail": {"q":"Breakout rooms in a Teams meeting are used to…","e":"The organizer assigns participants, sets a duration, then calls everyone back to the main meeting.","a":["Split participants into working subgroups","Book a physical meeting room equipped with Teams","Gather participants on screen in Together mode"]},
  "Dans Outlook, la boîte de réception « Prioritaire »… ¦ Remonte en haut les mails marqués d'un indicateur (drapeau)": {"q":"In Outlook, the “Focused” inbox…","e":"Outlook learns from your habits. You can correct it by moving a message to “Focused” or “Other”.","a":["Moves messages marked with a flag to the top","Automatically sorts important messages apart from the others","Groups messages from the same thread into a single conversation"]},
  "Quelles pratiques rendent tes mails plus efficaces ? ¦ Un objet clair et précis": {"q":"Which practices make your emails more effective?","e":"A good subject line is easy to find later, and one topic per email avoids endless threads. Copying the whole department floods inboxes: target your recipients.","a":["A clear, precise subject line","One topic per email","“Reply all” only when it's useful","Copying the whole department to keep a record"]},
  "Ton assistante doit gérer tes rendez-vous dans Outlook. Tu… ¦ Lui partages ton calendrier en lecture seule": {"q":"Your assistant needs to manage your appointments in Outlook. You…","e":"Delegation grants specific rights (read, edit, respond to invitations) without ever sharing credentials. Read-only sharing doesn't let them manage your appointments.","a":["Share your calendar with them as read-only","Give them delegate access to your calendar","Create a rule that forwards your invitations to them"]},
  "Les messages d'une conversation privée Teams sont visibles par tous les membres de l'équipe. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Messages in a private Teams chat are visible to all members of the team.","e":"False: a private chat only involves its participants. Channels, on the other hand, are visible to team members."},
  "Où sont stockés les fichiers partagés dans une conversation privée Teams (hors canal) ? ¦ Dans le site SharePoint de l'équipe": {"q":"Where are files shared in a private Teams chat (outside a channel) stored?","e":"In a chat, the file is placed in the “Microsoft Teams Chat Files” folder of the sender's OneDrive, with sharing granted to the participants. In a channel, it goes to the team's SharePoint.","a":["In the team's SharePoint site","In the OneDrive of the person who shared them","In the recipient's Exchange mailbox"]},
  "Un canal partagé Teams permet… ¦ D'inviter des personnes d'une autre organisation dans un seul canal, sans toute l'équipe": {"q":"A Teams shared channel lets you…","e":"Shared channels (Teams Connect) rely on Entra ID B2B direct connect: the external user stays in their own tenant and only accesses that channel.","a":["Invite people from another organization into a single channel, without the whole team","Open a channel to personal Microsoft accounts, without creating a guest account","Duplicate a channel across several teams, each with its own files"]},
  "En réunion Teams sur Windows, quel raccourci coupe ou réactive ton micro ? ¦ Ctrl+Maj+O": {"q":"In a Teams meeting on Windows, which shortcut mutes or unmutes your microphone?","e":"Ctrl+Shift+M mutes or unmutes the microphone without hunting for the button. Ctrl+Shift+O does the same for the camera, and Ctrl+Shift+K raises or lowers your hand.","a":["Ctrl+Shift+O","Ctrl+Shift+K","Ctrl+Shift+M"]},
  "Dans Teams, on peut programmer l'envoi d'un message de conversation à une date et une heure précises. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"In Teams, you can schedule a chat message to be sent at a specific date and time.","e":"True: right-click (or long-press) the Send button, then “Schedule send”. Handy so you don't disturb a colleague outside their working hours."},
  "Tu veux éviter la prolifération d'équipes Teams dans le tenant. Quelles mesures existent vraiment ? ¦ Réserver la création des groupes Microsoft 365 à un groupe de sécurité": {"q":"You want to prevent Teams sprawl in the tenant. Which measures actually exist?","e":"Every team is built on a Microsoft 365 group: so creation, expiration and naming are restricted at the group level (Entra ID). There is no “one team per person” quota.","a":["Restrict Microsoft 365 group creation to a security group","Apply an expiration policy to Microsoft 365 groups","Enforce a group naming policy (prefix, suffix, blocked words)","Limit each user to a single team in the Teams admin center"]},
  "Tu crées un événement dans le calendrier Outlook et tu veux que les invités puissent le rejoindre en visio. Tu… ¦ actives l'option « Réunion Teams » dans l'invitation": {"q":"You create an event in your Outlook calendar and want guests to be able to join it by video. You…","e":"The “Teams meeting” button in an Outlook invitation automatically generates the join link. Typing “Teams” in the location doesn't create any online meeting.","a":["turn on the “Teams meeting” option in the invitation","attach a Teams file to the invitation","add “Teams” in the Location field","send the link to your Teams profile separately"]},
  "Quelle cmdlet du module MicrosoftTeams attribue une stratégie de réunion à un utilisateur ? ¦ Grant-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy": {"q":"Which cmdlet of the MicrosoftTeams module assigns a meeting policy to a user?","e":"Teams policies are assigned with Grant-Cs… cmdlets; Set-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy changes the content of a policy, not its assignment.","placeholder":"Verb-Noun of the cmdlet","answers":["Grant-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy"]},
  "Dans le Centre d'administration Teams, où autorises-tu ou interdis-tu l'enregistrement des réunions pour un groupe d'utilisateurs ? ¦ Paramètres à l'échelle de l'organisation > Paramètres Teams": {"q":"In the Teams admin center, where do you allow or prevent meeting recording for a group of users?","e":"Cloud recording is a meeting policy setting, which you then assign to users or groups.","a":["Org-wide settings > Teams settings","Meetings > Meeting policies","Users > External access","Teams apps > Setup policies"]},
  "Tes utilisateurs ne doivent plus pouvoir discuter dans Teams avec les comptes d'un domaine partenaire précis. Tu vas dans… ¦ Réunions > Paramètres de réunion": {"q":"Your users must no longer be able to chat in Teams with accounts from a specific partner domain. You go to…","e":"External access (federation) in the Teams admin center lets you allow or block specific domains. Entra ID's external collaboration settings concern B2B guests, not Teams federation.","a":["Meetings > Meeting settings","Microsoft Entra ID > External collaboration settings","Users > External access, and you block that domain","Teams apps > Manage apps"]},
  "Une stratégie de configuration d'applications Teams permet d'installer et d'épingler des applications dans la barre latérale Teams des utilisateurs. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"A Teams app setup policy lets you install and pin apps in users' Teams sidebar.","e":"Setup policies (Teams apps > Setup policies) are used to preinstall and pin apps, and to set their order in the sidebar."},
  "Quels types de stratégies se gèrent dans le Centre d'administration Teams ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Stratégies de réunion": {"q":"Which types of policies are managed in the Teams admin center? (several answers)","e":"Meetings, messaging and app setup are Teams policies. Conditional Access is configured in Microsoft Entra ID, not in the Teams admin center.","a":["Meeting policies","Conditional Access policies","Messaging policies","App setup policies"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la création d'une équipe en PowerShell : ¦ Install-Module MicrosoftTeams": {"q":"Put the steps for creating a team in PowerShell in order:","e":"You install the module, connect to the tenant, create the team (New-Team returns its GroupId), then add members with Add-TeamUser.","items":["Install-Module MicrosoftTeams","Connect-MicrosoftTeams","New-Team -DisplayName \"Projet Alpha\"","Add-TeamUser -GroupId <id> -User <UPN>"]},
  "Ta conformité exige de conserver les messages des canaux Teams pendant plusieurs années. Tu crées… ¦ une stratégie de messagerie Teams qui interdit la suppression des messages": {"q":"Your compliance requirements call for retaining Teams channel messages for several years. You create…","e":"Retaining Teams messages is done with Microsoft Purview retention policies, with dedicated locations for channel messages and chats. A messaging policy doesn't prevent deletion on the compliance side.","a":["a Teams messaging policy that prevents message deletion","an Exchange transport rule that archives Teams messages","a Microsoft 365 group expiration policy set to 5 years","a Purview retention policy on the “Teams channel messages” location"]},
  "Un utilisateur se plaint d'une réunion Teams hachée hier. Où analyses-tu cette réunion précise ? ¦ Centre d'administration Teams > Utilisateurs > fiche de l'utilisateur > Réunions et appels": {"q":"A user complains about a choppy Teams meeting yesterday. Where do you analyze that specific meeting?","e":"Call analytics, on the user's page, details each meeting (network, devices, audio). Service health only shows global Microsoft incidents.","a":["Teams admin center > Users > the user's page > Meetings & calls","Microsoft Purview > Audit > Search the audit log","Microsoft 365 admin center > Health > Service health","Exchange admin center > Mail flow > Message trace"]},
  "Tu veux que quelques utilisateurs pilotes voient les fonctionnalités Teams en préversion publique. Tu utilises… ¦ une stratégie de réunion dédiée": {"q":"You want a few pilot users to see Teams features in public preview. You use…","e":"Teams update policies (Teams > Teams update policies) let you enable public preview access for targeted users.","a":["a dedicated meeting policy","a Teams update policy","a Teams Premium license","the Microsoft 365 Apps Monthly Enterprise Channel"]},
  "Quel paramètre de Set-CsTeamsMessagingPolicy empêche les utilisateurs de modifier leurs messages envoyés ? ¦ -AllowOwnerDeleteMessage $false": {"q":"Which parameter of Set-CsTeamsMessagingPolicy prevents users from editing their sent messages?","e":"AllowUserEditMessage controls editing of sent messages. AllowOwnerDeleteMessage concerns owners deleting other people's messages, and AllowUserChat turns off private chat altogether.","a":["-AllowOwnerDeleteMessage $false","-AllowEditMessage $false","-AllowUserEditMessage $false","-AllowUserChat $false"]},
  "Tu attribues une stratégie Teams à un groupe avec Grant-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy -Group. Quel paramètre fixe la priorité en cas de conflit entre groupes ? ¦ -Rank": {"q":"You assign a Teams policy to a group with Grant-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy -Group. Which parameter sets the priority when groups conflict?","e":"-Rank defines the priority of the group assignment: if a user belongs to several groups, the policy with the highest-priority rank (1) applies.","placeholder":"Parameter name","answers":["-Rank","Rank"]},
  "Si un utilisateur a une stratégie de réunion attribuée directement et une autre héritée d'un groupe, c'est la stratégie attribuée directement qui s'applique. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"If a user has a meeting policy assigned directly and another inherited from a group, the directly assigned policy applies.","e":"Direct assignment always wins over group inheritance, which itself wins over the global (organization-wide default) policy."},
  "Tu dois attribuer une stratégie Teams à une longue liste d'utilisateurs (sans groupe), en une opération asynchrone suivie. Tu utilises… ¦ Grant-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy -Global": {"q":"You need to assign a Teams policy to a long list of users (without a group), in a single tracked asynchronous operation. You use…","e":"New-CsBatchPolicyAssignmentOperation assigns a policy to a list of identities and returns an operation ID to track with Get-CsBatchPolicyAssignmentOperation. New-CsGroupPolicyAssignment requires a group, and -Global changes the tenant default.","a":["Grant-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy -Global","Invoke-CsBulkPolicyAssignment","New-CsGroupPolicyAssignment","New-CsBatchPolicyAssignmentOperation"]},
  "Réglementation oblige : le service Recherche et le service Ventes ne doivent jamais pouvoir se contacter dans Teams. La solution adaptée : ¦ Bloquer les deux services dans l'accès externe": {"q":"Because of regulations, the Research department and the Sales department must never be able to contact each other in Teams. The right solution:","e":"Information Barriers prevent communication and collaboration between segments of internal users. External access only concerns other organizations.","a":["Block both departments in external access","Microsoft Purview Information Barriers","A DLP policy on Teams chats","Two messaging policies that disable chat"]},
  "Pour la conformité (eDiscovery, rétention), où Microsoft 365 stocke-t-il ces données Teams ? (plusieurs réponses) ¦ Messages de conversation privée : boîtes aux lettres des participants": {"q":"For compliance (eDiscovery, retention), where does Microsoft 365 store this Teams data? (several answers)","e":"Teams messages are copied into Exchange mailboxes (participants' for chats, the group's for standard channels), and channel files live in SharePoint. OneDrive is used for files shared in chats, not for channel messages.","a":["Private chat messages: the participants' mailboxes","Standard channel messages: the team's Microsoft 365 group mailbox","Standard channel files: the team's SharePoint site","Standard channel messages: the team owner's OneDrive"]},
  "Quel paramètre de Set-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy règle l'expiration automatique des nouveaux enregistrements de réunion ? ¦ -NewMeetingRecordingExpirationDays": {"q":"Which parameter of Set-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy sets the automatic expiration of new meeting recordings?","e":"NewMeetingRecordingExpirationDays sets the number of days before recordings stored in OneDrive/SharePoint expire (-1 to never expire). AllowCloudRecordingForCalls concerns recording calls, AllowRecordingStorageOutsideRegion the storage location; MeetingRecordingRetentionDays doesn't exist.","a":["-NewMeetingRecordingExpirationDays","-MeetingRecordingRetentionDays","-AllowCloudRecordingForCalls","-AllowRecordingStorageOutsideRegion"]},
  "Remets dans l'ordre la mise en place des obstacles aux informations : ¦ Définir les segments avec New-OrganizationSegment": {"q":"Put the steps for setting up information barriers in order:","e":"You first segment the users, create the policies (inactive by default), activate them, then trigger their application, which can take some time.","items":["Define segments with New-OrganizationSegment","Create policies with New-InformationBarrierPolicy","Set the policies to Active","Start applying them with Start-InformationBarrierPoliciesApplication"]},
  "Supprimer une équipe Teams supprime aussi le groupe Microsoft 365 associé, qui reste restaurable pendant 30 jours. ¦ Vrai": {"q":"Deleting a Teams team also deletes the associated Microsoft 365 group, which remains restorable for 30 days.","e":"A team is built on a Microsoft 365 group: deleting it puts the group in soft-delete for 30 days, restorable from the admin center, Entra ID or PowerShell."},
  "Tu veux que tes utilisateurs puissent partager leur calendrier avec n'importe quel externe, mais uniquement en disponibilité (libre/occupé), sans objet ni lieu. Tu configures la stratégie de partage avec… ¦ -Domains \"*:CalendarSharingFreeBusyReviewer\"": {"q":"You want your users to be able to share their calendar with any external person, but only availability (free/busy), without subject or location. You configure the sharing policy with…","e":"With Set-SharingPolicy, “*” targets all external domains and FreeBusySimple limits sharing to availability. FreeBusyDetail adds subject and location, FreeBusyReviewer all details, and “Anonymous” concerns anonymous calendar publishing.","a":["-Domains \"*:CalendarSharingFreeBusyReviewer\"","-Domains \"Anonymous:CalendarSharingFreeBusySimple\"","-Domains \"*:CalendarSharingFreeBusySimple\"","-Domains \"*:CalendarSharingFreeBusyDetail\""]},
  "Tu veux interdire la participation anonyme à TOUTES les réunions Teams du tenant, quelle que soit la stratégie de l'organisateur. Tu exécutes… ¦ Set-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy -Identity Global -AllowAnonymousUsersToJoinMeeting $false": {"q":"You want to forbid anonymous participation in ALL Teams meetings in the tenant, regardless of the organizer's policy. You run…","e":"DisableAnonymousJoin, at the tenant meeting configuration level, applies to all meetings. Changing the Global policy doesn't affect users who have a different meeting policy assigned.","a":["Set-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy -Identity Global -AllowAnonymousUsersToJoinMeeting $false","Set-CsTeamsMeetingConfiguration -DisableAnonymousJoin $true","Set-CsExternalAccessPolicy -EnableFederationAccess $false","Set-CsTenantFederationConfiguration -AllowPublicUsers $false"]}
});
